7c83f87e302b667e737","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/e0c583772c0f1c0cbd41c7c83f87e302b667e737"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/30c36352779be4b0d8d726fc3e994cda85b11ee9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:47:35Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:47:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(sms): require authorized assignment and authenticated WebSockets (#209)\n\nAn authenticated SMS device could enumerate every waiting OTP request,\nincluding requests assigned to another device. Polling now returns only\nexplicitly assigned, waiting, unexpired work for that device. Unassigned\nand malformed legacy requests are withheld without mutation.\n\nThis follow-up also closes two adjacent claim/exposure paths:\n\n- `POST /api/sms/otp` refuses unassigned requests with HTTP 409 instead\nof letting the first authenticated device claim them.\n- `/api/sms/ws/sms-interceptor` authenticates `device_id` plus\n`X-Device-Key` before accepting or joining the connection manager.\n- Request completion is sent only to the assigned device, and newly\ncreated unassigned requests are not broadcast.\n- Naive UTC-to-epoch conversions were replaced with timezone-aware UTC.\n\nChart/app versions advance to 0.1.20/0.1.17 for an actual rollout. The\nmounted-route inventory now recognizes the WebSocket as a device-proof\nmigration gap rather than an unclassified platform-policy gap.\n\n### Validation\n\n- 439 backend tests pass on Python 3.12.\n- 52 focused SMS, security-regression, and mounted-inventory tests pass.\n- Black, isort, and `git diff --check` pass.\n- Uploaded head: `1024359298021361063021279e03cf9089da1ba9`.\n- Every uploaded Git blob was fetched again and matches the isolated\ncheckout:\n- `backend/app/routers/sms.py` —\n`8091e958ce8f1d9aee4a49f2daa0835b17e50ed1`\n- `backend/tests/test_security_regressions.py` —\n`a83132e0ef1aadd9185b89d7c3c202eb7b296575`\n- `backend/tests/test_sms_websocket_auth.py` —\n`e00947a778057937dbc4e8271de6acbde604c673`\n- `docs/security/mounted-route-authorization.json` —\n`8499668610c7832f03346d64e1389adbede5662c`\n- `docs/security/platform-auth-migration.md` —\n`864ff224168464bd80d003065b2cf23f4155583c`\n- `deploy/helm/fuzekeys/Chart.yaml` —\n`907bd9abb3a8ee92b177631d667c9ae47e35af2c`\n\nThis is containment, not completion of all FuzeKeys authorization gaps.\nPublic device enrollment, process-local plaintext device keys and\nrequests, a durable verified device principal, explicit authorized\nassignment lifecycle, owner/tenant bindings, platform resource policies,\nand exact instance grants remain unresolved. No required check,\napproval, credential, or deployment result is being bypassed or\nfabricated.\n\nAutomated work uses Israel''s explicitly authorized personal GitHub\nidentity exception. Ordinary repository checks and human review still\ngate merge.\n\n### Infrastructure callback/WebSocket containment\n\nThe infrastructure verification path now withholds unassigned jobs,\nrefuses first-device claims, rejects expired/completed/invalid callbacks\nbefore storing a code, and authenticates mobile-command WebSockets\nbefore acceptance. UTC-aware verification timestamps remove\nhost-timezone dependence. The command-send route still lacks an\nowner-authorized target-device contract and remains explicitly\nclassified as a platform-policy design gap.\n\nValidation on head `89733963c3fc70a99a8868846e4058dc01e7f18f`: 448\nbackend tests and 43 focused authorization/inventory tests pass; Black,\nisort and `git diff --check` pass. Chart/app versions advance to\n0.1.21/0.1.18.\n\nVerified uploaded blobs:\n\n- `backend/app/routers/infrastructure.py` —\n`3928ea6c4c4e18af7cc7adf817288e2d4fd0a942`\n- `backend/tests/test_infrastructure_device_auth.py` —\n`254c97afaf7b4b853a9ffbe9b37b9e1d1a753046`\n- `deploy/helm/fuzekeys/Chart.yaml` —\n`3f7bb23877cb96117ea7ba54e7d92eed353ca5ab`\n- `docs/security/mounted-route-authorization.json` —\n`2c7cafa79fefdbe039c2139e68abda244b8b79ba`\n- `docs/security/platform-auth-migration.md` —\n`35b686391514d6beef24e55c154af3d8f74083c7`\n- `scripts/mounted_authorization_inventory.py` —\n`15d955b7e315b6258c7427a07e9181a208617241`\n\n### Fresh head CI\n\nHead `89733963c3fc70a99a8868846e4058dc01e7f18f` passed CI/CD (run\n37548677742), Harden Gate (37548678039), Helm validation, Release Gate,\ndeployment validation, governance and drift checks. Fuze Code Review\npassed only under the documented provider-availability exception and\nproduced no approving review; A2A/MCP failed on the same unavailable\nlegacy provider chain. Repository approval and the human deploy-window\nmerge remain required.","tree":{"sha":"297e20189381011225d49a0dc4b361e8feeac26c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/297e20189381011225d49a0dc4b361e8feeac26c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/30c36352779be4b0d8d726fc3e994cda85b11ee9","verification":{"payload":"tree 297e20189381011225d49a0dc4b361e8feeac26c\nparent b063dd604affcb596096d85c355f70348ad8a7ad\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791370055 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791370055 +0300\n\nfix(sms): require authorized assignment and authenticated WebSockets (#209)\n\nAn authenticated SMS device could enumerate every waiting OTP request,\nincluding requests assigned to another device. Polling now returns only\nexplicitly assigned, waiting, unexpired work for that device. Unassigned\nand malformed legacy requests are withheld without mutation.\n\nThis follow-up also closes two adjacent claim/exposure paths:\n\n- `POST /api/sms/otp` refuses unassigned requests with HTTP 409 instead\nof letting the first authenticated device claim them.\n- `/api/sms/ws/sms-interceptor` authenticates `device_id` plus\n`X-Device-Key` before accepting or joining the connection manager.\n- Request completion is sent only to the assigned device, and newly\ncreated unassigned requests are not broadcast.\n- Naive UTC-to-epoch conversions were replaced with timezone-aware UTC.\n\nChart/app versions advance to 0.1.20/0.1.17 for an actual rollout. The\nmounted-route inventory now recognizes the WebSocket as a device-proof\nmigration gap rather than an unclassified platform-policy gap.\n\n### Validation\n\n- 439 backend tests pass on Python 3.12.\n- 52 focused SMS, security-regression, and mounted-inventory tests pass.\n- Black, isort, and `git diff --check` pass.\n- Uploaded head: `1024359298021361063021279e03cf9089da1ba9`.\n- Every uploaded Git blob was fetched again and matches the isolated\ncheckout:\n- `backend/app/routers/sms.py` —\n`8091e958ce8f1d9aee4a49f2daa0835b17e50ed1`\n- `backend/tests/test_security_regressions.py` —\n`a83132e0ef1aadd9185b89d7c3c202eb7b296575`\n- `backend/tests/test_sms_websocket_auth.py` —\n`e00947a778057937dbc4e8271de6acbde604c673`\n- `docs/security/mounted-route-authorization.json` —\n`8499668610c7832f03346d64e1389adbede5662c`\n- `docs/security/platform-auth-migration.md` —\n`864ff224168464bd80d003065b2cf23f4155583c`\n- `deploy/helm/fuzekeys/Chart.yaml` —\n`907bd9abb3a8ee92b177631d667c9ae47e35af2c`\n\nThis is containment, not completion of all FuzeKeys authorization gaps.\nPublic device enrollment, process-local plaintext device keys and\nrequests, a durable verified device principal, explicit authorized\nassignment lifecycle, owner/tenant bindings, platform resource policies,\nand exact instance grants remain unresolved. No required check,\napproval, credential, or deployment result is being bypassed or\nfabricated.\n\nAutomated work uses Israel''s explicitly authorized personal GitHub\nidentity exception. Ordinary repository checks and human review still\ngate merge.\n\n### Infrastructure callback/WebSocket containment\n\nThe infrastructure verification path now withholds unassigned jobs,\nrefuses first-device claims, rejects expired/completed/invalid callbacks\nbefore storing a code, and authenticates mobile-command WebSockets\nbefore acceptance. UTC-aware verification timestamps remove\nhost-timezone dependence. The command-send route still lacks an\nowner-authorized target-device contract and remains explicitly\nclassified as a platform-policy design gap.\n\nValidation on head `89733963c3fc70a99a8868846e4058dc01e7f18f`: 448\nbackend tests and 43 focused authorization/inventory tests pass; Black,\nisort and `git diff --check` pass. Chart/app versions advance to\n0.1.21/0.1.18.\n\nVerified uploaded blobs:\n\n- `backend/app/routers/infrastructure.py` —\n`3928ea6c4c4e18af7cc7adf817288e2d4fd0a942`\n- `backend/tests/test_infrastructure_device_auth.py` —\n`254c97afaf7b4b853a9ffbe9b37b9e1d1a753046`\n- `deploy/helm/fuzekeys/Chart.yaml` —\n`3f7bb23877cb96117ea7ba54e7d92eed353ca5ab`\n- `docs/security/mounted-route-authorization.json` —\n`2c7cafa79fefdbe039c2139e68abda244b8b79ba`\n- `docs/security/platform-auth-migration.md` —\n`35b686391514d6beef24e55c154af3d8f74083c7`\n- `scripts/mounted_authorization_inventory.py` —\n`15d955b7e315b6258c7427a07e9181a208617241`\n\n### Fresh head CI\n\nHead `89733963c3fc70a99a8868846e4058dc01e7f18f` passed CI/CD (run\n37548677742), Harden Gate (37548678039), Helm validation, Release Gate,\ndeployment validation, governance and drift checks. Fuze Code Review\npassed only under the documented provider-availability exception and\nproduced no approving review; A2A/MCP failed on the same unavailable\nlegacy provider chain. Repository approval and the human deploy-window\nmerge remain required.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxiNHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKNQQAEXbkHv4cmWvyiMufITxmS/4\n+sM3ZqiehXgeVjdsHyy1SrtUCtk2bQiVUygtVAL6Z/CUnqBidyo9Pa/sQA04x/Dj\nSeRUKRVSZyyK/Yo7CdeSRAPnZ94k3yb2oyFPzq3imWb53aUeJ1nlAvdX+PgorY+T\ng1s5qYqMB5gWqT9Unln3AAokwqFfdfT8SGe0MSi4Y4Lq2PcAcUxG9YscCwD7k73n\nrQQruBVUlMS8uVvj1pcs5+kCJptxvJEvMLiz8q2V5sRCPvNG1FIQMbVqqfp4DTZx\nOo3sN01GCP+MwB3bMdT0sd9QMUDM036R4x3wdEU26wt1hpmIF+3G30/6yoC0/9z9\n4JrmaSWKlUk3s4BY7WxLNWEFfvEUN5oPVmQtOfsOlup4YSvoIVR8uJb/iAvgKqvD\nNSMctLUslM5Qbuzc6tidUQ98pIAgeB9mNTGBmFDwJ9w8UM5wNNKYshZ6E0BrPhOJ\nHK0kw0hl4dzYshZrCF6KNFw/YXiU3u72BnO8sK3TwsgqpSfWqOTJpckUw5wyWdAT\nDjRclhUBEr8HFtLaYyWsQy/C1DhK6VqxnqSjPdXAxnYs+G5S9bw3RSu6HpcYJF6u\nA1r/kyKVghbc29tDmI3jzeXAr1eylCdWkUgOtSwGPCilryDUIF4lkjLjxc/iBDnR\n9+eAA2we7JuPakrkaLZz\n=p3U7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T10:47:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/30c36352779be4b0d8d726fc3e994cda85b11ee9","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDMwYzM2MzUyNzc5YmU0YjBkOGQ3MjZmYzNlOTk0Y2RhODViMTFlZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/b063dd604affcb596096d85c355f70348ad8a7ad","sha":"b063dd604affcb596096d85c355f70348ad8a7ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b063dd604affcb596096d85c355f70348ad8a7ad"}],"sha":"30c36352779be4b0d8d726fc3e994cda85b11ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/30c36352779be4b0d8d726fc3e994cda85b11ee9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b063dd604affcb596096d85c355f70348ad8a7ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:16:18Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:16:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Release provider vault and remediate frontend dependencies and API contracts (#205)\n\nGeneralizes vault credentials by provider and owner while keeping\nmetadata/configuration isolated. Eight Google connectors share canonical\nGmail custody bound to verified Google subject and OAuth client.\nCross-replica locks serialize updates, refresh tokens require proven\ncontinuity, and the secret is deleted only after its last reference.\nLegacy account combinations require explicit reauthorization. See\ndocs/security/google-credential-custody.md.\n\nAdds immutable local-to-platform account linking with simultaneous local\nand FuzeFront session proof. FuzeFront''s trusted session endpoint must\nverify active SQL tenant membership; missing proof, conflicts and\noutages deny linking. An additive migration stores only subject/tenant\nidentifiers, never session tokens. The optional Helm tenant setting\nremains empty until a real tenant is provisioned. Existing login and\nconnector behavior remain compatible. See\ndocs/security/platform-auth-migration.md.\n\nReplaces vulnerable CRA tooling with Vite/Vitest, updates Python\ndependencies, adds bounded pagination and strict create models, updates\nfrontend/OpenAPI consumers, and recognizes delegated service\nauthentication. The sealing workflow provisions the namespace-scoped\nAnthropic A2A secret from a configured repository credential. Health\nadvertises google-shared-v1 for FuzeFront''s release prerequisite.\n\nValidation: 268 backend tests passed locally, including the account-link\nregressions. New modules pass MyPy, Black and isort; OpenAPI projection\nretains 77 operations, and identifier/pagination gates pass. Earlier\nfrontend builds/tests and dependency audits passed. Fresh CI must verify\nthe final head; no gates were disabled.\n\nThe JWT advisory is remediated by PyJWT[crypto] 2.15.1; 61 focused\nauth/broker tests pass and its dependency closure audit is clean.\nsource-map-js is resolved to patched 1.2.2; clean frontend install,\nTypeScript, standalone and MFE builds pass with zero npm\nvulnerabilities. Exact blobs are verified.\n\nThe encrypted a2a-provider-anthropic manifest is now included using the\nexact generated #207 blob, with no plaintext or rotation. Its\nsource-presence prerequisite passes; cluster decryption and provider\nfunding remain unverified. Gitleaks 8.24.3 identified the finding as a\ndeterministic JWT regression fixture, not ciphertext. The fixture now\nderives its key at runtime; only the exact historical introducing\ncommit/path/rule/line fingerprint is excluded. The gate still detects a\nsynthetic AWS-shaped credential in the same filename, and 61\nauthentication/broker tests pass.\n\nProduction still requires resource-scoped policy schema, owner-grant\nbackfill and route enforcement, a provisioned tenant and valid funded\nmaintainer credentials. A read-only live cluster query on 2026-10-06\nshows backend image 0.1.13 and no FUZEKEYS_AUTHZ_TENANT value; this PR\nis not deployed. Account linking is implemented in code and requires the\nnew FuzeFront tenant-proof endpoint plus database migration to become\navailable. FuzeFront #1203 also requires the deployed google-shared-v1\nprotocol. Neither full authorization migration nor live Google\nconnectivity is claimed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"08776d692396ec3ec9182ae874a7781461adc2bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/08776d692396ec3ec9182ae874a7781461adc2bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/b063dd604affcb596096d85c355f70348ad8a7ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 08776d692396ec3ec9182ae874a7781461adc2bf\nparent 716b4f50a2c5619c754802caa2e67b14b5239837\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1791314178 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791314178 +0300\n\nRelease provider vault and remediate frontend dependencies and API contracts (#205)\n\nGeneralizes vault credentials by provider and owner while keeping\nmetadata/configuration isolated. Eight Google connectors share canonical\nGmail custody bound to verified Google subject and OAuth client.\nCross-replica locks serialize updates, refresh tokens require proven\ncontinuity, and the secret is deleted only after its last reference.\nLegacy account combinations require explicit reauthorization. See\ndocs/security/google-credential-custody.md.\n\nAdds immutable local-to-platform account linking with simultaneous local\nand FuzeFront session proof. FuzeFront''s trusted session endpoint must\nverify active SQL tenant membership; missing proof, conflicts and\noutages deny linking. An additive migration stores only subject/tenant\nidentifiers, never session tokens. The optional Helm tenant setting\nremains empty until a real tenant is provisioned. Existing login and\nconnector behavior remain compatible. See\ndocs/security/platform-auth-migration.md.\n\nReplaces vulnerable CRA tooling with Vite/Vitest, updates Python\ndependencies, adds bounded pagination and strict create models, updates\nfrontend/OpenAPI consumers, and recognizes delegated service\nauthentication. The sealing workflow provisions the namespace-scoped\nAnthropic A2A secret from a configured repository credential. Health\nadvertises google-shared-v1 for FuzeFront''s release prerequisite.\n\nValidation: 268 backend tests passed locally, including the account-link\nregressions. New modules pass MyPy, Black and isort; OpenAPI projection\nretains 77 operations, and identifier/pagination gates pass. Earlier\nfrontend builds/tests and dependency audits passed. Fresh CI must verify\nthe final head; no gates were disabled.\n\nThe JWT advisory is remediated by PyJWT[crypto] 2.15.1; 61 focused\nauth/broker tests pass and its dependency closure audit is clean.\nsource-map-js is resolved to patched 1.2.2; clean frontend install,\nTypeScript, standalone and MFE builds pass with zero npm\nvulnerabilities. Exact blobs are verified.\n\nThe encrypted a2a-provider-anthropic manifest is now included using the\nexact generated #207 blob, with no plaintext or rotation. Its\nsource-presence prerequisite passes; cluster decryption and provider\nfunding remain unverified. Gitleaks 8.24.3 identified the finding as a\ndeterministic JWT regression fixture, not ciphertext. The fixture now\nderives its key at runtime; only the exact historical introducing\ncommit/path/rule/line fingerprint is excluded. The gate still detects a\nsynthetic AWS-shaped credential in the same filename, and 61\nauthentication/broker tests pass.\n\nProduction still requires resource-scoped policy schema, owner-grant\nbackfill and route enforcement, a provisioned tenant and valid funded\nmaintainer credentials. A read-only live cluster query on 2026-10-06\nshows backend image 0.1.13 and no FUZEKEYS_AUTHZ_TENANT value; this PR\nis not deployed. Account linking is implemented in code and requires the\nnew FuzeFront tenant-proof endpoint plus database migration to become\navailable. FuzeFront #1203 also requires the deployed google-shared-v1\nprotocol. Neither full authorization migration nor live Google\nconnectivity is claimed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUkCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIXwQAB3kJEH3DJKbJl85B4xWreVd\n77ABZb7gZA0aOOX5W5JRzFIR1J1jpRVZ65GB5LobctzYDfiOs98mnVogzRYRWq5c\n9342zt715BoYyrMWfqqdMu2SgppPvI/XAszLvDyWi5YoyA9Bry/8kX/pGN4kKrO/\nZtGx6xSNfDdYgb9CnWNRsOw3sp8h9AwG+4wPuU5/W8o7ucrK5LTl