ptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/0c7359776736f3120f90bc2665025c4b13bb5938/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T13:45:33Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T13:45:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(governance): re-stamp governance-sync.yml so the commit-back stops failing silently\n\nRe-stamps governance-sync.yml from the FuzeSDLC canonical so the commit-back stops failing silently (duplicate Authorization header -> HTTP 400, masked by `git push | tee`). The file could not receive this fix through its own broken push, so it was re-stamped once, out of band, by the canonical installer.\n\nThe re-stamped workflow''s own commit-back already worked on this PR: 1 bot reconcile commit(s) landed on the branch, which the old copy could never push.\n\nAll required checks green on this head.\n\nRefs izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#386","tree":{"sha":"75a52fc4953331b45e929c5b9624556c150ed3f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/75a52fc4953331b45e929c5b9624556c150ed3f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/0c7359776736f3120f90bc2665025c4b13bb5938","verification":{"payload":"tree 75a52fc4953331b45e929c5b9624556c150ed3f9\nparent 08c7f8cc77a70ea163398bb4a2fd02635c23681a\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1790084733 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790084733 +0300\n\nfix(governance): re-stamp governance-sync.yml so the commit-back stops failing silently\n\nRe-stamps governance-sync.yml from the FuzeSDLC canonical so the commit-back stops failing silently (duplicate Authorization header -> HTTP 400, masked by `git push | tee`). The file could not receive this fix through its own broken push, so it was re-stamped once, out of band, by the canonical installer.\n\nThe re-stamped workflow''s own commit-back already worked on this PR: 1 bot reconcile commit(s) landed on the branch, which the old copy could never push.\n\nAll required checks green on this head.\n\nRefs izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#386","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsoZ9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMMQQADQmb7WAevMQzKt2oRVqGR7Z\nM/mgrkhIapxVlrjpQkgm1+xDBh2RwFwB79/IjmXaD+VESlPe58h7fU5OQGMlrMHG\n1HyiQkpUvYxIL/vzpy2mpstdVjSKPrm+0Fn3jM8kwgPBlhW8kUK3ZrDTEvygPlfw\nU9ACfcc1B3cgX0iAPRcvP1mPAuulXBwNLhnARnDbgajkKGXI5/tt9lcSgMFdlqbZ\nAXvfldgX70d0e6td8+Z3dxd5lcuElV1au0CoASa28joQ+6mhl4D4Buv0q4lQYpdZ\ngjxxFDc4m3tu6k0F1/d4f816i5FSKzOzdrGkGnMoUEFwwEHnKH3zHDBRTTkj2olg\nOOntMDqzXlielD1UmvpI8pr6213+JtNe34/imWiOlksYQ8nZfBD7V2zMPuOLu5IQ\n8uO5TFfqhsQOPpvArXzbCnCfbuCIR3cikaob7dqoKwX4gLCJBjDQWRygYKWcxQ6s\nVNyNyy3CiK35VCW3VuzRo9JvmI3rEAlIuqsSYP0yFgJVl408YAe48cund3zZVPLT\nAYca/l8iS8nDWwRFpVnqaLtHBIX2VM1q8bQg1oOGMbxtd1i+omI035RUd63n22e0\ne1MteBru/jymnRSPWnwXAYGfgtOqjvNg+Hf6MUG5xwgEG5dU4ybORnxMomH8kpAd\nrzb0qAYxIgAZrLJCffCi\n=PuU0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T13:45:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/0c7359776736f3120f90bc2665025c4b13bb5938","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDBjNzM1OTc3NjczNmYzMTIwZjkwYmMyNjY1MDI1YzRiMTNiYjU5Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/08c7f8cc77a70ea163398bb4a2fd02635c23681a","sha":"08c7f8cc77a70ea163398bb4a2fd02635c23681a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/08c7f8cc77a70ea163398bb4a2fd02635c23681a"}],"sha":"0c7359776736f3120f90bc2665025c4b13bb5938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/0c7359776736f3120f90bc2665025c4b13bb5938"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/08c7f8cc77a70ea163398bb4a2fd02635c23681a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T22:58:01Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T22:58:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): install the canonical @fuze entrypoint (#190)\n\nInstalls the canonical `@fuze` entrypoint from FuzeSDLC. Part of a\nfleet-wide rollout — **depends on izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#282**, merge that\nfirst.\n\n## Why this repo needs it\n\n`@fuze` was answered in **exactly one repo** (FuzeInfra). This repo''s\nissue templates already say `@fuze — please triage.` and the baseline\ndocuments `@fuze` as the delegation handle, so the mention landed\nnowhere — and a mention nothing answers is indistinguishable from an\nagent that simply has not replied yet.\n\n## What lands\n\n**`.github/workflows/fuze.yml`** — the canonical handler.\nMention-triggered on issues, issue comments, PR reviews and review\ncomments; gated to OWNER/MEMBER/COLLABORATOR; loop-guarded; deduped per\nissue.\n\n**No cluster credential of any kind.** FuzeInfra''s original is\ndeliberately cluster-capable (prod kubeconfig, kubectl/helm/terraform,\nin-cluster runner). Copying that verbatim to 22 repos would have handed\nprod cluster credentials to every product repo. It is split instead: the\nprivileged variant is a separate template installed only where\n`.fuze/manifest.json` declares `clusterOps.enabled: true`, which only\nFuzeInfra does. Verified on this repo before this commit was made —\n`grep -cE ''KUBE_CONFIG|terraform|runs-on: staging''` over the rendered\nentrypoint returns **0**, and no `fuze-cluster.yml` exists here.\n\n**LLM routing, not a hardcoded endpoint.** The original pins\n`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` to an in-cluster service DNS name that does not\nresolve from a GitHub-hosted runner — a verbatim copy would have failed\nDNS here. This routes through `./.github/actions/fuze-code-action` →\n`./.github/actions/llm-endpoint`, which probes the gateway and falls\nback to a direct vendor key.\n\n`allowed-bots` is set to a named list\n(`fuzeone-bot,github-actions,fuze-agent`, never `*`). Automated\nworkflows legitimately comment `@fuze` to hand work over, and without\nthis claude-code-action aborts ~1s in with \"Workflow initiated by\nnon-human actor\" — a failure that reads in a skimmed log exactly like a\nprovider outage.\n\n## `claude-auto-pr.yml` → `fuze-auto-pr.yml`\n\n**Naming only.** That workflow makes no LLM call — it is `gh pr create`\nand nothing else. Nothing was routed through LiteLLM and nothing was\nadded.\n\nThe old file is **removed**, not left beside the new one: both trigger\non a push to `claude/**` and both call `gh pr create` for the same\nbranch, so keeping it is a duplicate-PR bug rather than a rename. The\nnew trigger covers **both** `claude/**` (unchanged — claude-code-action\nstill names its branches that way) **and** `fuze/**`; no prefix was\ndropped.\n\nThis repo''s copy was a stale install-time snapshot, not a deliberate\nfork (only FuzeInfra''s carries a `fuze:fork` stamp), so the replacement\nis also a strict upgrade — it brings the agent-PR identity chain\n(fuze-agent App token → bot PAT → `GITHUB_TOKEN`) that the old copy\npredates.\n\n**Required-check safety, verified across all 22 governed repos:** no\nruleset anywhere names a context emitted by this workflow. The complete\ndistinct required-check set is 15 strings, none of them `open-draft-pr`\nor `Auto-PR from claude branches`; no classic branch protection exists\nanywhere, so that set is complete. Structurally consistent too — the\nworkflow triggers only on `push`, so it can never report on a\n`pull_request` to the default branch.\n\n## Verification done on this repo before committing\n\n- `grep` for the three privileged identifiers in the rendered entrypoint\n→ 0 hits.\n- `fuze-cluster.yml` absent.\n- `actionlint` exit 0 on both files.\n- `runs-on:` rendered from this repo''s declared `ci.runner`, not the\ntemplate''s default — a `runs-on` naming a pool that does not exist does\nnot fail, it queues forever.\n- Rendered by the canonical installer engine (`engine.reconcile` →\n`lib.render`), so both files carry a `fuze:managed` marker and\n`.fuze/installed.json` records them. Identical bytes to what\n`sdlc-bootstrap` would write.\n\n**Not proven, and not provable right now:** that a live `@fuze` mention\ncompletes. The fleet''s `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is currently invalid (not\nmerely exhausted), and mention mode deliberately does not attempt the\nOpenAI/Gemini rungs — so every `@fuze` / `@claude` mention hard-fails\ntoday regardless of routing. This PR fixes *where the mention lands*,\nnot whether the credential works.\n\n## Why a PR and not a sync\n\n`governance-sync` cannot push `.github/workflows/**` today and reports\nsuccess when the push fails — 16 of 22 repos lack the code path\nentirely, and in the other 6 the commit-back is rejected `400 Duplicate\nheader: \"Authorization\"` while a missing `set -o pipefail` turns the\nfailure green. See izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#283.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e65539bafde03a649afbb4ef9da72b81d1b327c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/7e65539bafde03a649afbb4ef9da72b81d1b327c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/08c7f8cc77a70ea163398bb4a2fd02635c23681a","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e65539bafde03a649afbb4ef9da72b81d1b327c\nparent 304ed2323d668857f08b1a238be3ee9be7961f7f\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1789513081 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789513081 +0300\n\nfeat(ci): install the canonical @fuze entrypoint (#190)\n\nInstalls the canonical `@fuze` entrypoint from FuzeSDLC. Part of a\nfleet-wide rollout — **depends on izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#282**, merge that\nfirst.\n\n## Why this repo needs it\n\n`@fuze` was answered in **exactly one repo** (FuzeInfra). This repo''s\nissue templates already say `@fuze — please triage.` and the baseline\ndocuments `@fuze` as the delegation handle, so the mention landed\nnowhere — and a mention nothing answers is indistinguishable from an\nagent that simply has not replied yet.\n\n## What lands\n\n**`.github/workflows/fuze.yml`** — the canonical handler.\nMention-triggered on issues, issue comments, PR reviews and review\ncomments; gated to OWNER/MEMBER/COLLABORATOR; loop-guarded; deduped per\nissue.\n\n**No cluster credential of any kind.** FuzeInfra''s original is\ndeliberately cluster-capable (prod kubeconfig, kubectl/helm/terraform,\nin-cluster runner). Copying that verbatim to 22 repos would have handed\nprod cluster credentials to every product repo. It is split instead: the\nprivileged variant is a separate template installed only where\n`.fuze/manifest.json` declares `clusterOps.enabled: true`, which only\nFuzeInfra does. Verified on this repo before this commit was made —\n`grep -cE ''KUBE_CONFIG|terraform|runs-on: staging''` over the rendered\nentrypoint returns **0**, and no `fuze-cluster.yml` exists here.\n\n**LLM routing, not a hardcoded endpoint.** The original pins\n`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` to an in-cluster service DNS name that does not\nresolve from a GitHub-hosted runner — a verbatim copy would have failed\nDNS here. This routes through `./.github/actions/fuze-code-action` →\n`./.github/actions/llm-endpoint`, which probes the gateway and falls\nback to a direct vendor key.\n\n`allowed-bots` is set to a named list\n(`fuzeone-bot,github-actions,fuze-agent`, never `*`). Automated\nworkflows legitimately comment `@fuze` to hand work over, and without\nthis claude-code-action aborts ~1s in with \"Workflow initiated by\nnon-human actor\" — a failure that reads in a skimmed log exactly like a\nprovider outage.\n\n## `claude-auto-pr.yml` → `fuze-auto-pr.yml`\n\n**Naming only.** That workflow makes no LLM call — it is `gh pr create`\nand nothing else. Nothing was routed through LiteLLM and nothing was\nadded.\n\nThe old file is **removed**, not left beside the new one: both trigger\non a push to `claude/**` and both call `gh pr create` for the same\nbranch, so keeping it is a duplicate-PR bug rather than a rename. The\nnew trigger covers **both** `claude/**` (unchanged — claude-code-action\nstill names its branches that way) **and** `fuze/**`; no prefix was\ndropped.\n\nThis repo''s copy was a stale install-time snapshot, not a deliberate\nfork (only FuzeInfra''s carries a `fuze:fork` stamp), so the replacement\nis also a strict upgrade — it brings the agent-PR identity chain\n(fuze-agent App token → bot PAT → `GITHUB_TOKEN`) that the old copy\npredates.\n\n**Required-check safety, verified across all 22 governed repos:** no\nruleset anywhere names a context emitted by this workflow. The complete\ndistinct required-check set is 15 strings, none of them `open-draft-pr`\nor `Auto-PR from claude branches`; no classic branch protection exists\nanywhere, so that set is complete. Structurally consistent too — the\nworkflow triggers only on `push`, so it can never report on a\n`pull_request` to the default branch.\n\n## Verification done on this repo before committing\n\n- `grep` for the three privileged identifiers in the rendered entrypoint\n→ 0 hits.\n- `fuze-cluster.yml` absent.\n- `actionlint` exit 0 on both files.\n- `runs-on:` rendered from this repo''s declared `ci.runner`, not the\ntemplate''s default — a `runs-on` naming a pool that does not exist does\nnot fail, it queues forever.\n- Rendered by the canonical installer engine (`engine.reconcile` →\n`lib.render`), so both files carry a `fuze:managed` marker and\n`.fuze/installed.json` records them. Identical bytes to what\n`sdlc-bootstrap` would write.\n\n**Not proven, and not provable right now:** that a live `@fuze` mention\ncompletes. The fleet''s `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is currently invalid (not\nmerely exhausted), and mention mode deliberately does not attempt the\nOpenAI/Gemini rungs — so every `@fuze` / `@claude` mention hard-fails\ntoday regardless of routing. This PR fixes *where the mention lands*,\nnot whether the credential works.\n\n## Why a PR and not a sync\n\n`governance-sync` cannot push `.github/workflows/**` today and reports\nsuccess when the push fails — 16 of 22 repos lack the code path\nentirely, and in the other 6 the commit-back is rejected `400 Duplicate\nheader: \"Authorization\"` while a missing `set -o pipefail` turns the\nfailure green. See izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#283.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqc15CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn6IQAECjhLvsOkl7K0wH+eCSJMG/\nEh06Hr5gHQInAppcMO3abjSclOyhNgFxR+h+OW0LMS6g44T6kwOGmnV2BQ/aoTLK\nD2CBGa3e98WZN0Wp5eJnhFMPEhnyecD1meCDjNwLHkU19c02QVKMV3Z+y5Vaob/h\nnS0K1fhtenBODsMuA77YYWZXvTfhPZZa89MojO0lv0UB02JAIlOqxjAP84kbNQGj\nUeXyq6HJwSFDJ5UvHBvIAP/vZo2XO344+v5L2twdBC3piPmxd2381PMMol7xrF9G\ncMsfezDqe32yscy2NPPFaC1XTXznhCuDcAN3TU2ExU1Kz3Y8XAif0Wd7+/MptIDE\n6ABIxgJiRqmGCUW+gWUppEcDzJHY4WuWvmJdJLVMwgkdszXwa9HKpNbdOqQF/LKH\njqJ8E1WbgPbgni7whpkWJrRBYTpyOQpoOndiNzLREmHx3mxpb0yhYYEJh4pCOsJy\nAMP3iPJ5Fd7D8/rXItyceWb2kIDgAeEsseD1ANg1C6XMjq7vzjKYzNeZXncq0lf9\nnW6eGBkFSGlRNkC+sbp8o3jbPl0unpuPcdp6RhSCJbkaVDns2PSOl+t4w+4evl12\nN1GyQnH6OfCajVxCuPZWYVLWsIRU9t4QZxxqpNR4++oXbBMcidU0R0bdBNOBwaKF\njXdVXwIUvRd1HC23SLH0\n=u4Dk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T22:58:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"h