/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/86228abb96e0384117b9916768111169e7305ec2","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDg2MjI4YWJiOTZlMDM4NDExN2I5OTE2NzY4MTExMTY5ZTczMDVlYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/7cba57ecd58500e88da28a55243920478f32d0a1","sha":"7cba57ecd58500e88da28a55243920478f32d0a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/7cba57ecd58500e88da28a55243920478f32d0a1"}],"sha":"86228abb96e0384117b9916768111169e7305ec2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/86228abb96e0384117b9916768111169e7305ec2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/7cba57ecd58500e88da28a55243920478f32d0a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T19:19:09Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T19:19:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(governance): re-pin baselineRef to the v1 moving alias (#188)\n\nRe-pins `.fuze/manifest.json` `baselineRef`: `main` -> `v1`. One-line\ndiff.\n\n## Why\n\nIt pinned **`main`** — the working edge. `governance/versioning.md` §5:\n*\"`main` … **Not** for consuming repos — unreviewed policy would\npropagate instantly.\"*\n\nNote this is a **convention, not a hard schema constraint**:\n`governance/repo-manifest.schema.json` states the rule in\n`baselineRef`''s `description` but declares no `enum` or `pattern`, so\nnothing was failing validation. The drift was silent because nothing\nchecks it.\n\n## Effect\n\n`v1` is the moving major alias, re-pointed on every compatible policy\nrelease, so this restores **automatic** propagation: the repo reconciles\nto the current standard on its next PR via `governance-sync`, with no\nper-repo fan-out.\n\n## Sequencing\n\nFuzeSDLC PR #278 (baseline **v1.11.0**) must merge first. `v1` currently\ndereferences to `2ffafc5` (= `v1.10.0`), which still carries the\n**broken** `llm-endpoint/action.yml` blob `78041e15`; the fix\n(`ab3f22e8`, #277) and #274 are on `main` only. #278 advances `v1` past\nboth.\n\n(Note: this repo''s default branch is `master`, not `main`.)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7bc8c90db2e9a74ab7ecccb034a3575dcedd4c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/7bc8c90db2e9a74ab7ecccb034a3575dcedd4c2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/7cba57ecd58500e88da28a55243920478f32d0a1","verification":{"payload":"tree 7bc8c90db2e9a74ab7ecccb034a3575dcedd4c2c\nparent 294c0a008580cc36a30f0aba65c87fe862ac1ceb\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1788376749 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788376749 +0300\n\nchore(governance): re-pin baselineRef to the v1 moving alias (#188)\n\nRe-pins `.fuze/manifest.json` `baselineRef`: `main` -> `v1`. One-line\ndiff.\n\n## Why\n\nIt pinned **`main`** — the working edge. `governance/versioning.md` §5:\n*\"`main` … **Not** for consuming repos — unreviewed policy would\npropagate instantly.\"*\n\nNote this is a **convention, not a hard schema constraint**:\n`governance/repo-manifest.schema.json` states the rule in\n`baselineRef`''s `description` but declares no `enum` or `pattern`, so\nnothing was failing validation. The drift was silent because nothing\nchecks it.\n\n## Effect\n\n`v1` is the moving major alias, re-pointed on every compatible policy\nrelease, so this restores **automatic** propagation: the repo reconciles\nto the current standard on its next PR via `governance-sync`, with no\nper-repo fan-out.\n\n## Sequencing\n\nFuzeSDLC PR #278 (baseline **v1.11.0**) must merge first. `v1` currently\ndereferences to `2ffafc5` (= `v1.10.0`), which still carries the\n**broken** `llm-endpoint/action.yml` blob `78041e15`; the fix\n(`ab3f22e8`, #277) and #274 are on `main` only. #278 advances `v1` past\nboth.\n\n(Note: this repo''s default branch is `master`, not `main`.)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmHatCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfFcQAJp0cyudzqupccLI6VYDknZi\nQsLx3no+j7sJOcU/xIwxOXHePQofukmAWzMzeqyKuQV1DPFlK4gpl+XdON565WJz\nzy5VPzgVCmCi1kBvZJD7J0z+zhaBXkNpbg7CrVx8uQGCZA5reqHtVWsII3JtnjsH\nDgJ0pp26xGU/nCEiJpddTjpUC9AEk3+H6J7ooEkBhXmwJ3Vpl/zLNk3H79AgG+Zw\ncbxLHaDyXe1RhajfMOKKDU7SLNaXK5PaRvfs61x6PzXTRcYGEPxOgb/mdKjDe/nA\nCu4rXoU47SvnThSupYc0D4TkVNRIFfV8zO9WyBbVt8fwdcMeNe4acRMYKgokKVc+\nAdO6rhgVHjq/ByyaO0ivMTCQPZxUrh/O+tuc3WIGwymnJ5dk1HcFaoQxsxoY6Tgg\nykXxoMBlCyMjG3hGTAl9Zp3zU8gZi7sNUMhcobU973L9nNPn23BAtRrwiXTg4zvB\nX1sW+r88ChwagP9i5VNL5+IvIbMNVG7RolmWcSzZMWiatBgsZ8LBuElEV5Hul5Pt\nRYOwmhT1JBeV+dd