ptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/5725727802b7ddc659b8ef7ee6f34612342e35c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:13:27Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:13:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(argocd): GitOps-manage the fuzekeys AppProject so app-of-apps self-heals (#40)\n\nMove project.yaml into applications/ so the app-of-apps reconciles the fuzekeys AppProject from git (sync-wave -1, Prune=false); point the root app-of-apps at the built-in default project to break the chicken-and-egg that left fuzekeys-apps Missing/OutOfSync (#34). Child Applications keep project: fuzekeys, preserving workload isolation.\n\nResidual risk (documented in review): assumes the built-in default AppProject is not locked down; could not verify the live cluster (GitOps/pull-based, no cluster credentials). Failure mode is safe and one-commit revertible, and the pre-PR state is already broken (#34), so this cannot regress a working system.\n\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0fc54ca021db5d6af5c6b52570a0588abd371d87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/0fc54ca021db5d6af5c6b52570a0588abd371d87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/5725727802b7ddc659b8ef7ee6f34612342e35c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 0fc54ca021db5d6af5c6b52570a0588abd371d87\nparent 6c4bacdee98ea5bdf119261762100d04d21a3aa2\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787771607 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787771607 +0300\n\nfix(argocd): GitOps-manage the fuzekeys AppProject so app-of-apps self-heals (#40)\n\nMove project.yaml into applications/ so the app-of-apps reconciles the fuzekeys AppProject from git (sync-wave -1, Prune=false); point the root app-of-apps at the built-in default project to break the chicken-and-egg that left fuzekeys-apps Missing/OutOfSync (#34). Child Applications keep project: fuzekeys, preserving workload isolation.\n\nResidual risk (documented in review): assumes the built-in default AppProject is not locked down; could not verify the live cluster (GitOps/pull-based, no cluster credentials). Failure mode is safe and one-commit revertible, and the pre-PR state is already broken (#34), so this cannot regress a working system.\n\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjzrXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+A4QAF7IdIlEnP4eRAq8DceBq6Ed\nPgZixrmEmim8fno4+93woTsWq76zUEQ1QD/Ta7YMnXzvd9+2BmmtG+kYRKadjg8A\n1dzo4B0JSZlwVtjq7BHDX1Pj2ZZHA9eqPxltTy/288Dh42e3Oj3dPrI2EGh9j9Kh\negNoNvsoPzldNsh+KG6dcjkC9W6MKK8uxdJrtpy643Fuli0a4GjL+CnxJQ7gnqBV\nJPdv58Tra7DWRoS/AQmc9XHJZ1HcMaB9qjfKiMOKul2vEj0n8vP8TvzAW8tjXjXh\n/LOdL9vpDAsG+EQbzVgp7ZCEu7BY6YFEQbGPfNjmUt01qWfP8/4xEhEUw/7R/IQb\nhfdSBHtbcy5+BbruNiSomfUGs+NJmt0DXAzRZrF9TpGK3QoWrscTVZLFrSYXBlDE\nEEcDsRs0OWsNzxEiY2vIz1xkHDTis6suxcF7yUVkCC1fsVHyHYcW/Ncjb5x0hda4\n4aHdwcJvj5Wf3e0NeVrk0AEgi8R19d3xuxv8IxYm6oQJX05ogjkZWmUj0ymYjazT\n7c5oUBVkLSE3Es0Y2Ed016Q9qfOdPHkx7URvgnFFbqB1wLjbHQZ49H4QqvCR9c77\nLMXOTn5pEZ4/9JRVMiPuEOGboNyRNRZslcGfxeu8k4LQtBZf0qGfB7F3LE9MTlks\nqdNZjuvZ5KgGMe2LK8m5\n=+Esy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T19:13:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://gith