s/affd7af29b3548cb157cf7646b582408b408d02e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/3f868209de99b286df1d290b17035541568850f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:07:17Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:07:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: pin actions/checkout to a SHA in the repo-local workflows (#102)\n\n#72 pinned setup-python, cache and codecov-action but left checkout on the\nfloating @v4 tag, because actionlint does not flag v4 and that PR was scoped to\nwhat actionlint reported. #46 would have covered it, but it proposed the equally\nfloating @v7 across ten HUB-OWNED workflows, so it was closed and the hub half\nwent to FuzeSDLC#117 instead — which normalised all 25 canonical templates to\nv7.0.1 pinned.\n\nThese four files are the repo-local remainder that no hub PR reaches:\n\n  ci.yml               x3\n  build-and-push.yml   x4\n  deploy-platform.yml  x2\n  seal-secrets.yml     x1\n\nall now actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1  # v7.0.1,\nthe same SHA the canonical templates use.\n\nThe other ten workflows still on @v4 are hub-owned — their canonical lives in\nFuzeSDLC/workflow-templates — and are deliberately untouched here; editing them\nlocally would fork them from canonical and be reconciled away.\n\nRationale unchanged from #72 and FuzeSDLC#98: a mutable tag can be repointed by\nits owner, as the trivy-action and kics-github-action compromises showed.\n\nVerified: actionlint 1.7.12 reports 0 errors across .github/workflows.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24b598b90581fa6a8d5e7630cf8d2a2e5f1c6279","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/24b598b90581fa6a8d5e7630cf8d2a2e5f1c6279"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/3f868209de99b286df1d290b17035541568850f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 24b598b90581fa6a8d5e7630cf8d2a2e5f1c6279\nparent c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787317637 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787317637 +0300\n\nci: pin actions/checkout to a SHA in the repo-local workflows (#102)\n\n#72 pinned setup-python, cache and codecov-action but left checkout on the\nfloating @v4 tag, because actionlint does not flag v4 and that PR was scoped to\nwhat actionlint reported. #46 would have covered it, but it proposed the equally\nfloating @v7 across ten HUB-OWNED workflows, so it was closed and the hub half\nwent to FuzeSDLC#117 instead — which normalised all 25 canonical templates to\nv7.0.1 pinned.\n\nThese four files are the repo-local remainder that no hub PR reaches:\n\n  ci.yml               x3\n  build-and-push.yml   x4\n  deploy-platform.yml  x2\n  seal-secrets.yml     x1\n\nall now actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1  # v7.0.1,\nthe same SHA the canonical templates use.\n\nThe other ten workflows still on @v4 are hub-owned — their canonical lives in\nFuzeSDLC/workflow-templates — and are deliberately untouched here; editing them\nlocally would fork them from canonical and be reconciled away.\n\nRationale unchanged from #72 and FuzeSDLC#98: a mutable tag can be repointed by\nits owner, as the trivy-action and kics-github-action compromises showed.\n\nVerified: actionlint 1.7.12 reports 0 errors across .github/workflows.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiE2FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsrcQAF7LTgS3f1exCbbD5ZwqIpgq\nuP5OUCU9wPcNCXI2WxaMyeqBtizhB2bZa/1cRk5o/sfV+suAKZyL9Yc0fCoAj14w\nU+tYhdOWrU7+9UitBnZlR3pL7dQlpS9QEg5u8zb11hmL9/Abv+HAogJ+PZI5kPO5\nE2QBB49VoVuST4iuB198kf+fNMrrzcEFYhw4a778hKm/Da5qYjvZp+jCxXoyt3PX\nt0LOiHDrJJFFle2i2Q67C2jfOCIJodViWL9+DjSTin04bO4K6pO6YF2TCdJDOxaK\n6odecRb3/pa5XZrF5tXHjC2H/NnZ2o06X17jPCEcJSDTHQYmWEuDGuEaQqtR2sm9\nBcz2HNiWVvHVIboD3kso2MACeXpmxZgKjrqwAxQOu4DihKLqRdMM87o7yBA93gs5\nSTHfmRQXSTX7563mD9Le3p9oGoTOQnWSeet0FWUNBZi8h2f/K0etvdrdC4F8bo3k\n5QyQ271wiTBXBtsAKfJuFodqOoPO3UzDGkErQ0HgAiES2Tp4gBrrTq+Qh7E6rHZb\naFTSdcM0daPEY8VlyNKU+cAm8YJ25XYDPd5MHOk0ISh0ptQRjjpzwXYudGbZW4Mk\nakcMNSrLW9RBISrwm/C0+xrwpjD76HHji+SMjF5Sd12FrIM/j6OlXHxAkuo+9vBd\nrh5LAImS1TzpOrm1az5u\n=UG2h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T13:07:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/3f868209de99b286df1d290b17035541568850f6","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDNmODY4MjA5ZGU5OWIyODZkZjFkMjkwYjE3MDM1NTQxNTY4ODUwZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b","sha":"c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b"}],"sha":"3f868209de99b286df1d290b17035541568850f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/3f868209de99b286df1d290b17035541568850f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:29:06Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:29:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(deploy): make merges to master actually roll out, and declare deploy-on-push (#90)\n\n* feat(deploy): make merges to master actually roll out, and declare deploy-on-push\n\nFuzeKeys was already most of the way to deploy-on-push without saying so.\nArgoCD''s app-of-apps runs automated prune+selfHeal against deploy/helm/fuzekeys\non master, every service leaves image.tag empty so the rendered tag is\nChart.appVersion, and build-and-push.yml tags the GHCR images with that same\nappVersion on every push to master.\n\nThe one thing missing was that appVersion only moved when somebody remembered to\nbump it by hand. Ship backend/frontend/tokenizer code without that bump and the\nimages are rebuilt under a tag the cluster is already running: Argo sees no chart\nchange, nothing restarts, and the deploy silently does not happen. A release\nmechanism whose failure mode is \"looks merged, never shipped\" is the problem\nworth fixing.\n\nrelease-gate.yml\n----------------\nFails a PR that touches backend/, frontend/ or pii-tokenizer/ without moving\nChart.appVersion, and checks the result is SemVer. Docs- and deploy-only PRs pass\nuntouched — they need no rollout.\n\nThe bump is authored by the PR, not committed by a bot, and that is deliberate: a\npush made with GITHUB_TOKEN does not trigger workflow runs, so a bot-pushed bump\nwould advance the PR head to a commit carrying zero checks and the required\ncontexts would never report on it. That is not theoretical — it is exactly what\ngovernance-sync''s push did to FuzeKeys#72, which sat with 0 check runs on its head\nSHA until the branch was rebuilt. CI insists the bump happened; it does not try to\nmake it.\n\nRegistered in .fuze/manifest.json as hardening.requiredChecks so it becomes a\nrequired context the next time the ruleset is applied.\n\nhardening.deployOnPush: true\n----------------------------\nMerging to master reaches production, so this is now declared rather than implied.\nThe canonical auto-merge.yml reads the flag and withholds bot-merge: a human\nmerges every PR, in a deploy window.\n\nCLAUDE.md carried the opposite claim and is corrected. Prod remains GitOps — Argo\nis still the only deployer and nothing here hand-deploys.\n\nVerified: the gate''s logic exercised against real git states — docs-only PR\npasses, app change without a bump fails, app change with 0.1.9 -> 0.1.10 passes\nand satisfies the SemVer check. actionlint 1.7.12 reports 0 errors across\n.github/workflows. Manifest validates against .fuze/repo-manifest.schema.json.\n\n* docs(expert): correct the deploy-on-push claim in the FuzeKeys expert\n\nThe expert told every agent that lands here ''No deploy-on-push ...\nhardening.deployOnPush:false''. That is now the opposite of the truth, and an\nexpert that misdescribes the deploy model is worse than no expert.\n\nThis file is repo-authored, not hub-owned: the canonical agents/fuzekeys-expert.md\nin FuzeSDLC is a stub whose body says ''replace this entire file body with\nrepo-specific content'', and governance-sync''s reconcile on #72 rewrote the other\nagents plus fuzefront-expert and fuzeinfra-expert while leaving this one alone.\nSo the fix belongs here rather than in the hub.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cc4b1d9afec4592f2cfd0d3bcb85e9542e97995","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/0cc4b1d9afec4592f2cfd0d3bcb85e9542e97995"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b","verification":{"payload":"tree 0cc4b1d9afec4592f2cfd0d3bcb85e9542e97995\nparent d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787300946 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787300946 +0300\n\nfeat(deploy): make merges to master actually roll out, and declare deploy-on-push (#90)\n\n* feat(deploy): make merges to master actually roll out, and declare deploy-on-push\n\nFuzeKeys was already most of the way to deploy-on-push without saying so.\nArgoCD''s app-of-apps runs automated prune+selfHeal against deploy/helm/fuzekeys\non master, every service leaves image.tag empty so the rendered tag is\nChart.appVersion, and build-and-push.yml tags the GHCR images with that same\nappVersion on every push to master.\n\nThe one thing missing was that appVersion only moved when somebody remembered to\nbump it by hand. Ship backend/frontend/tokenizer code without that bump and the\nimages are rebuilt under a tag the cluster is already running: Argo sees no chart\nchange, nothing restarts, and the deploy silently does not happen. A release\nmechanism whose failure mode is \"looks merged, never shipped\" is the problem\nworth fixing.\n\nrelease-gate.yml\n----------------\nFails a PR that touches backend/, frontend/ or pii-tokenizer/ without moving\nChart.appVersion, and checks the result is SemVer. Docs- and deploy-only PRs pass\nuntouched — they need no rollout.\n\nThe bump is authored by the PR, not committed by a bot, and that is deliberate: a\npush made with GITHUB_TOKEN does not trigger workflow runs, so a bot-pushed bump\nwould advance the PR head to a commit carrying zero checks and the required\ncontexts would never report on it. That is not theoretical — it is exactly what\ngovernance-sync''s push did to FuzeKeys#72, which sat with 0 check runs on its head\nSHA until the branch was rebuilt. CI insists the bump happened; it does not try to\nmake it.\n\nRegistered in .fuze/manifest.json as hardening.requiredChecks so it becomes a\nrequired context the next time the ruleset is applied.\n\nhardening.deployOnPush: true\n----------------------------\nMerging to master reaches production, so this is now declared rather than implied.\nThe canonical auto-merge.yml reads the flag and withholds bot-merge: a human\nmerges every PR, in a deploy window.\n\nCLAUDE.md carried the opposite claim and is corrected. Prod remains GitOps — Argo\nis still the only deployer and nothing here hand-deploys.\n\nVerified: the gate''s logic exercised against real git states — docs-only PR\npasses, app change without a bump fails, app change with 0.1.9 -> 0.1.10 passes\nand satisfies the SemVer check. actionlint 1.7.12 reports 0 errors across\n.github/workflows. Manifest validates against .fuze/repo-manifest.schema.json.\n\n* docs(expert): correct the deploy-on-push claim in the FuzeKeys expert\n\nThe expert told every agent that lands here ''No deploy-on-push ...\nhardening.deployOnPush:false''. That is now the opposite of the truth, and an\nexpert that misdescribes the deploy model is worse than no expert.\n\nThis file is repo-authored, not hub-owned: the canonical agents/fuzekeys-expert.md\nin FuzeSDLC is a stub whose body says ''replace this entire file body with\nrepo-specific content'', and governance-sync''s reconcile on #72 rewrote the other\nagents plus fuzefront-expert and fuzeinfra-expert while leaving this one alone.\nSo the fix belongs here rather than in the hub.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiAxSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAf8QAB3qhisYpq/BJXczd9Ipsyn2\nXvSfRVZydOMjOb4y61KM+Hn0P5G0oTqj1EtLedfd1AXZm0oHd9+NSaM2jhxfwx0H\ng8Xk7HXOhjawqEAUCSpwqdigxjcyWbjdRxcHRM6zRNN8QyAT8LPg5YtDLfNee1Dh\nMNjCOvbtPdxGdXpmoRgLELLNEnuEUe8V94frI0/qwmosJe4OMCkGQAGwc23GG1GW\n3lhk3V8bpr0cuI2vFydHnzhFW0Fit7KnsKHc23dHoSxNFg3SfcWn9eJJDKkYG/SS\ny4TWzL5rmNMRM8caWsy30uMh+uskZY3mT0qCCfHRSeqQu3IPYqIVyqIutLwm/v6w\nWsr2rCPBFi7Q2wdGxaAaGxi51VV4nJaIFjc9SEHpll2v0V6Kp1DqVgMJLVe4esbU\nYpciFReIHq2pq/jQGwv/fIhmGZCwO+LiOmPCfPolF0YVYsYU+58LK9PFz5S1Wk82\nNGsc5xQhHhASB+y/r3cyW6YoD8Y2dJD4OO2XRDVDEzOSyQhMIcshSN3voXZUwG+h\nZojtev8prHIUlXxy/16HHLsU+joSBgaHcLBXdwx9N4txzhrVedtAhoTkOXB2U28L\nGvfLWAVJ5HeJb8+jJAUQ4FqoQ//+YWjbzNcC4HNKgQ2BCCyU3YnvVGCEH0ZhH8am\niZNbXCSNZlAAaW00aDdP\n=D+H5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T08:29:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGMzZjU1NjU1OTRkNWZlMGFhYzZkYzhkMjUxYWY2YzQ3NWM4MzNkOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22","sha":"d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22"}],"sha":"c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/c3f5565594d5fe0aac6dc8d251af6c475c833d8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T07:57:25Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T07:57:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(sdlc): bootstrap to FuzeSDLC v1.8.0 via the capability installer (#92)\n\nReplaces #71, a v1.6.0 snapshot from 2026-08-10. Re-runs the installer against\ncurrent master instead of rebasing a three-month-old render: the engine is\nidempotent and ledger-driven, so a fresh run produces the correct tree rather\nthan a merge of two stale ones.\n\n#71 could not simply be rebased. It edited google_integration.py to change\nmanual_signup''s signature while the route still sat BELOW /signup/{identity_id}.\nMaster moved it above, because declaration order is load-bearing -- a\nparameterised route declared first swallows the literal, and /signup/manual was\nunreachable in production until #82 fixed it.\n\nThis is not \"re-applying\" hardening. CLAUDE.md''s already-hardened line enumerates\nthe ruleset, Harden Gate, signed commits, the automation stack and nightly\nreconciliation; all five are in place and untouched. The capability INSTALLER is\na separate thing that had never run here -- there was no .fuze/installed.json at\nall.\n\nCanonical checked out at the tag this repo pins: baselineRef v1 -> d4c7231,\nbaseline v1.8.0. The engine refuses to run from a canonical ahead of the pin,\ncorrectly, since governance-sync fetches at that ref on every PR.\n\n61 files, +6144/-1. The only modifications to existing files are an `engines`\nblock in backend/package.json and frontend/package.json; everything else is a\npure addition -- .fuze/installed.json (the provenance ledger whose absence froze\nevery managed file at whatever version first installed it), 40 .claude/skills/**,\n6 workflows, 8 scripts, .nvmrc/.npmrc/.github/actionlint.yaml.\n\nNothing merged earlier was touched, verified file by file: deploy-platform.yml,\nci.yml, governance/api-version-allowlist.txt, both Argo Applications,\nkeys-broker/role.json, accounts.py and conftest.py are byte-identical to master.\n.fuze/manifest.json is NOT modified.\n\nVerified: backend suite 225 passed / 0 skipped; actionlint 0 findings over the 6\nnew workflows; gate-api-version both halves PASS against the hub''s current gate;\nstamp-frames --check a clean no-op; new test_gate_identifier.py 12 tests pass.\n\nINSTALLED BUT NOT ENABLED, called out so it is not mistaken for silent\nactivation: gate_identifier.py reports 16 findings, but the gate-identifier JOB\nis absent from this repo''s harden-gate.yml, so installing the script does not\nturn the gate on. And `engines` declares node >=24 while ci.yml''s matrix is\n18/20 -- advisory only, since no .npmrc sets engine-strict.\n\nThree code-scanning findings surfaced by this PR are fixed at source in FuzeSDLC\n#142, since the files are hub-reconciled.\n\nCloses #71","tree":{"sha":"564c339c255c429f1218a67b4a0f43e4067b1238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/564c339c255c429f1218a67b4a0f43e4067b1238"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22","verification":{"payload":"tree 564c339c255c429f1218a67b4a0f43e4067b1238\nparent 25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787299045 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787299045 +0300\n\nchore(sdlc): bootstrap to FuzeSDLC v1.8.0 via the capability installer (#92)\n\nReplaces #71, a v1.6.0 snapshot from 2026-08-10. Re-runs the installer against\ncurrent master instead of rebasing a three-month-old render: the engine is\nidempotent and ledger-driven, so a fresh run produces the correct tree rather\nthan a merge of two stale ones.\n\n#71 could not simply be rebased. It edited google_integration.py to change\nmanual_signup''s signature while the route still sat BELOW /signup/{identity_id}.\nMaster moved it above, because declaration order is load-bearing -- a\nparameterised route declared first swallows the literal, and /signup/manual was\nunreachable in production until #82 fixed it.\n\nThis is not \"re-applying\" hardening. CLAUDE.md''s already-hardened line enumerates\nthe ruleset, Harden Gate, signed commits, the automation stack and nightly\nreconciliation; all five are in place and untouched. The capability INSTALLER is\na separate thing that had never run here -- there was no .fuze/installed.json at\nall.\n\nCanonical checked out at the tag this repo pins: baselineRef v1 -> d4c7231,\nbaseline v1.8.0. The engine refuses to run from a canonical ahead of the pin,\ncorrectly, since governance-sync fetches at that ref on every PR.\n\n61 files, +6144/-1. The only modifications to existing files are an `engines`\nblock in backend/package.json and frontend/package.json; everything else is a\npure addition -- .fuze/installed.json (the provenance ledger whose absence froze\nevery managed file at whatever version first installed it), 40 .claude/skills/**,\n6 workflows, 8 scripts, .nvmrc/.npmrc/.github/actionlint.yaml.\n\nNothing merged earlier was touched, verified file by file: deploy-platform.yml,\nci.yml, governance/api-version-allowlist.txt, both Argo Applications,\nkeys-broker/role.json, accounts.py and conftest.py are byte-identical to master.\n.fuze/manifest.json is NOT modified.\n\nVerified: backend suite 225 passed / 0 skipped; actionlint 0 findings over the 6\nnew workflows; gate-api-version both halves PASS against the hub''s current gate;\nstamp-frames --check a clean no-op; new test_gate_identifier.py 12 tests pass.\n\nINSTALLED BUT NOT ENABLED, called out so it is not mistaken for silent\nactivation: gate_identifier.py reports 16 findings, but the gate-identifier JOB\nis absent from this repo''s harden-gate.yml, so installing the script does not\nturn the gate on. And `engines` declares node >=24 while ci.yml''s matrix is\n18/20 -- advisory only, since no .npmrc sets engine-strict.\n\nThree code-scanning findings surfaced by this PR are fixed at source in FuzeSDLC\n#142, since the files are hub-reconciled.\n\nCloses #71","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiATlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPysQAKRKrlLLW/HXG1+5A3LEQ81T\nyrhPb9C6IVoGrWkNtS1L6pmxBUgjlMAHUqmSRPZu5Ca3UqnC+Cx073QPk3Gpiz7f\nNwUEEB69b/pmHzNfR723J1yfKdBBNXjgzeCwgptlFhaYX1CpiezBm1DEpqj31ep+\n1EBxS/Li8wxaVckLQPucB/APN8SYJpVokX4fS9aXI8aDklVku00UugCnNuM72e80\nxw2fitZCqgArSFSqjjN+pjbdaiTnnYrjNgIhYb8GN69T1ZA6bm+po96IC+kBUQze\nMVKyb3wynO2nn0GINlJiWv6e4tAWWIjFqPjSOyruJbuaVJfO+jMh8aKhQQxauJTV\ni2K5J2rbkOkN+d9emdP01bWkwPUCuBSOpFSpzjbmvCTmY1uXQvAKBu2kOkCRbjSB\nRXH+Ub/pBwDnE/gqDbfyYDf3k0HFq+8OvlmsQJFoWwfQ/7IeMSmv2HFnW7FOe4L5\nTCNfQQNQWqyfRZz9D247h4CZlb9dk826iYjEUMzeGzts8SgDMBuAi90zBL/Gtx/I\neSO0L5obWMSSanxAQ0LRhyAvi8tGgjl+0r+2ZGU/6095j3+kh5fTHRlNMAy9cuoK\nuCVWkqRXsZYvYy+7eF10fU7sq7LYoU1xTa0tJHHBZ8yZxJkW7B8VBfLJYDMT9MHK\njWCh8HIvPPiix5MdjwWi\n=0HbT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T07:57:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGQ3NmMyOWM4ZWFiMTJkMzNhMTZmZDE2MmQyYjg2YjFmODk4YTRiMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d","sha":"25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d"}],"sha":"d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/d76c29c8eab12d33a16fd162d2b86b1f898a4b22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T07:49:17Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T07:49:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy-platform): actionlint ignored the file list, so the ratchet did nothing (#93)\n\nThe ratchet added in #87 did not work. raven-actions/actionlint''s `files:` input\ndoes not accept a list -- given six space-separated paths it silently falls back\nto its default glob. Its own log on #92 is unambiguous:\n\n    Found 6 errors in 24 files\n\n24 is every workflow in the repo. So the job still hard-failed on the whole tree,\non the same six pre-existing findings in hub-reconciled files, while LOOKING\nscoped -- the worst kind of broken, because the step was named \"changed workflows\nonly\" and the summary agreed with it.\n\nI verified the six new workflows passed clean before opening #92. That was true\nand beside the point: the action was never linting only those six. I tested the\nfiles in isolation rather than the invocation.\n\nFixed by invoking actionlint as a pinned binary instead of through the action.\nThe binary takes explicit paths, so the scope is the scope -- there is no input\ncontract to misread. Version and SHA-256 are pinned and the checksum verified\nbefore extraction, matching how harden-gate installs gitleaks; the digest was\nchecked against the official actionlint_1.7.12_checksums.txt rather than taken\nfrom the download. shellcheck ships on ubuntu-latest and actionlint picks it up\nautomatically, so coverage is unchanged -- same checks, invoked directly.\n\nSimulated both real cases locally with the same binary CI now uses:\n  - this PR''s changed set (deploy-platform.yml alone)   -> exit 0\n  - #92''s changed set (the 6 installer-added workflows) -> exit 0\n\nThe master-branch step still reports the whole-tree backlog as a warning, so the\nsix findings stay visible. They are fixed at source in FuzeSDLC #143.","tree":{"sha":"80dcfc6349ca64c89df50ca4c64384c195f4a859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/80dcfc6349ca64c89df50ca4c64384c195f4a859"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d","verification":{"payload":"tree 80dcfc6349ca64c89df50ca4c64384c195f4a859\nparent 144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787298557 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787298557 +0300\n\nfix(deploy-platform): actionlint ignored the file list, so the ratchet did nothing (#93)\n\nThe ratchet added in #87 did not work. raven-actions/actionlint''s `files:` input\ndoes not accept a list -- given six space-separated paths it silently falls back\nto its default glob. Its own log on #92 is unambiguous:\n\n    Found 6 errors in 24 files\n\n24 is every workflow in the repo. So the job still hard-failed on the whole tree,\non the same six pre-existing findings in hub-reconciled files, while LOOKING\nscoped -- the worst kind of broken, because the step was named \"changed workflows\nonly\" and the summary agreed with it.\n\nI verified the six new workflows passed clean before opening #92. That was true\nand beside the point: the action was never linting only those six. I tested the\nfiles in isolation rather than the invocation.\n\nFixed by invoking actionlint as a pinned binary instead of through the action.\nThe binary takes explicit paths, so the scope is the scope -- there is no input\ncontract to misread. Version and SHA-256 are pinned and the checksum verified\nbefore extraction, matching how harden-gate installs gitleaks; the digest was\nchecked against the official actionlint_1.7.12_checksums.txt rather than taken\nfrom the download. shellcheck ships on ubuntu-latest and actionlint picks it up\nautomatically, so coverage is unchanged -- same checks, invoked directly.\n\nSimulated both real cases locally with the same binary CI now uses:\n  - this PR''s changed set (deploy-platform.yml alone)   -> exit 0\n  - #92''s changed set (the 6 installer-added workflows) -> exit 0\n\nThe master-branch step still reports the whole-tree backlog as a warning, so the\nsix findings stay visible. They are fixed at source in FuzeSDLC #143.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiAL9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4P8QAFlY1iYb9WL1jvkvZNx4eM9A\nLx76pWTvp3a3ItXQAkTGdSzhF87ByXLRWdeEl+bcTgxM4tZhfEJp/jCa5pS9G0LP\nQXe1/+ed5Fh3E2Q6MewIlhi0PhjVp4bc3f7R9aXmkXF5W0SpFKuOYyBNiMXOqRsy\nsas+84eBBaTg1RwRZP0xkDrcD7MStyP38vkglGGspRumOtvBxH67WZIVFa1uFGNe\nXXxeF6/nMRVt+H2tjcyxmZPB3zy9r2PoS5CQMxS2leKwjaG/uj3GEjIw/lenKSh0\nczZzzSkBvZLr38hUvOW8w5hBL3KFYcY7M/zkSo18svBFDCDtR6gcHxBsBJNHPrLK\nN7cShYk4V7mUQY2lmjo8QO41p++ZNSWHoCYvZWPM2dPDlbNRjOushO0eC3ZsiG5p\nwzZh8LLG4ApiWcowqo07FciMmQMYOzPSOyTKp5LHEH8WCTGKUX8jbG1OnvXwmotq\nuIMo/FiDkwxrwDLx7Xabmmt6WvXAZO/jVj09TaqkWkxL6/3cY+eQ6bR3zy8fmX3p\n+cxcDKrTmVcliRevfepk2E/wbk5fdqXc0knPEEt4RYE1QHjycT3WA/le1ZHRYB9D\ni6qZdpiIuQpdklOBPIjCB6MV8pjVitBg1CvLv84V7sDm5C1LcwQw+SKcLNDCd2KZ\ngvK6y0TQgb1UdqYSRaWa\n=jtoA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T07:49:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDI1NjI2Y2E2YTZkOWY4MGEwNmIyYjU5OTdhYzEzMjA0MTljYzczN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace","sha":"144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace"}],"sha":"25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/25626ca6a6d9f80a06b2b5997ac1320419cc737d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:50:44Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:50:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(argocd): make fuzekeys-sealed self-heal and sync before the platform (#87)\n\nCombines #38 (issue #35) and #39 (issue #36), rebased onto master. They were\nopened three seconds apart off the same base, edit the same Application at\ndisjoint hunks, and merge cleanly against each other -- two halves of one\ncold-start fix. Verified still needed: of the 37 master commits since their\nmerge-base, the only two touching deploy/argocd/** were an unrelated MCP feature\nand a docs edit.\n\nORDERING. fuzekeys-sealed gets sync-wave -1, fuzekeys-platform 0. The platform''s\nPreSync migrate Job hard-depends on Secrets the sealed app provides\n(ghcr-pull-secret to pull the private image, fuzekeys-secrets via envFrom).\nWithout a wave they reconcile concurrently; on a cold cluster PreSync races ahead\nof the SealedSecrets materialising, the Job wedges in ImagePullBackOff, PreSync\nnever completes, and the platform app latches Missing/OutOfSync.\n\nSELF-HEAL. ServerSideApply plus a retry backoff on fuzekeys-sealed. Argo can\nattempt the first sync before FuzeInfra''s sealed-secrets controller has\nregistered the SealedSecret CRD; that apply fails and the error lands in\n.status.operationState, not .status.conditions -- which is why #34/#35/#36 all\nshow `conditions: null`. ServerSideApply also avoids the client-side\nlast-applied-configuration annotation on the large encryptedData blobs, which\napproaches the 262 KiB metadata limit and leaves creationTimestamp diffing\nforever. Not novel configuration: fuzekeys-platform already had both, and the two\nApplications'' syncPolicy are now identical.\n\nALSO, because it blocked this PR: the actionlint job hard-failed on the WHOLE\nworkflow tree over 6 pre-existing shellcheck findings in three hub-reconciled\nworkflows this repo cannot fix. It is now ratcheted to the workflows a PR\nchanges, matching the pattern gate-line-endings.yml documents in this same repo.\nNet effect is MORE coverage: the trigger paths were deploy/** and itself, so\nediting any workflow previously triggered no lint at all. .github/workflows/** is\nnow a trigger. actionlint is pinned to a commit SHA, addressing the Semgrep\nmutable-tag finding on both call sites.\n\nCloses #35\nCloses #36","tree":{"sha":"466ec43d93d6742eb89a06a0820750647caf0a9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/466ec43d93d6742eb89a06a0820750647caf0a9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace","verification":{"payload":"tree 466ec43d93d6742eb89a06a0820750647caf0a9d\nparent 40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787255444 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787255444 +0300\n\nfix(argocd): make fuzekeys-sealed self-heal and sync before the platform (#87)\n\nCombines #38 (issue #35) and #39 (issue #36), rebased onto master. They were\nopened three seconds apart off the same base, edit the same Application at\ndisjoint hunks, and merge cleanly against each other -- two halves of one\ncold-start fix. Verified still needed: of the 37 master commits since their\nmerge-base, the only two touching deploy/argocd/** were an unrelated MCP feature\nand a docs edit.\n\nORDERING. fuzekeys-sealed gets sync-wave -1, fuzekeys-platform 0. The platform''s\nPreSync migrate Job hard-depends on Secrets the sealed app provides\n(ghcr-pull-secret to pull the private image, fuzekeys-secrets via envFrom).\nWithout a wave they reconcile concurrently; on a cold cluster PreSync races ahead\nof the SealedSecrets materialising, the Job wedges in ImagePullBackOff, PreSync\nnever completes, and the platform app latches Missing/OutOfSync.\n\nSELF-HEAL. ServerSideApply plus a retry backoff on fuzekeys-sealed. Argo can\nattempt the first sync before FuzeInfra''s sealed-secrets controller has\nregistered the SealedSecret CRD; that apply fails and the error lands in\n.status.operationState, not .status.conditions -- which is why #34/#35/#36 all\nshow `conditions: null`. ServerSideApply also avoids the client-side\nlast-applied-configuration annotation on the large encryptedData blobs, which\napproaches the 262 KiB metadata limit and leaves creationTimestamp diffing\nforever. Not novel configuration: fuzekeys-platform already had both, and the two\nApplications'' syncPolicy are now identical.\n\nALSO, because it blocked this PR: the actionlint job hard-failed on the WHOLE\nworkflow tree over 6 pre-existing shellcheck findings in three hub-reconciled\nworkflows this repo cannot fix. It is now ratcheted to the workflows a PR\nchanges, matching the pattern gate-line-endings.yml documents in this same repo.\nNet effect is MORE coverage: the trigger paths were deploy/** and itself, so\nediting any workflow previously triggered no lint at all. .github/workflows/** is\nnow a trigger. actionlint is pinned to a commit SHA, addressing the Semgrep\nmutable-tag finding on both call sites.\n\nCloses #35\nCloses #36","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh1qUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJoIQAEkwts+GfaG9FPYpr1aJrUKE\nMrXxe+zRYTYGZOV4LKiV0iWiJsn7wkuvVGXKRmE1iJMiK/GTzDBAyNo2PwAKRr/B\nv+5luJOKwDac3jz6BgpKLpQehY34bhnG0b7kla8iNJO7PnA7ZWZ6AjwMkibdwCQH\nDceafpzmLR1a29dO2gTsfOrZEOXQmuBQVPXXtTG+TiSi9EuhcPG2ePOTT17HbBOw\njesgDDQjMUndXjVd6OPmeDo3oDkH6vHyXIPGzJq9TQrlLe4oTys4F5ZRd9cfG0HL\nZ/UrwgeBp6/BjPhm0c/3WRgBnRZtn6L75kG5EL+xCyrdsPly9HneWb0fkZEwEdrR\n6cMkfh6nH7b3GAr78XDspNL6EV/4NHj7udmK2ZhK4MOOYneS2XjA3lSErjyMhQWQ\ngwXqovoWZ1r34IZr3KnALzARApej+9hl5ls5R63rQ5c3pIbn/GSBh+4pI99wouCf\nMBitEMbrBgUpX9W+0wTK3negucrJLpIVFLOnvOAu3zXeaCkL02nZWzSJbfixUtxk\nhkrI9pLRLPBwzMHxbZdR+ALvyRAzeTf746nsFh8ouwtRneGn5car+mI1FMOVtqHC\nuLTQxhRIkFhUbMZJbCtL78NY7ogBXuhpdUvM+vJXuoaJqqTYSr8MVMoydR1YBXGX\nAxl4XCeMnNEhqk5K7Jkg\n=9Gvv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T19:50:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDE0NGVkNWI5YjFmMzM1MzFhYjMwZjdkYjU1M2Q5MzYzOGE2MjlhY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669","sha":"40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669"}],"sha":"144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/144ed5b9b1f33531ab30f7db553d93638a629ace"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:27:32Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:27:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): match the host''s React 19 singleton so the remote actually mounts (#89)\n\n* fix(frontend): match the host''s React 19 singleton so the remote actually mounts\n\nRefs FuzeFront#658. Second of the Module-Federation remotes, after\nFuzePicker#71 (merged) proved the fix. FuzeKeys is the only other remote in\nthe family on the `^18.0.0` form.\n\nfrontend/vite.config.ts declared:\n\n  shared: {\n    react:       { singleton: true, requiredVersion: ''^18.0.0'' },\n    ''react-dom'': { singleton: true, requiredVersion: ''^18.0.0'' },\n  }\n\nFuzeFront''s frontend/vite.config.ts declares both singletons at ''^19.0.0'' and\nships React 19. As the Module-Federation host it IS the shared-singleton\ncontract for the family. `singleton: true` with a requiredVersion the host\ncannot satisfy makes the remote fall back to its OWN React copy, and two\nReacts in one tree throw \"Invalid hook call\" the moment a hook runs -- so the\nportal mounts the remote and renders nothing.\n\nChanged, per the family toolchain floor:\n\n  react / react-dom            ^18.2.0   -> ^19.2.0\n  @types/react                 ^18.2.37  -> ^19.2.0\n  @types/react-dom             ^18.2.15  -> ^19.2.0\n  MF shared requiredVersion    ^18.0.0   -> ^19.0.0\n\nVERIFIED, not assumed:\n  - No React 19 removals in frontend/src: no defaultProps on function\n    components, no propTypes, no string refs. The single `ReactDOM.render`\n    grep hit is a STRING LITERAL inside setupTests.ts''s console-warning\n    filter, not a call -- checked rather than counted. index.tsx already uses\n    createRoot from react-dom/client.\n  - npm install resolves a single react/react-dom 19.2.8 (npm ls, depth 0);\n    package-lock.json updated to match so CI installs the same tree.\n  - vite build succeeds, 3470 modules, emits remoteEntry.js and\n    __federation_expose_FuzeKeysApp.\n  - The BUILT OUTPUT carries requiredVersion:''^19.0.0'' and there is no `^18`\n    anywhere in dist-mfe. Checking the artifact, not the source, because the\n    source is what was already lying.\n\nREFINEMENT TO THE CANARY''S METHOD, worth carrying to the remaining remotes:\nFuzePicker''s build embedded requiredVersion in remoteEntry.js; this one puts\nit in __federation_fn_import-*.js and remoteEntry.js contains no version\nstring at all. Grepping only remoteEntry.js would have reported \"no\nrequiredVersion found\" on a correct build and, worse, would report the same\non a broken one. Grep the whole build output.\n\nNOT VERIFIED HERE, and it is the thing that actually matters: that the remote\nnow mounts and renders inside the live portal. That needs the image rebuilt,\ndeployed, and loaded in a browser against app.fuzefront.com -- unreachable\nfrom this environment. Confirm after deploy, ideally with the\nui-runtime-validation console check.\n\n* fix(frontend): give useRef an initial value — React 19 dropped the 0-arg overload\n\nCI caught what my local verification did not:\n\n  src/components/SitesDatabase.tsx(90,20): error TS2554:\n  Expected 1 arguments, but got 0.\n\n`useRef<IntersectionObserver>()` was legal under @types/react 18 and is an\nerror under 19: the zero-argument overload was removed, so a ref must be\ngiven an explicit initial value. This is the only such call site in\nfrontend/src -- checked, one occurrence.\n\nMY VERIFICATION GAP, worth naming so the remaining remotes do not repeat it.\nFor this PR and for FuzePicker#71 I ran `vite build` and inspected the built\nartifact, and treated a green build as \"the React 19 bump is safe\". It is\nnot: vite build does NOT type-check. tsc runs as a separate `type-check`\nscript and it is the only thing that sees @types/react changes at all. A\nReact major bump is precisely a TYPES change, so the one check I skipped was\nthe one aimed at the class of breakage I was introducing.\n\nThe pre-flight scan I did run -- ReactDOM.render / defaultProps / propTypes /\nstring refs -- is a scan for RUNTIME removals. It cannot see a removed\ntype overload, and passing it says nothing about compilation.\n\nFor the remaining remotes: run `npm run type-check` (or tsc --noEmit) as well\nas the build, and treat the build alone as insufficient.\n\nVerified after this change: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `eslint --max-warnings 0`\nclean, `vite build` succeeds and still emits remoteEntry.js with\nrequiredVersion ''^19.0.0'' and no ^18 in the output.\n\n* fix(frontend): bump @headlessui/react to v2 — the actual React 19 blocker\n\nUnblocks the CRA build that failed on this branch:\n\n  Attempted import error: ''__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED''\n  is not exported from ''react'' (imported as ''r'').\n\nThe culprit is @headlessui/react@1.7.19. Its dist/utils/stable-collection.js\ndoes `import * as r from \"react\"` and reads\n`r.__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED`, which React 19\nremoved. The error message even names the binding -- \"imported as ''r''\" --\nand that file is the only place in node_modules that imports react under\nthat name and touches the symbol. v2.2.10 does not use it.\n\nI PREVIOUSLY BLAMED antd/rc-util, AND WAS WRONG. That deserves recording\nrather than quiet deletion, because the reasoning failure is reusable:\n\n  - I grepped node_modules for the symbol, saw rc-util (a transitive dep of\n    antd), and treated the grep hit as the cause.\n  - It was not even a candidate on the evidence I already had. rc-util reads\n    the symbol off a spread of react-dom, not react; the error says react.\n    And the error named the binding ''r''; rc-util imports as ''ReactDOM''.\n  - The proposed remedy that followed -- an antd 5 -> 6 major migration --\n    was large, breaking, and would not have worked.\n\nProven by experiment rather than argument, in this order:\n  1. antd 5.26 -> 6.6.1                    -> build STILL FAILS\n  2. antd 6 + @ant-design/icons 6, with\n     rc-util absent from the tree entirely\n     (`npm ls rc-util` -> empty)           -> build STILL FAILS\n  3. antd left at 5.26, @headlessui/react\n     1.7.19 -> 2.2.10                      -> Compiled successfully.\n\nStep 2 is the one that settles it: the build still failed with rc-util\ncompletely gone, so rc-util was never the cause. antd is untouched by this\ncommit and needs no migration.\n\nSurface is one file: src/components/SitesDatabase.tsx imports { Tab }. v2\nkeeps that export, and tsc confirms the types still line up.\n\nVerified, all four, on this branch:\n  - npm run build (react-scripts / CRA)  -> Compiled successfully\n  - tsc --noEmit                         -> clean\n  - eslint --max-warnings 0              -> clean\n  - vite build (the MF remote)           -> emits remoteEntry.js, output\n    carries requiredVersion:''^19.0.0'', no ^18 anywhere in dist-mfe\n\nNote CRA (react-scripts) is deprecated upstream as of Feb 2025 and this repo\nalready builds its Module-Federation remote with Vite. Retiring the CRA half\nwould remove this whole class of blocker permanently, but that is a separate\ndecision and is deliberately not bundled here.","tree":{"sha":"795a066147aa51513dbfea6be769feea22a8b4de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/795a066147aa51513dbfea6be769feea22a8b4de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669","verification":{"payload":"tree 795a066147aa51513dbfea6be769feea22a8b4de\nparent 603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787239652 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787239652 +0300\n\nfix(frontend): match the host''s React 19 singleton so the remote actually mounts (#89)\n\n* fix(frontend): match the host''s React 19 singleton so the remote actually mounts\n\nRefs FuzeFront#658. Second of the Module-Federation remotes, after\nFuzePicker#71 (merged) proved the fix. FuzeKeys is the only other remote in\nthe family on the `^18.0.0` form.\n\nfrontend/vite.config.ts declared:\n\n  shared: {\n    react:       { singleton: true, requiredVersion: ''^18.0.0'' },\n    ''react-dom'': { singleton: true, requiredVersion: ''^18.0.0'' },\n  }\n\nFuzeFront''s frontend/vite.config.ts declares both singletons at ''^19.0.0'' and\nships React 19. As the Module-Federation host it IS the shared-singleton\ncontract for the family. `singleton: true` with a requiredVersion the host\ncannot satisfy makes the remote fall back to its OWN React copy, and two\nReacts in one tree throw \"Invalid hook call\" the moment a hook runs -- so the\nportal mounts the remote and renders nothing.\n\nChanged, per the family toolchain floor:\n\n  react / react-dom            ^18.2.0   -> ^19.2.0\n  @types/react                 ^18.2.37  -> ^19.2.0\n  @types/react-dom             ^18.2.15  -> ^19.2.0\n  MF shared requiredVersion    ^18.0.0   -> ^19.0.0\n\nVERIFIED, not assumed:\n  - No React 19 removals in frontend/src: no defaultProps on function\n    components, no propTypes, no string refs. The single `ReactDOM.render`\n    grep hit is a STRING LITERAL inside setupTests.ts''s console-warning\n    filter, not a call -- checked rather than counted. index.tsx already uses\n    createRoot from react-dom/client.\n  - npm install resolves a single react/react-dom 19.2.8 (npm ls, depth 0);\n    package-lock.json updated to match so CI installs the same tree.\n  - vite build succeeds, 3470 modules, emits remoteEntry.js and\n    __federation_expose_FuzeKeysApp.\n  - The BUILT OUTPUT carries requiredVersion:''^19.0.0'' and there is no `^18`\n    anywhere in dist-mfe. Checking the artifact, not the source, because the\n    source is what was already lying.\n\nREFINEMENT TO THE CANARY''S METHOD, worth carrying to the remaining remotes:\nFuzePicker''s build embedded requiredVersion in remoteEntry.js; this one puts\nit in __federation_fn_import-*.js and remoteEntry.js contains no version\nstring at all. Grepping only remoteEntry.js would have reported \"no\nrequiredVersion found\" on a correct build and, worse, would report the same\non a broken one. Grep the whole build output.\n\nNOT VERIFIED HERE, and it is the thing that actually matters: that the remote\nnow mounts and renders inside the live portal. That needs the image rebuilt,\ndeployed, and loaded in a browser against app.fuzefront.com -- unreachable\nfrom this environment. Confirm after deploy, ideally with the\nui-runtime-validation console check.\n\n* fix(frontend): give useRef an initial value — React 19 dropped the 0-arg overload\n\nCI caught what my local verification did not:\n\n  src/components/SitesDatabase.tsx(90,20): error TS2554:\n  Expected 1 arguments, but got 0.\n\n`useRef<IntersectionObserver>()` was legal under @types/react 18 and is an\nerror under 19: the zero-argument overload was removed, so a ref must be\ngiven an explicit initial value. This is the only such call site in\nfrontend/src -- checked, one occurrence.\n\nMY VERIFICATION GAP, worth naming so the remaining remotes do not repeat it.\nFor this PR and for FuzePicker#71 I ran `vite build` and inspected the built\nartifact, and treated a green build as \"the React 19 bump is safe\". It is\nnot: vite build does NOT type-check. tsc runs as a separate `type-check`\nscript and it is the only thing that sees @types/react changes at all. A\nReact major bump is precisely a TYPES change, so the one check I skipped was\nthe one aimed at the class of breakage I was introducing.\n\nThe pre-flight scan I did run -- ReactDOM.render / defaultProps / propTypes /\nstring refs -- is a scan for RUNTIME removals. It cannot see a removed\ntype overload, and passing it says nothing about compilation.\n\nFor the remaining remotes: run `npm run type-check` (or tsc --noEmit) as well\nas the build, and treat the build alone as insufficient.\n\nVerified after this change: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `eslint --max-warnings 0`\nclean, `vite build` succeeds and still emits remoteEntry.js with\nrequiredVersion ''^19.0.0'' and no ^18 in the output.\n\n* fix(frontend): bump @headlessui/react to v2 — the actual React 19 blocker\n\nUnblocks the CRA build that failed on this branch:\n\n  Attempted import error: ''__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED''\n  is not exported from ''react'' (imported as ''r'').\n\nThe culprit is @headlessui/react@1.7.19. Its dist/utils/stable-collection.js\ndoes `import * as r from \"react\"` and reads\n`r.__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED`, which React 19\nremoved. The error message even names the binding -- \"imported as ''r''\" --\nand that file is the only place in node_modules that imports react under\nthat name and touches the symbol. v2.2.10 does not use it.\n\nI PREVIOUSLY BLAMED antd/rc-util, AND WAS WRONG. That deserves recording\nrather than quiet deletion, because the reasoning failure is reusable:\n\n  - I grepped node_modules for the symbol, saw rc-util (a transitive dep of\n    antd), and treated the grep hit as the cause.\n  - It was not even a candidate on the evidence I already had. rc-util reads\n    the symbol off a spread of react-dom, not react; the error says react.\n    And the error named the binding ''r''; rc-util imports as ''ReactDOM''.\n  - The proposed remedy that followed -- an antd 5 -> 6 major migration --\n    was large, breaking, and would not have worked.\n\nProven by experiment rather than argument, in this order:\n  1. antd 5.26 -> 6.6.1                    -> build STILL FAILS\n  2. antd 6 + @ant-design/icons 6, with\n     rc-util absent from the tree entirely\n     (`npm ls rc-util` -> empty)           -> build STILL FAILS\n  3. antd left at 5.26, @headlessui/react\n     1.7.19 -> 2.2.10                      -> Compiled successfully.\n\nStep 2 is the one that settles it: the build still failed with rc-util\ncompletely gone, so rc-util was never the cause. antd is untouched by this\ncommit and needs no migration.\n\nSurface is one file: src/components/SitesDatabase.tsx imports { Tab }. v2\nkeeps that export, and tsc confirms the types still line up.\n\nVerified, all four, on this branch:\n  - npm run build (react-scripts / CRA)  -> Compiled successfully\n  - tsc --noEmit                         -> clean\n  - eslint --max-warnings 0              -> clean\n  - vite build (the MF remote)           -> emits remoteEntry.js, output\n    carries requiredVersion:''^19.0.0'', no ^18 anywhere in dist-mfe\n\nNote CRA (react-scripts) is deprecated upstream as of Feb 2025 and this repo\nalready builds its Module-Federation remote with Vite. Retiring the CRA half\nwould remove this whole class of blocker permanently, but that is a separate\ndecision and is deliberately not bundled here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhxzkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArcwQAE69WQJVhVinW/s9E6MoixEy\n5XQ0zm5ZH0u3ZRd1fMiIvlKxkYkkCsgxz5HOHTLc8x7KWI4I/0Hi+fEi8dSTIBeh\n/Aqj57QF2wQt8ucn7WnGw+tHJrnNdE29snpuny22rCH+Ely22Aw7zzl44D6M+XfE\nqj+9hHG8Pq8AdVz9VfnzjwKc2fUZ898Z5eNJI2iYcCPf4r/qvGoalcNkoFESrOpe\neywmThSk4044awaRtf0oW31pBq1aeZY3PierTjcNNyZvV2Y1ZsVSNIF5a/HWxAja\nYPbK1eN/W+DPhOzB1dpz0DKUyaFjBCdXj4iEsasHCfkJGUMYZ/nQvANJLY9cPDVZ\nBvYMpVJqEL2RMGi0oNWtyRBSJZu1ZNmB+Ogohl20sZLUKMqs3RCEr1rHQ4Q7OKUD\n91knEfp2RX4v6nsDK3oTz3C0Pq+9N6b01FRs3C789scMvfVddh3eLahbF96ATsAe\nQMKvXNq+5QdKM2pClRIr3F98wwNK656sSRpZ33X9AfyArwG8A9YmxDqOQdAY1lz5\nefYmBnhogvzoFFQ4il86dzJB/1aMM92n45SZPuWUSNfKOEJtOnlP4ioDbEuYxzvj\n8SgzYD30Eh6kKJeBS3VuR1bQXVFrRswFW+56eO6j0ZP1CWb3dxTQRioA7mLcp5dP\nUlEO0U1G4BiUG+wzycwC\n=7fO0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T15:27:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDQwNzEyY2NjZTczZmQ3Nzc4N2UyNjY1OTUzMjY4YjQyNGU0MDQ2Njk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183","sha":"603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183"}],"sha":"40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/40712ccce73fd77787e2665953268b424e404669"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:33Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:44:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a2a): reshape the keys-broker role to the contract, without inheriting tools (#88)\n\nRebase of #69 onto master, reduced to the one file that is this repo''s to\nchange, plus a fix for a privilege inheritance the original introduced.\n\nFive of #69''s six files were hub-reconciled (governance_sync.py declares\nFRAMEWORK_DIRS = schema, roles/_base, sync, providers) and master already held\nNEWER copies, so merging them would have written stale content the next sync\nreverts. Only agent-templates/roles/<role>/role.json is repo-owned.\n\nThe breakage is real: master''s role.json fails its own schema with 3 errors\n(''role'' required and missing; six unexpected top-level keys; two unexpected keys\nunder a2a) and renders an EMPTY system prompt, so validate.py''s\n`assert payload[\"system\"]` fails and the card projection has no description. The\nreshaped file validates with 0 errors and renders 2434 characters.\n\nTHE ADDED FIX. #69 introduced `extends: \"_base\"` while declaring no tools of its\nown. _base supplies agent_toolset_20260401 plus the github and handoff\nmcp_toolsets, each with permission_policy always_allow. Rendering #69 through the\nreal loader confirms the credential-broker agent would carry GitHub write at\nalways_allow -- in a file that declares services.github: \"none\". services does\nnot gate it; the schema calls it \"informational ... not sent to the API\".\n\nPinning \"tools\": [] and \"mcp_servers\": [] overrides it, because load_manifest\nmerges child over base per key (merged[k] = v) rather than concatenating, so an\nexplicit empty array replaces _base''s. Verified after: no tools, no mcp_servers,\nsystem prompt and model intact. Latent today (a2a.enabled: false) but a\ncontradiction inside the file whose purpose is least privilege.\n\nPolicy preserved verbatim: release_tiers, audit, securitySchemes.oidc/.mtls and\nrecipientKey move into metadata. Two narrowings from #69 kept: a2a.extendedOnly\n(keeps a credential broker off the anonymous agent card) and services k8s/cloud\nnone.\n\nCloses #69","tree":{"sha":"0d6489561f8f72e2eae885021bed93572fb9b8f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/0d6489561f8f72e2eae885021bed93572fb9b8f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d6489561f8f72e2eae885021bed93572fb9b8f5\nparent b9956801c7e756a7a39d7ceff8e6e095601fbcd1\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787208273 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787208273 +0300\n\nfix(a2a): reshape the keys-broker role to the contract, without inheriting tools (#88)\n\nRebase of #69 onto master, reduced to the one file that is this repo''s to\nchange, plus a fix for a privilege inheritance the original introduced.\n\nFive of #69''s six files were hub-reconciled (governance_sync.py declares\nFRAMEWORK_DIRS = schema, roles/_base, sync, providers) and master already held\nNEWER copies, so merging them would have written stale content the next sync\nreverts. Only agent-templates/roles/<role>/role.json is repo-owned.\n\nThe breakage is real: master''s role.json fails its own schema with 3 errors\n(''role'' required and missing; six unexpected top-level keys; two unexpected keys\nunder a2a) and renders an EMPTY system prompt, so validate.py''s\n`assert payload[\"system\"]` fails and the card projection has no description. The\nreshaped file validates with 0 errors and renders 2434 characters.\n\nTHE ADDED FIX. #69 introduced `extends: \"_base\"` while declaring no tools of its\nown. _base supplies agent_toolset_20260401 plus the github and handoff\nmcp_toolsets, each with permission_policy always_allow. Rendering #69 through the\nreal loader confirms the credential-broker agent would carry GitHub write at\nalways_allow -- in a file that declares services.github: \"none\". services does\nnot gate it; the schema calls it \"informational ... not sent to the API\".\n\nPinning \"tools\": [] and \"mcp_servers\": [] overrides it, because load_manifest\nmerges child over base per key (merged[k] = v) rather than concatenating, so an\nexplicit empty array replaces _base''s. Verified after: no tools, no mcp_servers,\nsystem prompt and model intact. Latent today (a2a.enabled: false) but a\ncontradiction inside the file whose purpose is least privilege.\n\nPolicy preserved verbatim: release_tiers, audit, securitySchemes.oidc/.mtls and\nrecipientKey move into metadata. Two narrowings from #69 kept: a2a.extendedOnly\n(keeps a credential broker off the anonymous agent card) and services k8s/cloud\nnone.\n\nCloses #69","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhqJRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXtUQAAyitjaAjM8mwHBYIz5EyU5q\nPSVLSmN4bQigeDg1l4C22vNcRRyquwwCgf+F7hOSxGMeqjiMzcJdVhB9gjLRL09O\njuT6bF9IgaT/Aec2zAZGTel8cZ37FuwkaHkD48g1NE4XvZuvYVcztsfu1Fd1CS6l\nfz6bkLS2s1LZ7KTKtyVkiAWnY28XwzjOn17AqjLyjTEbcRT/i45+uvYwhWXlhPcD\nqZmcLcu3oDJRQz4EH5gPkXt6I54JcIX8iEF310yavFuu8mNSct7HcCpoQ7idFB9c\nVTPKUImQeJaMo1kjdEdftNytO57EWVF0qY8ocoFWqo5gmCtNvamQdVTWokreWlPB\necvfkOWiV7U7Za8KgrFyEwht0G4Gjt6FEdAkXYNGWvuZ4w5GfXH7ar7dPL3FUkV0\nPDRzRiXGl2oN8rmfR4wZOAQS7PTZWu7kF2/LT62qznHtlMhMF8Jmquzj1f1v+SST\newIEVYJV3669+0TfrlY0wf5q4jbpQ6UHei8XWgC1d/QX6XnxREIHxxJFBGIBqTyx\nH56spcDN/4C4fiCyLHFCLV09ph0uvZFoV9C2vyz27jRCkggSYP1ScJh+k1vBMw+l\nAvig5SRyxz/MLOKRB2doLqZD+HBSxopsO/gTd+b3wArbzdAUVBqaJ4RQY97OKgHc\nQq2MhVcEoua3xuSxf6/7\n=oagW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T06:44:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDYwM2M4ZjAxZjE3MTYyYmNlNjgyODUwZDJmNzgxZjcxY2FhMTMxODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/b9956801c7e756a7a39d7ceff8e6e095601fbcd1","sha":"b9956801c7e756a7a39d7ceff8e6e095601fbcd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b9956801c7e756a7a39d7ceff8e6e095601fbcd1"}],"sha":"603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/603c8f01f17162bce682850d2f781f71caa13183"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b9956801c7e756a7a39d7ceff8e6e095601fbcd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:32:34Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:32:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(governance): record the pre-standard API paths in an allowlist (#86)\n\nRecords the 36 contract paths and 19 caller paths that predate the /api/v{N}/\nstandard, so gate-api-version fails only what is NEW when it reaches this repo.\n\nVerified: both gate halves pass with this file, and a probe adding\n/api/brand-new-thing still FAILS -- nothing is excused beyond what is written.\n\nOrganised by what the entries actually are, because two are not debt:\n\n  Section 1 -- NOT this service''s surface. /api/generate is Ollama''s completion\n  endpoint (f\"{self.base_url}/api/generate\"); /api/docs is a docs link built for\n  a third-party SITE record (f\"{base_url}/api/docs\"). Listed only because the\n  gate cannot tell someone else''s base URL from ours. Changing either breaks the\n  integration rather than improving it.\n\n  Section 2 -- real debt, 36 routes whose root cause is five APIRouter prefixes\n  (sms, google, credentials, infrastructure, llm-scraper) plus /api/info on the\n  app. Grouped by owning router: fixing one prefix retires every route beneath.\n\n  Section 3 -- the same debt from the client, in TypeScript template form.\n\nTiming, corrected from the PR description: this repo pins baselineRef=v1, which\nresolves to FuzeSDLC''s v1.8.0 tag, and gate-api-version landed on FuzeSDLC main\nAFTER that tag. So the gate arrives when a new baseline is cut and the v1 alias\nmoves -- a fleet-wide rollout decision -- not on the next nightly reconciliation.\nSeeding ahead of that is still the right order; there is simply no deadline.","tree":{"sha":"b3194ac906aec6ab28e987acd7d92f6e3f8cad3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/b3194ac906aec6ab28e987acd7d92f6e3f8cad3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/b9956801c7e756a7a39d7ceff8e6e095601fbcd1","verification":{"payload":"tree b3194ac906aec6ab28e987acd7d92f6e3f8cad3f\nparent 2df3bba020e1c420a9abdb99737b9203d7df3ed0\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787207554 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787207554 +0300\n\nchore(governance): record the pre-standard API paths in an allowlist (#86)\n\nRecords the 36 contract paths and 19 caller paths that predate the /api/v{N}/\nstandard, so gate-api-version fails only what is NEW when it reaches this repo.\n\nVerified: both gate halves pass with this file, and a probe adding\n/api/brand-new-thing still FAILS -- nothing is excused beyond what is written.\n\nOrganised by what the entries actually are, because two are not debt:\n\n  Section 1 -- NOT this service''s surface. /api/generate is Ollama''s completion\n  endpoint (f\"{self.base_url}/api/generate\"); /api/docs is a docs link built for\n  a third-party SITE record (f\"{base_url}/api/docs\"). Listed only because the\n  gate cannot tell someone else''s base URL from ours. Changing either breaks the\n  integration rather than improving it.\n\n  Section 2 -- real debt, 36 routes whose root cause is five APIRouter prefixes\n  (sms, google, credentials, infrastructure, llm-scraper) plus /api/info on the\n  app. Grouped by owning router: fixing one prefix retires every route beneath.\n\n  Section 3 -- the same debt from the client, in TypeScript template form.\n\nTiming, corrected from the PR description: this repo pins baselineRef=v1, which\nresolves to FuzeSDLC''s v1.8.0 tag, and gate-api-version landed on FuzeSDLC main\nAFTER that tag. So the gate arrives when a new baseline is cut and the v1 alias\nmoves -- a fleet-wide rollout decision -- not on the next nightly reconciliation.\nSeeding ahead of that is still the right order; there is simply no deadline.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhp+CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmsQQAA17gyHxxiKmWUL56YgtwsUw\nuQiL5bzuNiRZy+VFlSfs03oViPb0u6uVfjqmR