ew_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/e10fd0ae60d5bd0fae628e960028810e5f1006d5","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGUxMGZkMGFlNjBkNWJkMGZhZTYyOGU5NjAwMjg4MTBlNWYxMDA2ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/293c87353d8da68648fc7b9da24b4ccd894793ab","sha":"293c87353d8da68648fc7b9da24b4ccd894793ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/293c87353d8da68648fc7b9da24b4ccd894793ab"}],"sha":"e10fd0ae60d5bd0fae628e960028810e5f1006d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/e10fd0ae60d5bd0fae628e960028810e5f1006d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/293c87353d8da68648fc7b9da24b4ccd894793ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:34:36Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:34:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(google): correct the Google integration paths, bodies and route order (#82)\n\nFollow-up to #81. Three client bugs and one backend bug:\n\n* getGoogleAccounts sent /accounts?identity_id=N; the route is /accounts/{identity_id}, a PATH parameter, so it 404''d. The failure was swallowed into {accounts: [], total: 0}, which renders as \"this identity has no Google accounts\".\n* signupWithIdentity POSTed to the literal /signup/identity (binding identity_id=\"identity\", failing int validation) and sent {identity_id, config} when the handler''s only body parameter is config.\n* testIdentityConversion called /test/identity/{id}; the route is /test/identity-conversion/{id}, and it takes no body.\n* None of the four sent the bearer token, and all these routes are behind get_current_user, so fixing paths alone would have traded 404 for 403.\n* /signup/manual was declared AFTER /signup/{identity_id}. Starlette matches in declaration order and the parameterised route also matches \"manual\", so it bound identity_id=\"manual\" and returned 422 — manual_signup was unreachable. The client had this one right the whole time.\n\nAdds legacyApiClient (same interceptors, bare origin) for the eight routers not yet under /api/v1, kept as a separate export so the un-versioned surface stays countable.\n\nAdds backend/tests/test_google_route_order.py — 10 tests covering declaration order, that manual_signup is reachable, the five route shapes the client depends on, and that the two guessed paths do NOT exist. Verified non-vacuous: reverting the route order turns both ordering tests red.\n\ncontracts/openapi.yaml regenerated; --check clean.","tree":{"sha":"cef18143c58cd975df2bfeeed21bdb004f79ffcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/cef18143c58cd975df2bfeeed21bdb004f79ffcf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/293c87353d8da68648fc7b9da24b4ccd894793ab","verification":{"payload":"tree cef18143c58cd975df2bfeeed21bdb004f79ffcf\nparent c5a9604671fc04c7d16741245e6dc5fa443f4527\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787171676 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787171676 +0300\n\nfix(google): correct the Google integration paths, bodies and route order (#82)\n\nFollow-up to #81. Three client bugs and one backend bug:\n\n* getGoogleAccounts sent /accounts?identity_id=N; the route is /accounts/{identity_id}, a PATH parameter, so it 404''d. The failure was swallowed into {accounts: [], total: 0}, which renders as \"this identity has no Google accounts\".\n* signupWithIdentity POSTed to the literal /signup/identity (binding identity_id=\"identity\", failing int validation) and sent {identity_id, config} when the handler''s only body parameter is config.\n* testIdentityConversion called /test/identity/{id}; the route is /test/identity-conversion/{id}, and it takes no body.\n* None of the four sent the bearer token, and all these routes are behind get_current_user, so fixing paths alone would have traded 404 for 403.\n* /signup/manual was declared AFTER /signup/{identity_id}. Starlette matches in declaration order and the parameterised route also matches \"manual\", so it bound identity_id=\"manual\" and returned 422 — manual_signup was unreachable. The client had this one right the whole time.\n\nAdds legacyApiClient (same interceptors, bare origin) for the eight routers not yet under /api/v1, kept as a separate export so the un-versioned surface stays countable.\n\nAdds backend/tests/test_google_route_order.py — 10 tests covering declaration order, that manual_signup is reachable, the five route shapes the client depends on, and that the two guessed paths do NOT exist. Verified non-vacuous: reverting the route order turns both ordering tests red.\n\ncontracts/openapi.yaml regenerated; --check clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhhNcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADSEQAImGgngRyvIecX7RTmeHmNq7\ncHbnafBvlKeS33n9ehmG6Sdm4o2viDc0Dd8nLxMZk/oV62sIuwNmv/aBmfmjK4fA\ngD3/Cfn+J5FpvNR2UHpXhIXzW7WMTxPFpF/Oiwrk5A7Wj