ys/commits/c5a9604671fc04c7d16741245e6dc5fa443f4527"}],"sha":"293c87353d8da68648fc7b9da24b4ccd894793ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/293c87353d8da68648fc7b9da24b4ccd894793ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/c5a9604671fc04c7d16741245e6dc5fa443f4527/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:54:19Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:54:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(registration): register.sh required jq, which the init image does not have (#83)\n\n* fix(registration): register.sh required jq, which the init image does not have\n\nThe registration init container runs on curlimages/curl:8.8.0. That image''s\nentire userland is three files: bin/busybox, bin/sh, usr/bin/curl. There is no\njq. register.sh opened with a `command -v jq || die` preflight and used jq at\neight further call sites, so the container died before it ever contacted the\nregistry and the pod CrashLoopBackOff''d.\n\nThe resulting pod state is identical to the state a rejected token produces,\nwhich is why this survived: the symptom people were reading as an auth problem\nwas, here, a missing binary.\n\nFuzeMarket is the one product whose registration works in production, and it has\nalways parsed with grep/sed for exactly this reason. This ports that technique in\nas four documented helpers -- json_flat, json_nonempty_object, json_str,\njson_nested_str -- and drops the jq preflight. The script''s own structure is\nunchanged: the PUT manifest refresh, the 409 concurrent-replica race handling,\nthe optional policy and billing steps, and the fail-closed exit all behave\nexactly as before.\n\nTwo details the helpers encode deliberately:\n\n  - Every extraction flattens newlines first. Manifests are pretty-printed, so a\n    key and its value are not on the same line.\n  - The value patterns allow whitespace after the colon. FuzeMarket shipped a\n    version requiring `\"status\":\"x\"`, so a response serialised as `\"status\": \"x\"`\n    parsed to empty and silently took the wrong branch.\n\nAdds registration/__tests__/, which is what would have caught this. It runs the\nreal script against a mock registry with PATH restricted to the image''s toolset,\nso a machine that happens to have jq installed cannot mask a reintroduced\ndependency. Four scenarios -- fresh, existing-inactive, existing-active,\nbad-token -- plus checks that the POST body round-trips as valid JSON and that no\njq invocation survives anywhere in the script.\n\nReverting register.sh to the jq version fails 5 of the 7 checks. Notably\nbad-token still passes against the broken script, which is the same confusion\ndescribed above showing up in the test suite: a fail-closed exit is the expected\nresult there either way.\n\nWired into CI as registration-test.yml, on the registration/** path.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a4a5f8a102899927e6e1e96e42f7d67e06f89778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/a4a5f8a102899927e6e1e96e42f7d67e06f89778"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/c5a9604671fc04c7d16741245e6dc5fa443f4527","verification":{"payload":"tree a4a5f8a102899927e6e1e96e42f7d67e06f89778\nparent aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787169259 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787169259 +0300\n\nfix(registration): register.sh required jq, which the init image does not have (#83)\n\n* fix(registration): register.sh required jq, which the init image does not have\n\nThe registration init container runs on curlimages/curl:8.8.0. That image''s\nentire userland is three files: bin/busybox, bin/sh, usr/bin/curl. There is no\njq. register.sh opened with a `command -v jq || die` preflight and used jq at\neight further call sites, so the container died before it ever contacted the\nregistry and the pod CrashLoopBackOff''d.\n\nThe resulting pod state is identical to the state a rejected token produces,\nwhich is why this survived: the symptom people were reading as an auth problem\nwas, here, a missing binary.\n\nFuzeMarket is the one product whose registration works in production, and it has\nalways parsed with grep/sed for exactly this reason. This ports that technique in\nas four documented helpers -- json_flat, json_nonempty_object, json_str,\njson_nested_str -- and drops the jq preflight. The script''s own structure is\nunchanged: the PUT manifest refresh, the 409 concurrent-replica race handling,\nthe optional policy and billing steps, and the fail-closed exit all behave\nexactly as before.\n\nTwo details the helpers encode deliberately:\n\n  - Every extraction flattens newlines first. Manifests are pretty-printed, so a\n    key and its value are not on the same line.\n  - The value patterns allow whitespace after the colon. FuzeMarket shipped a\n    version requiring `\"status\":\"x\"`, so a response serialised as `\"status\": \"x\"`\n    parsed to empty and silently took the wrong branch.\n\nAdds registration/__tests__/, which is what would have caught this. It runs the\nreal script against a mock registry with PATH restricted to the image''s toolset,\nso a machine that happens to have jq installed cannot mask a reintroduced\ndependency. Four scenarios -- fresh, existing-inactive, existing-active,\nbad-token -- plus checks that the POST body round-trips as valid JSON and that no\njq invocation survives anywhere in the script.\n\nReverting register.sh to the jq version fails 5 of the 7 checks. Notably\nbad-token still passes against the broken script, which is the same confusion\ndescribed above showing up in the test suite: a fail-closed exit is the expected\nresult there either way.\n\nWired into CI as registration-test.yml, on the registration/** path.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgnrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA72MQAIGpHVRewrhVNg8KLlU2rwpS\ntF2mSBhcn0g3e9uXyC4KIZ0YXUouT+KNih8IkzJe+k5RY4yNerCNDn4ISzXvlwog\nvjr5dD5vhkMFbLVjFWTcv5Ec/XEUXPW6VaL4hVggk0Fz809eCS7nkoJuHxpsYTeX\nCE/VquoZfRVwlNgcy6zWdHrmcvetVjp5ZerrNg3k5bjeHu+sI7B1rUy6OK8iHLmp\nsVmq8ITjjTYPXWmcxkiy1tw4NwuxbuaM50jY0u7rbPYOEe6sG26nOFrpspDtsNY/\nRMVSK5cmHzk/UcFVXhwZbm2a9D/5EFDfeBo9ZMcTewnn7yclv3zk8SyOTXmpdFiN\nZxCTQ2EoKEMUzz3EfurDEkxsJEyV51SENpnZAZy2ZCbV0G9Bxi5vRaeFp+NtF/Ja\nOmyw9dpVeIQt7KHDuJOeixQn5yYy8Zc9kX7MruBWRlIv1rWtNEdIFGwLCLuxw4gZ\n38DKn3bu4xIOrvzUdbHu+dqstQRjMwq5X/6EhqNc24pBRA9GRlrEkbnY0ARCQR8J\nGAWwY72UXCp5lGXDf814MP4hjew7gmcSJrH/69IFiVYqpHCpZGfZa8zmoymWTo7h\nADMZ2uRPXKJooSdgLFq0Cd15rkzz7kGheBsQwYh82CWJZUWhrkrsz0iE0fmuHN0x\nVk5I+hVf466QsFrThO0p\n=ACxZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/c5a9604671fc04c7d16741245e6dc5fa443f4527","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGM1YTk2MDQ2NzFmYzA0YzdkMTY3NDEyNDVlNmRjNWZhNDQzZjQ1Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51","sha":"aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51"}],"sha":"c5a9604671fc04c7d16741245e6dc5fa443f4527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/c5a9604671fc04c7d16741245e6dc5fa443f4527"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:53:46Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:53:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools (#84)\n\n* ci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools\n\nizzywdev/AITools held only two reusable workflows and a README, and is being deleted.\nBoth now live in the canonical (FuzeSDLC#122), so the caller stubs repoint:\n\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n\nThis is only possible now because AITools was PUBLIC and FuzeSDLC is PRIVATE: a\nprivate repo''s workflows are by default callable only from that same repo. The owner\nhas opened Settings -> Actions -> General -> Access (\"Accessible from repositories\nowned by the user\"), so these resolve.\n\nNO `runner:` INPUT HERE, deliberately. The reusable workflows now take one, because a\nreusable workflow''s job runs in the CALLER''s context and bills to the CALLER -- which\non a private repo with the Actions budget exhausted means it never starts at all. This\nrepo is PUBLIC, so its GitHub-hosted jobs run unmetered and the `ubuntu-latest` default\nis correct. Passing a value would be change for its own sake.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6b71f9eac5e06587422cf10ef72cfd4602c5637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/f6b71f9eac5e06587422cf10ef72cfd4602c5637"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51","verification":{"payload":"tree f6b71f9eac5e06587422cf10ef72cfd4602c5637\nparent 2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787169226 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787169226 +0300\n\nci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools (#84)\n\n* ci: call the reusable workflows from FuzeSDLC, not AITools\n\nizzywdev/AITools held only two reusable workflows and a README, and is being deleted.\nBoth now live in the canonical (FuzeSDLC#122), so the caller stubs repoint:\n\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-claude-ci-autofix.yml@main\n    izzywdev/AITools/.github/workflows/telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n      -> izzywdev/FuzeSDLC/.github/workflows/reusable-telegram-pr-merged.yml@main\n\nThis is only possible now because AITools was PUBLIC and FuzeSDLC is PRIVATE: a\nprivate repo''s workflows are by default callable only from that same repo. The owner\nhas opened Settings -> Actions -> General -> Access (\"Accessible from repositories\nowned by the user\"), so these resolve.\n\nNO `runner:` INPUT HERE, deliberately. The reusable workflows now take one, because a\nreusable workflow''s job runs in the CALLER''s context and bills to the CALLER -- which\non a private repo with the Actions budget exhausted means it never starts at all. This\nrepo is PUBLIC, so its GitHub-hosted jobs run unmetered and the `ubuntu-latest` default\nis correct. Passing a value would be change for its own sake.\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgnKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOIwQAKTFo30iAIgkcHQx/EqYil2D\naqr+GqC4wusysItxDDYHJ31P5tUvUAz6Wo6hGitMVV7xYiNmcUX/px991lgFyh41\nE4RiP5uAU2DnpoUhKkO5l12UKct+FKjTi0KB0JDl7F3Ld+ImU8syyhI0jdlzylwL\n7OwCFymASZ7JAeMYs1/cgZMs5tMAMQ/WjquiuRMAisLzdRBF2ICV3RWoToyCajPw\n/sxenL6hVSAGOVW7d2WnlRNjyWUR7ZATD5nC+HaSSIKSwivVCCyutTwjlVY5VZ5X\nXlf7UF8Pbl4uQ56I4M7BH26BnY4ZcFro/6JChPs3qXMRAOzfTJNKbaJmdYHirGMm\nVZWGVVTgX/EhfLQ/Oy93WYa7mMt+PTw6R9+9PChi1io7FMLFSgPu9BoUYpsQcopF\nINtxCyeNR+tUjLO20AH2saDe5641O7O73hE1X8S/RhXQxFUumzl/kOjMEI6lQcjo\nxuDWWBl+tM204oicwSan7LcKZFPJjZiHUIexlhbAlkh61zYkov+pZszJMXG8wSJR\n7hfuwidj3Ya9Jdp/hyqmOE10Yg2jooRL/NHReXat/jGUc/HpQk0bQ505eEb0onZZ\nH3Eyc6HaP24HNnazGW2cAWF3pPA3ZHruMjrAp7FkZH6mSEUKt9jteYDIhJ1GCHFL\nFZohD/P8DCnMtcbFbkac\n=dhyF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:53:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGFhMDBiMGY1NjFjNDljZTkxZTRlNDQ2YWE4ZDMwZTIxZDk1N2VjNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29","sha":"2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29"}],"sha":"aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/aa00b0f561c49ce91e4e446aa8d30e21d957ec51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:09:32Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:09:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): route API calls through one versioned client (#81)\n\nThree callers each resolved the API base differently and all three shipped broken:\n\n* Accounts.tsx fetched ''/api/accounts'' -- un-versioned (404) and relative, so under Module Federation it hit the shell''s origin rather than the API host. It is a routed page in MfeApp.tsx, i.e. it ships in the remote FuzeFront delivers.\n* googleApi.ts fetched `${baseUrl}/api/identities` -- also 404, then swallowed the failure and returned three hardcoded people (\"John Doe\", \"Jane Smith\", \"Bob Johnson\"). That is why nobody noticed: an identity vault displayed invented identities instead of an error, defeating GoogleIntegrationPage.loadIdentities, which already surfaces failures via notification.error.\n* authService.ts used the bare REACT_APP_API_URL as its axios baseURL. That env var carries the origin only, so in the Module Federation build it posted to <host>/auth/login, missing /api/v1 entirely -- login was broken there.\n\nOnly SitesDatabase.tsx got it right, appending /api/v1 itself.\n\nAdds src/services/apiClient.ts: one axios instance with baseURL `<origin>/api/v1`, carrying the bearer-token request interceptor and 401 handling that previously lived privately inside authService. Callers now pass resource-relative paths and never spell the prefix. The token matters as much as the path -- both endpoints are behind get_current_user, so a corrected path without auth would have traded 404 for 403.\n\nAdds src/services/__tests__/apiClient.test.ts: this shipped because nothing asserted the prefix.\n\nVerified: lint, type-check, build under CI=true, 12 tests across 2 suites.\n\nCloses #80","tree":{"sha":"ad0a36ed9491bed26b296bc86a182a540008bb9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/ad0a36ed9491bed26b296bc86a182a540008bb9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29","verification":{"payload":"tree ad0a36ed9491bed26b296bc86a182a540008bb9c\nparent 885312c4f47e0567e207155b1513143ec2ca16cf\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787159372 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787159372 +0300\n\nfix(frontend): route API calls through one versioned client (#81)\n\nThree callers each resolved the API base differently and all three shipped broken:\n\n* Accounts.tsx fetched ''/api/accounts'' -- un-versioned (404) and relative, so under Module Federation it hit the shell''s origin rather than the API host. It is a routed page in MfeApp.tsx, i.e. it ships in the remote FuzeFront delivers.\n* googleApi.ts fetched `${baseUrl}/api/identities` -- also 404, then swallowed the failure and returned three hardcoded people (\"John Doe\", \"Jane Smith\", \"Bob Johnson\"). That is why nobody noticed: an identity vault displayed invented identities instead of an error, defeating GoogleIntegrationPage.loadIdentities, which already surfaces failures via notification.error.\n* authService.ts used the bare REACT_APP_API_URL as its axios baseURL. That env var carries the origin only, so in the Module Federation build it posted to <host>/auth/login, missing /api/v1 entirely -- login was broken there.\n\nOnly SitesDatabase.tsx got it right, appending /api/v1 itself.\n\nAdds src/services/apiClient.ts: one axios instance with baseURL `<origin>/api/v1`, carrying the bearer-token request interceptor and 401 handling that previously lived privately inside authService. Callers now pass resource-relative paths and never spell the prefix. The token matters as much as the path -- both endpoints are behind get_current_user, so a corrected path without auth would have traded 404 for 403.\n\nAdds src/services/__tests__/apiClient.test.ts: this shipped because nothing asserted the prefix.\n\nVerified: lint, type-check, build under CI=true, 12 tests across 2 suites.\n\nCloses #80","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqheNMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4hIQAGZ+1kSa8RsTIPYgAPf2rMip\nsnSAYQHvd73DTD0RMqnyDseiu0N7OVnUuTVtswEBqTNW4agepjHq5NanvkyMhIvA\njN6RkPppNJbg6cvyqpQH7XLQJfio9UScCpdcTaEk8NjFVn44Wqs4Xq7EEh2uAL93\ntzNqeJS4uTBLDe1GMIZqKQXKKRVIkAtUfCrgyXUHf0PtPjGmQK9rz+sUkACU25WU\nytTQu2Jb3Gi7Fp1+KQu3Uhra6oMMhhK1Txu4MQia7k+WtAYbEXPaqs2nG5Y95l5I\n+0E1piuXAJIt+pXMJeGBtu+AQVYP0gWnKnm1300QAQZAiShrqWR+op1PCMl9PxSc\nx0jCRPs0ERVDAFOdei1BiE2CO8nfbagb6p5eayXdCKswGGwuM+jEIRmAexUGqxJU\niL8vmZw4RwsO5CSkpr8u8ohP60EMfKzZz+EfjtiTYA2j1dzMseBT5BHUNOhq9TeM\n+jCZYA8T74IOIVgNa7qymkdkL5NxyxWZ3nKmiTB9aswp6VH9OIVZRkys5n1L5dZ2\n0R7gpOVqxqZeYLmFpTLZ0jhOrD0EekotjzNU4OmgbFNFWe0R2LY15vh3/DrVWc86\nwjX+zwroxKZgTb6aYHGEozK1Fv1akAjGVzjLxOfFFgSdMOgCFfhR/rVALZr5PRqE\nUD7cTqFSvoWCK2YmhsqJ\n=BaHK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T17:09:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDI1NjlmMWU1NGRmYmQwYjdkYzVhMmRhMzYyYjU1NDhhZTU1OTlhMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/885312c4f47e0567e207155b1513143ec2ca16cf","sha":"885312c4f47e0567e207155b1513143ec2ca16cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/885312c4f47e0567e207155b1513143ec2ca16cf"}],"sha":"2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/2569f1e54dfbd0b7dc5a2da362b5548ae5599a29"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/885312c4f47e0567e207155b1513143ec2ca16cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:56:02Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:56:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(helm): actually register this app with the FuzeFront portal (#76)\n\nAdds the registration init container the portal onboarding depends on: the\nmanifest/policy payloads, a registration ConfigMap mounted 0755, and an\nunconditional init container on the frontend Deployment.\n\nRegistration is a pod-startup precondition, not an optional extra — if it cannot\nregister, the pod must CrashLoopBackOff rather than come up invisible to the portal.\nFuzeKeys was one of two products with no init container at all, which is why it\nnever appeared however healthy its pods looked.","tree":{"sha":"4bb7c222d8113988571b27b51ee557d8a6bd9329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/4bb7c222d8113988571b27b51ee557d8a6bd9329"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/885312c4f47e0567e207155b1513143ec2ca16cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 4bb7c222d8113988571b27b51ee557d8a6bd9329\nparent 9491636ec3bff6301e421d9bc2719571894a828d\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787158562 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787158562 +0300\n\nfix(helm): actually register this app with the FuzeFront portal (#76)\n\nAdds the registration init container the portal onboarding depends on: the\nmanifest/policy payloads, a registration ConfigMap mounted 0755, and an\nunconditional init container on the frontend Deployment.\n\nRegistration is a pod-startup precondition, not an optional extra — if it cannot\nregister, the pod must CrashLoopBackOff rather than come up invisible to the portal.\nFuzeKeys was one of two products with no init container at all, which is why it\nnever appeared however healthy its pods looked.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqheAiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ9YQAD6fW0bWNwSkCu2ztIubRSnt\nSsJbmkztHrH+M5yoQ70vXpkaqOFF5Wt7JjREsFYPtsHB3yq9QPnjsqh+n5aGkm1z\nqhRa4ts/tu6bNS+C3trCgCG4X+zA7z2HI/e56q/sskCFuRq4xZdwB5lZ3txs8m2o\nyvb8qI9uYab9W1u1+ND+KLZxOPYp7RqLS+EPA1T9uKmbU4EDsO14i0HuwB9zT2fW\nO4h0V/C0Q2B+UNNU/gBWoOGKqdWzZ3GAu1ie7n9x+Yb4QdJLrPd8meHr2lKu0jWg\