eKeys/commits/885312c4f47e0567e207155b1513143ec2ca16cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/9491636ec3bff6301e421d9bc2719571894a828d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:41:20Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:41:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(identity): adopt the entity-identifier standard (namespace ''keys'') (#77)\n\n* feat(identity): adopt the entity-identifier standard (namespace ''keys'')\n\nDeclares this repo''s identity namespace and takes the dependency on the identity\npackage, satisfying the two ABSENCE checks in gate_identifier.py:\n\n  --namespace  wants `identity.namespace` DECLARED in .fuze/manifest.json\n  --adoption   wants a real dependency on the identity package\n\nWhy this is its own PR: --adoption currently fails in EVERY product repo, so it\nred-lights every rollout PR regardless of what that PR changes. gate_identifier\nruns four times in CI (contracts, --registry-parity, --namespace, --adoption) and\nthe rollout PRs only ever fixed the first. Landing adoption on the default branch\nclears the fourth for every PR that follows, because checks run against the\nmerge result.\n\nThe namespace is DECLARED, never derived from the directory name — a repo rename\nwould otherwise silently orphan every id already issued, surfacing much later as\nunresolvable references with no obvious cause. Value follows FuzeFront''s own\nmanifest, which declares \"front\": the de-prefixed product name. Reserved spine\nprefixes (usr/org/prt/app, billing, messaging) stay owned by FuzeFront; this\nproduct''s own types namespace as keys_<type>.\n\nDependency landed in `backend/package.json`.\n\nVerified before committing, against the real gate rather than by inspection:\n  gate_identifier.py . --adoption   -> OK  (was: \"declares no dependency on an\n                                            identity package\")\n  gate_identifier.py . --namespace  -> OK\nBoth files still parse as JSON, and the diff is additions only — no reformatting.\nA json.dump round-trip would have rewritten the whole manifest (inline arrays\nexpanded to multi-line) and buried a 9-line change in a 200-line reflow, so these\nare text insertions.\n\nKNOWN GAP, deliberately not papered over: @izzywdev/fuzefront-identity@1.0.0 is\npublished and installable, but the PYTHON half is not. identity-py-publish.yml on\nFuzeFront has never run — it fires on identity-py-v* tags and no such tag exists —\nso `fuzefront-identity` cannot be pip-installed today. Repos whose entity work is\nPython-side therefore adopt via their Node manifest here; wiring the Python\nruntime is a follow-up once that wheel is released.\n\n* fix(identity): sync package-lock for the identity dependency\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: c0b8227c-5cc8-4947-9873-b651218ff6f2\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: fuzeone-bot <fuzeone-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"314e1e5c1a237eb5fa63d8d9f5bd4b28919c09d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/314e1e5c1a237eb5fa63d8d9f5bd4b28919c09d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/9491636ec3bff6301e421d9bc2719571894a828d","verification":{"payload":"tree 314e1e5c1a237eb5fa63d8d9f5bd4b28919c09d4\nparent 43b8633238bcdadece4eeb355c09e56c7733bbbc\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787157680 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787157680 +0300\n\nfeat(identity): adopt the entity-identifier standard (namespace ''keys'') (#77)\n\n* feat(identity): adopt the entity-identifier standard (namespace ''keys'')\n\nDeclares this repo''s identity namespace and takes the dependency on the identity\npackage, satisfying the two ABSENCE checks in gate_identifier.py:\n\n  --namespace  wants `identity.namespace` DECLARED in .fuze/manifest.json\n  --adoption   wants a real dependency on the identity package\n\nWhy this is its own PR: --adoption currently fails in EVERY product repo, so it\nred-lights every rollout PR regardless of what that PR changes. gate_identifier\nruns four times in CI (contracts, --registry-parity, --namespace, --adoption) and\nthe rollout PRs only ever fixed the first. Landing adoption on the default branch\nclears the fourth for every PR that follows, because checks run against the\nmerge result.\n\nThe namespace is DECLARED, never derived from the directory name — a repo rename\nwould otherwise silently orphan every id already issued, surfacing much later as\nunresolvable references with no obvious cause. Value follows FuzeFront''s own\nmanifest, which declares \"front\": the de-prefixed product name. Reserved spine\nprefixes (usr/org/prt/app, billing, messaging) stay owned by FuzeFront; this\nproduct''s own types namespace as keys_<type>.\n\nDependency landed in `backend/package.json`.\n\nVerified before committing, against the real gate rather than by inspection:\n  gate_identifier.py . --adoption   -> OK  (was: \"declares no dependency on an\n                                            identity package\")\n  gate_identifier.py . --namespace  -> OK\nBoth files still parse as JSON, and the diff is additions only — no reformatting.\nA json.dump round-trip would have rewritten the whole manifest (inline arrays\nexpanded to multi-line) and buried a 9-line change in a 200-line reflow, so these\nare text insertions.\n\nKNOWN GAP, deliberately not papered over: @izzywdev/fuzefront-identity@1.0.0 is\npublished and installable, but the PYTHON half is not. identity-py-publish.yml on\nFuzeFront has never run — it fires on identity-py-v* tags and no such tag exists —\nso `fuzefront-identity` cannot be pip-installed today. Repos whose entity work is\nPython-side therefore adopt via their Node manifest here; wiring the Python\nruntime is a follow-up once that wheel is released.\n\n* fix(identity): sync package-lock for the identity dependency\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: c0b8227c-5cc8-4947-9873-b651218ff6f2\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: fuzeone-bot <fuzeone-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhdywCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA7kQAGN/cmLKoQ+dxN4vx32ksc3O\nnmjVY3hrPzpXQwM4vVmj8SPuKJYDU6SJsaDr02RaDXM385t3cRwLdVcEZ8pLHkNO\nkY0kBNed0/lSnDKXEvgEu4hAII4bSGNLiQI2ON9Lo9bi8LkEpRQjz2qE7snt+OiM\nRgW60d1XyJYbYM5+a6dWzR+AFAUDmiB98P+fKE7v3ZTKeoc88h/QVX7MVEnInE9+\nPtTl8x4e