m/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/ac69f35abbc0b721adf2fba32230dbe5b3427009/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:51:59Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:51:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): python-jose 3.5.0 — clears CVE-2024-33663 with no pyasn1 trade-off (#79)\n\n3.3.0 carried CVE-2024-33663 (CRITICAL, JWT algorithm confusion), CVE-2024-33664 and PYSEC-2025-185. 3.4.0 — the version the advisories name as fixed — caps pyasn1<0.5.0, which resolves to 0.4.8 and its own 6 advisories, so it looked like a forced trade-off. 3.5.0 relaxed that to pyasn1>=0.5.0, so the resolver takes a clean pyasn1 0.6.4.\n\nMeasured with pip-audit:\n  3.3.0 -> 5 jose advisories, pyasn1 0.6.4 clean   (6 total)\n  3.4.0 -> 0 jose advisories, pyasn1 0.4.8 with 6  (7 total)\n  3.5.0 -> 0 jose advisories, pyasn1 0.6.4 clean   (1 total)\n\nThe remaining ecdsa PYSEC-2026-1325 is transitive at every version with no fix released, and stays baselined.\n\nVerified past the resolver: create_access_token/jwt.decode round-trips under 3.5.0 and a forged alg=none token is rejected (JWSError). auth.py already passes an explicit algorithms=[ALGORITHM] at the decode site.\n\nAudit baseline drops 95 -> 92 python advisories; three removed, none added.\n\nCloses #75","tree":{"sha":"a60e849612b07c739fe5abf2edc4de9179c0ec60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/a60e849612b07c739fe5abf2edc4de9179c0ec60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/ac69f35abbc0b721adf2fba32230dbe5b3427009","verification":{"payload":"tree a60e849612b07c739fe5abf2edc4de9179c0ec60\nparent bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787154719 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787154719 +0300\n\nfix(security): python-jose 3.5.0 — clears CVE-2024-33663 with no pyasn1 trade-off (#79)\n\n3.3.0 carried CVE-2024-33663 (CRITICAL, JWT algorithm confusion), CVE-2024-33664 and PYSEC-2025-185. 3.4.0 — the version the advisories name as fixed — caps pyasn1<0.5.0, which resolves to 0.4.8 and its own 6 advisories, so it looked like a forced trade-off. 3.5.0 relaxed that to pyasn1>=0.5.0, so the resolver takes a clean pyasn1 0.6.4.\n\nMeasured with pip-audit:\n  3.3.0 -> 5 jose advisories, pyasn1 0.6.4 clean   (6 total)\n  3.4.0 -> 0 jose advisories, pyasn1 0.4.8 with 6  (7 total)\n  3.5.0 -> 0 jose advisories, pyasn1 0.6.4 clean   (1 total)\n\nThe remaining ecdsa PYSEC-2026-1325 is transitive at every version with no fix released, and stays baselined.\n\nVerified past the resolver: create_access_token/jwt.decode round-trips under 3.5.0 and a forged alg=none token is rejected (JWSError). auth.py already passes an explicit algorithms=[ALGORITHM] at the decode site.\n\nAudit baseline drops 95 -> 92 python advisories; three removed, none added.\n\nCloses #75","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhdEgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxrQQAFTDF2iHwHY7UZK8WrmzNX56\nx9TwjbeiKNm9zHKftPu3HdesIb6O7jldSKWVXheIeRta0oy24arInWstaaBeMJnf\nQP0ktD8ZXdUbCvELi16dsLixIpzLVLIC0Bqs5jxUD9of6WfjJ12QI9K+mmdxcREi\nFYFJDDvpDYt6XLdFtxKrN3M43nde9sgz0iMVDUHr/herL7l5pimrHOFhmsXIqXIi\nb/ViE1AChL6Xihht6bTrXRqP9uw6xMOS3r2bLdMf1lo1Jl5pAnTyGmdGKBNcnYrD\nHuD3VIh12Vjma9iJuy9LjrhPpeAa+bigE9egvviOqo0ZzLCzEv59roEJGmynPkdj\nAPci+Frp0d0ZOYrhLha0tQAJ9tZDxJrqqFHSMslxYy7I6mJaCeV/IIVwheOFM8ro\nXTkB9EqkZtB/hU5XhnFemQ9R5YEsyZndvplpsmQEjYHY3+v2LvCqAN65rd0IF6v1\nphvBkP/CuSVFZSU2Qx+xuzvjclb5prsH7YNunZ+5thfDMKocPl5WLkqlqSJj6yW2\nedeKMk38rBIiJusFZQk2Yc4sh97TnXFyhZR1UGd4PziurkrtKRtBV6bigqnpt/3e\n9n/lzlgs8YN7EfZa6gFQp9UIs9MqGiCL34GdUW/u2ilCEyU3NfF4giKtmykzlun9\n4pv95mk1ExFAUKiRU0J6\n=TTb0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T15:52:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/ac69f35abbc0b721adf2fba32230dbe5b3427009","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGFjNjlmMzVhYmJjMGI3MjFhZGYyZmJhMzIyMzBkYmU1YjM0MjcwMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd","sha":"bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd"}],"sha":"ac69f35abbc0b721adf2fba32230dbe5b3427009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/ac69f35abbc0b721adf2fba32230dbe5b3427009"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:45:23Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:45:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: pin outdated actions to SHAs and make Codecov upload honest (#72)\n\nactionlint reported 6 \"runner too old to run on GitHub Actions\" errors\nagainst ci.yml (setup-python@v4 x3, cache@v3, codecov-action@v3 x2).\n\nBump each to its current major and pin to a 40-char commit SHA with the\nversion as a trailing comment, matching the convention adopted in\nFuzeSDLC#98 — a mutable tag can be repointed by its owner, as the\ntrivy-action and kics-github-action compromises showed.\n\n  actions/setup-python  v4 -> v7.0.0\n  actions/cache         v3 -> v6.1.0\n  codecov/codecov-action v3 -> v7.0.0\n\nThe Codecov bump is not a mechanical version change:\n\n- v7 removed the singular `file:` input (it is `files:` now). Left as-is\n  the bump would have silently orphaned the coverage paths and fallen\n  back to auto-search, so both steps are updated to `files:`.\n\n- codecov-action v4+ does not support tokenless uploads for same-repo\n  runs; only PRs from forks of public repos are exempt. Both steps\n  previously omitted `fail_ci_if_error`, so a failed upload would have\n  gone green. Whether CODECOV_TOKEN is configured could not be verified\n  from this environment, so rather than leave a step that looks like it\n  uploads coverage but does not, the steps now pass the token, fail loudly\n  on upload error, and skip visibly when the secret is absent.\n\nVerified with actionlint 1.7.7 and 1.7.12: 6 errors before, 0 after,\nacross .github/workflows/*.yml. No ignore rules or continue-on-error.\n\nRebased onto master after #74 landed the lint-and-test repair; that PR\nleft every `uses:` line untouched, so this change applies cleanly and\nremains limited to action versions and the Codecov step inputs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a1516a7e0eba43a1ab60a2947e228f67a50f1d36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/a1516a7e0eba43a1ab60a2947e228f67a50f1d36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd","verification":{"payload":"tree a1516a7e0eba43a1ab60a2947e228f67a50f1d36\nparent 17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787154323 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787154323 +0300\n\nci: pin outdated actions to SHAs and make Codecov upload honest (#72)\n\nactionlint reported 6 \"runner too old to run on GitHub Actions\" errors\nagainst ci.yml (setup-python@v4 x3, cache@v3, codecov-action@v3 x2).\n\nBump each to its current major and pin to a 40-char commit SHA with the\nversion as a trailing comment, matching the convention adopted in\nFuzeSDLC#98 — a mutable tag can be repointed by its owner, as the\ntrivy-action and kics-github-action compromises showed.\n\n  actions/setup-python  v4 -> v7.0.0\n  actions/cache         v3 -> v6.1.0\n  codecov/codecov-action v3 -> v7.0.0\n\nThe Codecov bump is not a mechanical version change:\n\n- v7 removed the singular `file:` input (it is `files:` now). Left as-is\n  the bump would have silently orphaned the coverage paths and fallen\n  back to auto-search, so both steps are updated to `files:`.\n\n- codecov-action v4+ does not support tokenless uploads for same-repo\n  runs; only PRs from forks of public repos are exempt. Both steps\n  previously omitted `fail_ci_if_error`, so a failed upload would have\n  gone green. Whether CODECOV_TOKEN is configured could not be verified\n  from this environment, so rather than leave a step that looks like it\n  uploads coverage but does not, the steps now pass the token, fail loudly\n  on upload error, and skip visibly when the secret is absent.\n\nVerified with actionlint 1.7.7 and 1.7.12: 6 errors before, 0 after,\nacross .github/workflows/*.yml. No ignore rules or continue-on-error.\n\nRebased onto master after #74 landed the lint-and-test repair; that PR\nleft every `uses:` line untouched, so this change applies cleanly and\nremains limited to action versions and the Codecov step inputs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhc+TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtOAQAC9UN8GMi0HlJPD/+pA7sZhR\nfDb1voubHjZeW5/El6JTBwCbfnFGgmG0TcBxdy9cK156fZSGzPg/OWv+bvN1imfu\nRK5YsZjFWQnnCf+GtDPb8BL0bZKAEWh2NNofq7ismLjDDUZdi8iiMxKLYemAYHp+\nNAkZBcAAYoJvHZflsfflboB4GAZPGOHjezcEmW45VvPMxuh+m6ewG1gP823qFXOf\n47FkzAdHDfzyWAQPjVAe6r6r7zMItEcmFocS52m81GlUBqM27cCNhH3tv4g1qgiK\nWjI2tU98Jld0uKenW3PZ6Ko9gYl+4hmeRlKxsHOLFYyX9H1Zr6j//9v5TsfUacpE\n5o8Vp/rx6sxWTAaX6BJCGXyyH47CliUfzgcysHBCVta/a4SzC7yG/cUt7O4kSFMp\nwH89TvQXUMyphGKxE3KSPFmqVTyxACiltXV5HpgjnXgh7DKhvqqxJGuH8dqL7Nxy\nUlTjBsR40hC7AjEhrzcM3hDbLGJCo2F/TIQn6EkoAYUzehL8RCsdvKuUjaQEC0xt\nJEwNGvRwU0tr3SiaRawjbBMgCIHaOIhPhXa/yisG8Pa4KV8FCq3k74dTAvLZOcWf\nbSNTZoh47gQOSuEf5/D/3BOC7tinx0tH+JRHqF/9q/3+jpQRFG0wP/E/mZg0XA+d\nQwj3CMSLkZXGvMMhtW9L\n=PzY8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T15:45:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGJjNDdjZGEwNDZiYjM1NmE3MmZjNGJmYzczZTE0ZTBlYzM3ZDJjY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90","sha":"17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90"}],"sha":"bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/bc47cda046bb356a72fc4bfc73e14e0ec37d2ccd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:44:28Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:44:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): repair ci.yml — the workflow has never passed, and the gates it encodes were all broken (#74)\n\nci.yml had never been green in 122 runs. The first failing step was `black --check` (100 of 107 files unformatted), so nothing after it had ever executed.\n\nFixes the whole chain: Black/isort config and formatting, 4 real flake8 F821/F824 bugs, mypy (backend/app had no __init__.py; 346 legacy errors baselined by module), the missing frontend lint/type-check scripts, CRA build under CI=true, the missing @testing-library/dom peer, and 73 backend test failures.\n\nReal bugs found by the dead gates: password hashing was broken in production (passlib 1.7.4 + unpinned bcrypt 5.x), GET /api/v1/integrations/sites returned HTTP 500, account passwords were minted with the Mersenne Twister, site capabilities never resolved for the product''s own identifier, unknown sites returned 200, and requests.post had no timeout.\n\nsecurity-scan: safety replaced with pip-audit (safety 3.x requires an account and could never pass); npm audit fix cleared 30 vulns including all 3 critical; remaining pre-existing debt is baselined by scripts/dependency_audit.py, which fails on any new advisory.\npermit-io-scraper-test: repointed from scrapers/permit_io (never existed in git history) to the real integration package.\n\nFollow-ups: #73 (rewrite 53 quarantined tests), #75 (python-jose CVE trade-off).","tree":{"sha":"7d6deabb67631aecf3afbcc1d2f75d64109b715e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/7d6deabb67631aecf3afbcc1d2f75d64109b715e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d6deabb67631aecf3afbcc1d2f75d64109b715e\nparent 483aba23af7c8500eee87013e770e3b10e098509\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1787075068 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787075068 +0300\n\nfix(ci): repair ci.yml — the workflow has never passed, and the gates it encodes were all broken (#74)\n\nci.yml had never been green in 122 runs. The first failing step was `black --check` (100 of 107 files unformatted), so nothing after it had ever executed.\n\nFixes the whole chain: Black/isort config and formatting, 4 real flake8 F821/F824 bugs, mypy (backend/app had no __init__.py; 346 legacy errors baselined by module), the missing frontend lint/type-check scripts, CRA build under CI=true, the missing @testing-library/dom peer, and 73 backend test failures.\n\nReal bugs found by the dead gates: password hashing was broken in production (passlib 1.7.4 + unpinned bcrypt 5.x), GET /api/v1/integrations/sites returned HTTP 500, account passwords were minted with the Mersenne Twister, site capabilities never resolved for the product''s own identifier, unknown sites returned 200, and requests.post had no timeout.\n\nsecurity-scan: safety replaced with pip-audit (safety 3.x requires an account and could never pass); npm audit fix cleared 30 vulns including all 3 critical; remaining pre-existing debt is baselined by scripts/dependency_audit.py, which fails on any new advisory.\npermit-io-scraper-test: repointed from scrapers/permit_io (never existed in git history) to the real integration package.\n\nFollow-ups: #73 (rewrite 53 quarantined tests), #75 (python-jose CVE trade-off).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBA