com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/483aba23af7c8500eee87013e770e3b10e098509","sha":"483aba23af7c8500eee87013e770e3b10e098509","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/483aba23af7c8500eee87013e770e3b10e098509"}],"sha":"17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/17980dd86dd601b6afdc6b9a8d03729cc1415d90"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99821070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev","id":99821070,"login":"izzywdev","node_id":"U_kgDOBfMmDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izzywdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/483aba23af7c8500eee87013e770e3b10e098509/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:39:34Z","email":"99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Israel Weinberg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:39:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(deploy): correct the Argo ownership claim — FuzeKeys owns its manifests (#67)\n\ndeploy/argocd/README.md opened with \"FuzeInfra owns Argo `Application` and\n`AppProject` objects ... this directory therefore must not gain any NEW\nApplication manifest\", and described the manifests already present as leftovers\n\"from before the family moved Application ownership to FuzeInfra\", to be deleted\nby a later workstream.\n\nWrong on both counts. No such move happened, and these are not leftovers — they\nare the wiring. Acting on that instruction would have deleted FuzeKeys''s only\npath to prod, its AppProject and its sealed-secret reconciler.\n\nFuzeInfra''s docs/CONSUMER_ONBOARDING_SHARED_CLUSTER.md:\n\n  \"Boundary: the consumer owns its deploy/** (Helm/kustomize + Argo Applications\n   + sealed secrets). FuzeInfra owns the cluster, Argo, the tunnel, and the\n   shared datastores.\"\n\nThat boundary names sealed secrets explicitly, so deploy/argocd/sealed/ belongs\nhere for the same reason the Applications do. FuzeInfra''s\n.github/workflows/argocd-register.yml is built around the same contract: a \"Path\nin the consumer repo holding the Argo Application/AppProject manifests\", applied\nONCE, after which \"ArgoCD polls and self-syncs the consumer''s deploy/argocd\nmanifests\".\n\nThe same claim was propagated across the fleet in one session and used to DELETE\nApplications outright in FuzeService #32 and FuzeSales #44. Those are being\nreverted. FuzeKeys''s were not deleted, so this is documentation-only: `git\nstatus` shows one changed file and every manifest is byte-identical to master.\n\nWHAT THE FILE NOW SAYS INSTEAD. The real invariant is ONE Application per\nworkload; FuzeContact #33 and FuzeMarket #61 removed duplicates, not consumer\nownership. FuzeKeys''s manifests are not duplicates — the app-of-apps recurses\ninto applications/ and each child owns a different path. The README now lists\nthem, says they are live wiring, must not be deleted, and that no second\nApplication may be added for a path already listed.\n\nspec.project was \"FuzeInfra''s decision\"; it is `fuzekeys`, defined by\nproject.yaml in this same directory. FuzeInfra''s argocd/projects/ holds\nfuzeagent, fuzefront, fuzeinfra, fuzemarket, fuzepicker and fuzeplan — no\nfuzekeys — so this repo''s project is the only one that resolves.\n\nVerified: all four manifests still parse and all three Applications carry\n`project: fuzekeys`; deploy/helm/fuzekeys and deploy/argocd/sealed both exist.\nNo cluster operation performed.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c5a6dd19b8e50bcb8a15391881598ef79c84911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/9c5a6dd19b8e50bcb8a15391881598ef79c84911"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/483aba23af7c8500eee87013e770e3b10e098509","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c5a6dd19b8e50bcb8a15391881598ef79c84911\nparent 61f57e5818494af5a5006c5efbf095395d79f329\nauthor Israel Weinberg <99821070+izzywdev@users.noreply.github.com> 1786383574 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786383574 +0300\n\ndocs(deploy): correct the Argo ownership claim — FuzeKeys owns its manifests (#67)\n\ndeploy/argocd/README.md opened with \"FuzeInfra owns Argo `Application` and\n`AppProject` objects ... this directory therefore must not gain any NEW\nApplication manifest\", and described the manifests already present as leftovers\n\"from before the family moved Application ownership to FuzeInfra\", to be deleted\nby a later workstream.\n\nWrong on both counts. No such move happened, and these are not leftovers — they\nare the wiring. Acting on that instruction would have deleted FuzeKeys''s only\npath to prod, its AppProject and its sealed-secret reconciler.\n\nFuzeInfra''s docs/CONSUMER_ONBOARDING_SHARED_CLUSTER.md:\n\n  \"Boundary: the consumer owns its deploy/** (Helm/kustomize + Argo Applications\n   + sealed secrets). FuzeInfra owns the cluster, Argo, the tunnel, and the\n   shared datastores.\"\n\nThat boundary names sealed secrets explicitly, so deploy/argocd/sealed/ belongs\nhere for the same reason the Applications do. FuzeInfra''s\n.github/workflows/argocd-register.yml is built around the same contract: a \"Path\nin the consumer repo holding the Argo Application/AppProject manifests\", applied\nONCE, after which \"ArgoCD polls and self-syncs the consumer''s deploy/argocd\nmanifests\".\n\nThe same claim was propagated across the fleet in one session and used to DELETE\nApplications outright in FuzeService #32 and FuzeSales #44. Those are being\nreverted. FuzeKeys''s were not deleted, so this is documentation-only: `git\nstatus` shows one changed file and every manifest is byte-identical to master.\n\nWHAT THE FILE NOW SAYS INSTEAD. The real invariant is ONE Application per\nworkload; FuzeContact #33 and FuzeMarket #61 removed duplicates, not consumer\nownership. FuzeKeys''s manifests are not duplicates — the app-of-apps recurses\ninto applications/ and each child owns a different path. The README now lists\nthem, says they are live wiring, must not be deleted, and that no second\nApplication may be added for a path already listed.\n\nspec.project was \"FuzeInfra''s decision\"; it is `fuzekeys`, defined by\nproject.yaml in this same directory. FuzeInfra''s argocd/projects/ holds\nfuzeagent, fuzefront, fuzeinfra, fuzemarket, fuzepicker and fuzeplan — no\nfuzekeys — so this repo''s project is the only one that resolves.\n\nVerified: all four manifests still parse and all three Applications carry\n`project: fuzekeys`; deploy/helm/fuzekeys and deploy/argocd/sealed both exist.\nNo cluster operation performed.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqegzWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdHoQAEiH7oALDKkJ4dp1dawtMe97\n5oPtlSjVTLtIi7EOxEKJ2glImfFc6GZpaHiThdYy/GeOK+42S3mlmLP0K1FDBTiX\nKZOCtOihkGUnCpmAUqE5MRide/mX2ODBkWYeosSdE0XLswopENXdxZrgkxRGmopn\nnWQGPzq0UrEKt9bbb9Nh2ShfuYQrjLzEQjqJOmPGq5OtC6nzKMZ4IBDztmDB+YYi\nnEGvoFma94PNjOLT7BWdlqQSbli9soa6yb3BMfIvDGtLhgd0+Xdmg44o+tby+iob\nwT1c0jiEvl3dHHjFSKLy68h6J4l