:"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/43e070a54fc206d95b0ad5fd7a49f73297ad47b0","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDQzZTA3MGE1NGZjMjA2ZDk1YjBhZDVmZDdhNDlmNzMyOTdhZDQ3YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba","sha":"d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba"}],"sha":"43e070a54fc206d95b0ad5fd7a49f73297ad47b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/43e070a54fc206d95b0ad5fd7a49f73297ad47b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:20:27Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:20:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(registration): self-register FuzeKeys with the FuzeFront portal (#62)\n\n* feat(registration): self-register FuzeKeys with the FuzeFront portal\n\n- registration/manifest.json — identity + nav { section: platform, order: 10 }.\n  `platform` rather than a lifecycle stage: FuzeKeys is a capability the other apps\n  consume (providesTo lists 18 repos), not a step in plan -> build -> sell -> serve.\n\n  The MF contract is real and verified against frontend/vite.config.ts +\n  frontend/Dockerfile: scope=fuzeKeysApp, module=./FuzeKeysApp, remoteEntry at\n  https://keys.prod.fuzefront.com/apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js (base ''/apps/fuzekeys/''\n  + the keys.prod.fuzefront.com ingress; the Dockerfile comment says outright that\n  FuzeFront fetches remoteEntry.js from that path, and nginx.conf serves it).\n\n- registration/policy.json — derived from backend/app/models/: Identity, Account,\n  VaultAsset (identity_cards + api_credentials), Site, SignupScript, ApiKey.\n\n  READING A SECRET IS NOT A READ. VaultAsset splits `read` (list/inspect metadata) from\n  `reveal` (return the decrypted value), and `reveal` is granted to admin ONLY. That\n  lets operator create and rotate credentials without being able to read back an\n  existing one — the property that makes an operator role safe to hand out. Folding\n  reveal into ordinary `read` would have silently handed every viewer the vault.\n  SignupScript:run is likewise split from writes; it drives real account creation\n  against third-party sites.\n\n- .fuze/manifest.json — mcp scaffold (enabled:false) + mcp-maintainer in agents, which\n  now resolves after FuzeSDLC#66. The note carries the same constraint: a tool that\n  returns a decrypted secret must never be classified as a read.\n\nValidated: manifest passes the generated AppManifest schema; every permission resolves\nto a resource+action the same document declares; VaultAsset:reveal confirmed to be held\nby admin alone.\n\nNOT DONE, deliberately: the init container is not wired. deploy/helm/fuzekeys is a\nmulti-service chart (backend, frontend, vault, tokenizer, presidio, litellm) and exactly\none deployment must register. frontend is the natural owner since it serves the remote,\nbut confirming that is devops-engineer''s call, flagged not guessed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* fix(governance): supply the mcp-maintainer agent file + auto-merge permissions\n\nTwo red checks with the same root shape: something was DECLARED without the file\nthat backs it, and neither gate could self-heal.\n\ngovernance-sync: the manifest declares `mcp-maintainer`, and FuzeSDLC now carries\nthe canonical agent — but governance_sync.py only COPIES a file that already exists\nand has drifted. A wholly absent one is reported `missing` and hard-fails\n(governance_sync.py:84), so `--write` was never going to create it. Added\n.claude/agents/mcp-maintainer.md from the canonical, plus the mcp-maintain.yml\nworkflow where absent, so the declared surface actually has something behind it.\n\nauto-merge.yml: no permissions block, so the default read-only GITHUB_TOKEN made\n`gh pr merge --auto` fail with \"Resource not accessible by integration\" every run.\nFuzeSDLC#66 fixed the canonical template; this copy was stale. Workflow drift is\ndeliberately ADVISORY in governance-sync (the job cannot push workflow files), so\nnothing would ever have reconciled it on its own.\n\nVerified with governance_sync.py against the canonical: ok=True, missing=[].\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* feat(mobile): declare the mobile requirements contract\n\nNo repo in the family declared `mobile` at all, so `mobile-app-engineer` had nothing\nto read on merge and no gate could tell \"mobile is out of scope\" from \"nobody wrote\nit down\".\n\nUses the EXISTING canonical contract — FuzeSDLC\nagent-templates/schema/mobile-requirements.schema.json — which already sanctions a\n`mobile` block inside .fuze/manifest.json. No new schema and no new agent were\ninvented: mobile-app-engineer, mobile-packaging and mobile-conformance already exist.\n\nstrategy: pwa matches what FuzeFront actually ships — an installable PWA wrapped as a\nsigned Android TWA — rather than react-native/flutter, which nothing here uses.\ntargets omit ios until there is a signing identity for it.\n\nThe acceptance list is deliberately concrete (no horizontal scroll at 375, 44px tap\ntargets, Lighthouse >= 80, and the standalone URL rendering with no portal chrome),\nbecause an acceptance block of good intentions verifies nothing.\n\nValidated against the canonical schema; confirmed a missing `required`, an\nunknown strategy and an unknown target are all rejected.\n\nNOTE ON SEQUENCING: this declares mobile INTENT only. The `modes: [\"portal\",\n\"standalone\"]` + `routing.host` that a mobile build actually wraps cannot be added to\nregistration/manifest.json until FuzeFront#444 merges — AppManifest is\nadditionalProperties:false, so those keys would fail validation against the currently\npublished schema. Registration side follows once that lands.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* feat(registration): declare standalone surface via modes + routing.host\n\nThis repo declares a `mobile` block, and a mobile build can only wrap a\nURL that stands on its own — an app store has nothing to point at\notherwise. The manifest previously said only `mode: \"portal\"`, so there\nwas no standalone surface to wrap and no host to wrap it at. That made\nthe mobile contract unsatisfiable on its face.\n\nFuzeFront#444 added `modes` to AppManifest for exactly this: the scalar\n`mode` is single-valued and so cannot express a product that is genuinely\nboth — mounted in the host shell on the web, and separately reachable on\nits own host for the mobile wrapper. `modes` is the multi-valued form and\nwins where both are present.\n\n- `modes: [\"portal\", \"standalone\"]` — portal stays the default surface.\n  The scalar `mode` is kept unchanged (still REQUIRED, now deprecated)\n  and equals `modes[0]`, as the contract requires.\n- `routing.host` — the user-facing standalone host, `<slug>.fuzefront.com`.\n  Distinct from `*.prod.fuzefront.com`, which is the infra host serving\n  the portal `remoteEntry`. Portal integration is untouched.\n\nValidated against packages/onboarding-kit/manifest.schema.json at merged\nmaster (9d2b0af).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb43ab91dff7ce930909b82010758b96eeac2792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/cb43ab91dff7ce930909b82010758b96eeac2792"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba","verification":{"payload":"tree cb43ab91dff7ce930909b82010758b96eeac2792\nparent 72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785334827 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785334827 +0300\n\nfeat(registration): self-register FuzeKeys with the FuzeFront portal (#62)\n\n* feat(registration): self-register FuzeKeys with the FuzeFront portal\n\n- registration/manifest.json — identity + nav { section: platform, order: 10 }.\n  `platform` rather than a lifecycle stage: FuzeKeys is a capability the other apps\n  consume (providesTo lists 18 repos), not a step in plan -> build -> sell -> serve.\n\n  The MF contract is real and verified against frontend/vite.config.ts +\n  frontend/Dockerfile: scope=fuzeKeysApp, module=./FuzeKeysApp, remoteEntry at\n  https://keys.prod.fuzefront.com/apps/fuzekeys/remoteEntry.js (base ''/apps/fuzekeys/''\n  + the keys.prod.fuzefront.com ingress; the Dockerfile comment says outright that\n  FuzeFront fetches remoteEntry.js from that path, and nginx.conf serves it).\n\n- registration/policy.json — derived from backend/app/models/: Identity, Account,\n  VaultAsset (identity_cards + api_credentials), Site, SignupScript, ApiKey.\n\n  READING A SECRET IS NOT A READ. VaultAsset splits `read` (list/inspect metadata) from\n  `reveal` (return the decrypted value), and `reveal` is granted to admin ONLY. That\n  lets operator create and rotate credentials without being able to read back an\n  existing one — the property that makes an operator role safe to hand out. Folding\n  reveal into ordinary `read` would have silently handed every viewer the vault.\n  SignupScript:run is likewise split from writes; it drives real account creation\n  against third-party sites.\n\n- .fuze/manifest.json — mcp scaffold (enabled:false) + mcp-maintainer in agents, which\n  now resolves after FuzeSDLC#66. The note carries the same constraint: a tool that\n  returns a decrypted secret must never be classified as a read.\n\nValidated: manifest passes the generated AppManifest schema; every permission resolves\nto a resource+action the same document declares; VaultAsset:reveal confirmed to be held\nby admin alone.\n\nNOT DONE, deliberately: the init container is not wired. deploy/helm/fuzekeys is a\nmulti-service chart (backend, frontend, vault, tokenizer, presidio, litellm) and exactly\none deployment must register. frontend is the natural owner since it serves the remote,\nbut confirming that is devops-engineer''s call, flagged not guessed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* fix(governance): supply the mcp-maintainer agent file + auto-merge permissions\n\nTwo red checks with the same root shape: something was DECLARED without the file\nthat backs it, and neither gate could self-heal.\n\ngovernance-sync: the manifest declares `mcp-maintainer`, and FuzeSDLC now carries\nthe canonical agent — but governance_sync.py only COPIES a file that already exists\nand has drifted. A wholly absent one is reported `missing` and hard-fails\n(governance_sync.py:84), so `--write` was never going to create it. Added\n.claude/agents/mcp-maintainer.md from the canonical, plus the mcp-maintain.yml\nworkflow where absent, so the declared surface actually has something behind it.\n\nauto-merge.yml: no permissions block, so the default read-only GITHUB_TOKEN made\n`gh pr merge --auto` fail with \"Resource not accessible by integration\" every run.\nFuzeSDLC#66 fixed the canonical template; this copy was stale. Workflow drift is\ndeliberately ADVISORY in governance-sync (the job cannot push workflow files), so\nnothing would ever have reconciled it on its own.\n\nVerified with governance_sync.py against the canonical: ok=True, missing=[].\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* chore(governance): reconcile managed files to FuzeSDLC v1 [skip ci]\n\n* feat(mobile): declare the mobile requirements contract\n\nNo repo in the family declared `mobile` at all, so `mobile-app-engineer` had nothing\nto read on merge and no gate could tell \"mobile is out of scope\" from \"nobody wrote\nit down\".\n\nUses the EXISTING canonical contract — FuzeSDLC\nagent-templates/schema/mobile-requirements.schema.json — which already sanctions a\n`mobile` block inside .fuze/manifest.json. No new schema and no new agent were\ninvented: mobile-app-engineer, mobile-packaging and mobile-conformance already exist.\n\nstrategy: pwa matches what FuzeFront actually ships — an installable PWA wrapped as a\nsigned Android TWA — rather than react-native/flutter, which nothing here uses.\ntargets omit ios until there is a signing identity for it.\n\nThe acceptance list is deliberately concrete (no horizontal scroll at 375, 44px tap\ntargets, Lighthouse >= 80, and the standalone URL rendering with no portal chrome),\nbecause an acceptance block of good intentions verifies nothing.\n\nValidated against the canonical schema; confirmed a missing `required`, an\nunknown strategy and an unknown target are all rejected.\n\nNOTE ON SEQUENCING: this declares mobile INTENT only. The `modes: [\"portal\",\n\"standalone\"]` + `routing.host` that a mobile build actually wraps cannot be added to\nregistration/manifest.json until FuzeFront#444 merges — AppManifest is\nadditionalProperties:false, so those keys would fail validation against the currently\npublished schema. Registration side follows once that lands.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n* feat(registration): declare standalone surface via modes + routing.host\n\nThis repo declares a `mobile` block, and a mobile build can only wrap a\nURL that stands on its own — an app store has nothing to point at\notherwise. The manifest previously said only `mode: \"portal\"`, so there\nwas no standalone surface to wrap and no host to wrap it at. That made\nthe mobile contract unsatisfiable on its face.\n\nFuzeFront#444 added `modes` to AppManifest for exactly this: the scalar\n`mode` is single-valued and so cannot express a product that is genuinely\nboth — mounted in the host shell on the web, and separately reachable on\nits own host for the mobile wrapper. `modes` is the multi-valued form and\nwins where both are present.\n\n- `modes: [\"portal\", \"standalone\"]` — portal stays the default surface.\n  The scalar `mode` is kept unchanged (still REQUIRED, now deprecated)\n  and equals `modes[0]`, as the contract requires.\n- `routing.host` — the user-facing standalone host, `<slug>.fuzefront.com`.\n  Distinct from `*.prod.fuzefront.com`, which is the infra host serving\n  the portal `remoteEntry`. Portal integration is untouched.\n\nValidated against packages/onboarding-kit/manifest.schema.json at merged\nmaster (9d2b0af).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GaPa3JgrVNtWrGvqQEAEqv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <izzy.weinberg@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqagwrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATIAQAHWpZt4kD8KEpHDgPNinaA/M\nsA7kPknuheeJ0TaY381aEL8vUwbD20IqQ/2OdqeWeN5ohUM1cqB06cchsxj5Y8fV\nMSu7rrVxRb84pV+d/ejyE3hlnIEVUN6Om3tZHKhQCmm/7YfVmc0OSCBqhOgFumfc\nkkrKj4+F+1W2eDnTJdklZYPJLf9y9b7TjwgFAYKmq27xv8S5S0ZZFF6qtlVgDgeM\n4iT/AnjpaP+yVlK8oPzrc+fEIsDr6K5M+yB4Tis087CK/AZbHBarVIRJjfOGORn3\n0LH4CWHWIjSq25GNSaxKedYMxPpCELgdJGijqtUczug/+53s1bG/iVrIY+sz/hyY\neHrRD1RXD/TwhNZ/Q+qjrfoyHuKOI0vpvMZTBCc8Nu7nW0iniTUDortMfVpMknTA\n4fczSFs+5PuUVTHQtY/X+zEMaSBhO2RKAxvwxiNfC3suFqBTpf3OhLEWI85wMM/v\nZXP8265y1deFKL7rDYC/fd9vfkkYoZphB1aYX2nLiYmWX7/YdByzC4Vnd7KkjerH\nAX8JMv1UsUwfz+qQb8DymBJdQfa1efpqG8Uk66xo/FC+ze7LELj1Yk6G0vXXPuVH\njCS4Rej1rF1feV9rLTnqg1Hjh6DZFrXwlygP260HYnUGdDl5RHvhWexgS/dXXf+W\nKEPqARc3WwRbf2WNP7j3\n=HvOX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T14:20:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGQ3MzA3MzQ1YzFiOThjNWY3MDY3Njg0M2EzNjQ1MDkyOGQzY2U0YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0","sha":"72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0"}],"sha":"d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/d7307345c1b98c5f70676843a36450928d3ce4ba"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T11:04:36Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T11:04:36Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"message":"fix(nginx): use specific ACAO origin instead of wildcard — CF strips ACAO:*\n\nCloudflare strips Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * from responses (confirmed by\ncomparing with FuzeAgent which uses a specific origin and passes through CF).\nSwitch to ACAO: https://app.fuzefront.com + Vary: Origin so the browser\nreceives the CORS header and the federation dynamic import succeeds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3","tree":{"sha":"35c401fdebd83cd46db8c1748e068ebeae584712","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/35c401fdebd83cd46db8c1748e068ebeae584712"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 35c401fdebd83cd46db8c1748e068ebeae584712\nparent f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f\nauthor SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785323076 +0300\ncommitter SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785323076 +0300\n\nfix(nginx): use specific ACAO origin instead of wildcard — CF strips ACAO:*\n\nCloudflare strips Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * from responses (confirmed by\ncomparing with FuzeAgent which uses a specific origin and passes through CF).\nSwitch to ACAO: https://app.fuzefront.com + Vary: Origin so the browser\nreceives the CORS header and the federation dynamic import succeeds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3\n","reason":"no_user","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAggH15zrr03C0uhLXeinc5yB1pD3\neNdMgHLfG5v9/Yt+UAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQM3cG3HC9KWI8X+SyGADPLr1hKj9uJmNQD5g9XVN+dMx7hjYr4g4OyhvAalWNx6W6u\nfe+mSDGmsoBIUiMWoPbQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKDcyMjM4YTU0ZGNiN2ZiMTExMDMxMWU2ZTI1MDFlZTI4Y2E4YWQyYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f","sha":"f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f"}],"sha":"72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/72238a54dcb7fb1110311e6e2501ee28ca8ad2a0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T10:50:59Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T10:50:59Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"message":"fix(nginx): add s-maxage=0,no-store to MFE location to prevent CF caching\n\nCloudflare was caching remoteEntry.js with the old immutable headers and\nstripping CORS headers from its cached responses. s-maxage=0 explicitly\ninstructs Cloudflare not to store these assets in its CDN edge cache;\nno-store covers browser-level caching too. The ^~ prefix (from prev commit)\nstill ensures the regex long-cache location doesn''t override CORS headers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3","tree":{"sha":"d518992782e0a4c333b47510d68c6e5b8a8ef3e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/d518992782e0a4c333b47510d68c6e5b8a8ef3e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f","verification":{"payload":"tree d518992782e0a4c333b47510d68c6e5b8a8ef3e0\nparent b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea\nauthor SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785322259 +0300\ncommitter SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785322259 +0300\n\nfix(nginx): add s-maxage=0,no-store to MFE location to prevent CF caching\n\nCloudflare was caching remoteEntry.js with the old immutable headers and\nstripping CORS headers from its cached responses. s-maxage=0 explicitly\ninstructs Cloudflare not to store these assets in its CDN edge cache;\nno-store covers browser-level caching too. The ^~ prefix (from prev commit)\nstill ensures the regex long-cache location doesn''t override CORS headers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3\n","reason":"no_user","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAggH15zrr03C0uhLXeinc5yB1pD3\neNdMgHLfG5v9/Yt+UAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAkgDcQDLhe+//EJ27h6Smbiu+WJneMR/5efW+z8G+Gbr5QSw8VYxKJiVCyCkbBum2\nXkraqR46pr9gHvr6+/lAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGYzN2RlNmY3YmM1Njc2YWZiOTBkNWJkYTBlNTVmYjgyNjZhY2EzNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea","sha":"b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea"}],"sha":"f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/f37de6f7bc5676afb90d5bda0e55fb8266aca36f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T10:22:39Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T10:22:39Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"message":"fix(nginx): use ^~ prefix on /apps/fuzekeys/ to block regex location override\n\nThe ~* \\.js$ long-cache location was taking priority over the /apps/fuzekeys/\nprefix location (regex > prefix in nginx matching order), stripping the CORS\nheaders from remoteEntry.js and the federation chunk imports. ^~ stops regex\nmatching for this prefix, so Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * is correctly applied\nto all MFE assets and dynamic imports succeed in the FuzeFront host.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3","tree":{"sha":"d9bc562db6f80fa4305677cf7ca9300b0bd087a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/d9bc562db6f80fa4305677cf7ca9300b0bd087a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea","verification":{"payload":"tree d9bc562db6f80fa4305677cf7ca9300b0bd087a2\nparent a4845835e67238d958317efc7e303dd2ae4175ef\nauthor SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785320559 +0300\ncommitter SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785320559 +0300\n\nfix(nginx): use ^~ prefix on /apps/fuzekeys/ to block regex location override\n\nThe ~* \\.js$ long-cache location was taking priority over the /apps/fuzekeys/\nprefix location (regex > prefix in nginx matching order), stripping the CORS\nheaders from remoteEntry.js and the federation chunk imports. ^~ stops regex\nmatching for this prefix, so Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * is correctly applied\nto all MFE assets and dynamic imports succeed in the FuzeFront host.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3\n","reason":"no_user","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAggH15zrr03C0uhLXeinc5yB1pD3\neNdMgHLfG5v9/Yt+UAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLPeh8NR2pyb22KYvnvIOgTCamKgbkaEJEupE9wMUrdQFHoQnoW3/PBupNFs9ez5bz\nT0U78wh+ZofcNhNT70gQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea","node_id":"C_kwDOO0IuAdoAKGI3ZjcyYjk1MzNjZWNlM2M4YWQyYWRiZTU5OWIwOWJiNTcwNTI2ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commit/a4845835e67238d958317efc7e303dd2ae4175ef","sha":"a4845835e67238d958317efc7e303dd2ae4175ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/a4845835e67238d958317efc7e303dd2ae4175ef"}],"sha":"b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/b7f72b9533cece3c8ad2adbe599b09bb570526ea"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/commits/a4845835e67238d958317efc7e303dd2ae4175ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T15:19:22Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T15:19:22Z","email":"signmeup@example.com","name":"SignMeUp Developer"},"message":"feat(frontend): migrate FuzeKeys from iframe to Module Federation remote\n\n- vite.config.ts: add `define` shim so existing process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL\n  refs work in the Vite MFE build without changing source files; VITE_API_URL\n  build-arg overrides, defaults to prod API URL\n- Dockerfile (MFE stage): accept VITE_API_URL ARG so CI can override per-env\n- tsconfig.json: add node types + include vite.config.ts to resolve TS errors\n- Chart.yaml: bump chart 0.1.6 → 0.1.7, appVersion 0.1.5 → 0.1.6 to trigger\n  new image build with the Vite MFE assets (remoteEntry.js at /apps/fuzekeys/)\n\nDB (applied directly):\n  fuzefront_platform.apps WHERE slug=''fuzekeys''\n    integration_type: iframe → module-federation\n    remote_url: https://keys.prod.fuzefront.com/apps/fuzekeys\n    scope: fuzeKeysApp  module: ./FuzeKeysApp\n    manifest.integration: type/remoteEntry/scope/module updated\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3","tree":{"sha":"15199aceefa4d9e659a6e098c19c241a17d6ad8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/trees/15199aceefa4d9e659a6e098c19c241a17d6ad8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/izzywdev/FuzeKeys/git/commits/a4845835e67238d958317efc7e303dd2ae4175ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 15199aceefa4d9e659a6e098c19c241a17d6ad8a\nparent 65f49568136a7f9d067448c8ad2bf20c8171fc63\nauthor SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785251962 +0300\ncommitter SignMeUp Developer <signmeup@example.com> 1785251962 +0300\n\nfeat(frontend): migrate FuzeKeys from iframe to Module Federation remote\n\n- vite.config.ts: add `define` shim so existing process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL\n  refs work in the Vite MFE build without changing source files; VITE_API_URL\n  build-arg overrides, defaults to prod API URL\n- Dockerfile (MFE stage): accept VITE_API_URL ARG so CI can override per-env\n- tsconfig.json: add node types + include vite.config.ts to resolve TS errors\n- Chart.yaml: bump chart 0.1.6 → 0.1.7, appVersion 0.1.5 → 0.1.6 to trigger\n  new image build with the Vite MFE assets (remoteEntry.js at /apps/fuzekeys/)\n\nDB (applied directly):\n  fuzefront_platform.apps WHERE slug=''fuzekeys''\n    integration_type: iframe → module-federation\n    remote_url: https://keys.prod.fuzefront.com/apps/fuzekeys\n    scope: fuzeKeysApp  module: ./FuzeKeysApp\n    manifest.integration: type/remoteEntry/scope/module updated\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session-Id: be266aef-d8b5-4446-9ba7-3d14905610a3\n","reason":"no_user","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAggH15zrr03C0uhLXeinc5yB1pD3\neNdMgHLfG5v9/Yt+UAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQI5PYEaVDBbdQkLfrQRkNdIc1brh74iKjvtS1ugivhjHAFRv1t7bJNRaLYD3UdBnTE\nw2V2io4bX/fh3Mr79D6ww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","v