ttps://api.github.com/users/kroky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commits/438362cb945cfbd6b2425f6c516287453cee0775/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:00:18Z","email":"kroky6@gmail.com","name":"Victor Emanouilov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:00:18Z","email":"kroky6@gmail.com","name":"Victor Emanouilov"},"message":"[NEW][UX] Report engine: add unified aggregations across Elastic, Manticore and MySQL\n---\n* [NEW][UX] Report engine: add unified aggregations across Elastic, Manticore and MySQL\nAdd a backend-agnostic aggregation layer to PluginList and related search\nplugins, with wiki-syntax grouping/metrics, tiered execution, and chart/table\noutput templates.\n* Introduce Search\\Query\\Aggregation tree (Terms, Metric, Formula, Join) parsed\n  from {group}/{metric}/{having}/{join} blocks via WikiBuilder and orchestrated\n  by QueryFacade (tier selection, search enrichment, join resolution)\n* Execute aggregations natively on Elastic and Manticore where possible; fall\n  back to a MySQL temp-table tier (Compiler/Executor) for complex cases\n  (derived metrics, formulas, having, cardinality/stats, direct-mode MySQL)\n* Normalize results in Search\\ResultSet\\AggregationResult with per-engine\n  builders/readers (Search\\Elastic\\*, Search\\Manticore\\*) and attach them to\n  Search_ResultSet\n* Add OUTPUT modes for scalar aggregations, aggregate tables, and Chart.js\n  charts (templates + tiki-aggregations.js adapter glue); wire into list,\n  listexecute, customsearch, and chartjs plugins\n* Add integration tests shared across Elastic, Manticore, and MySQL backends\n\nSee merge request tikiwiki/tiki!10266","tree":{"sha":"8e036c02e6856eb71f656627c8ae61f50b6d89e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/git/trees/8e036c02e6856eb71f656627c8ae61f50b6d89e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/git/commits/438362cb945cfbd6b2425f6c516287453cee0775","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2064350?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kroky","id":2064350,"login":"kroky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQzNTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commit/438362cb945cfbd6b2425f6c516287453cee0775","node_id":"C_kwDOO1SSh9oAKDQzODM2MmNiOTQ1Y2ZiZDZiMjQyNWY2YzUxNjI4NzQ1M2NlZTA3NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commit/49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b","sha":"49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commits/49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b"}],"sha":"438362cb945cfbd6b2425f6c516287453cee0775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commits/438362cb945cfbd6b2425f6c516287453cee0775"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49983752?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Moise-Nturubika","id":49983752,"login":"Moise-Nturubika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTgzNzUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commits/49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:46:50Z","email":"nturumoussa@gmail.com","name":"Moïse Nturubika"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:46:50Z","email":"kroky6@gmail.com","name":"Victor Emanouilov"},"message":"[ENH] SUBLIST: Enable pagination for SUBLIST results in Smarty templates\n---\n* [ENH] SUBLIST: Simplify per-parent pagination slice\n\nDrop the closure that built a small array just to loop-reassign it\ninto $this->data. Slice and set the count/offset/max fields directly\ninstead, per review feedback.\n\n* [ENH] SUBLIST: Paginate per parent row instead of on the shared query\n\nAddress review: a sublist search is one query shared (via OR) across\nevery matched parent row, so applying max/offset to that query would\npaginate the shared pool, not any one parent''s own children - broken\nas soon as more than one parent row is involved.\n\nMove pagination into applySublistPagination(), run right after\nformatResult(). By then, reverseMapping has already sorted each\nfetched record to its true parent (exact per-entry equality check,\nuntouched by this change), so slicing each parent''s own resolved list\nby offset/max pages correctly regardless of how many parents are in\nplay. The search itself goes back to fetching everything unconditionally,\nexactly as before this feature existed.\n\n* [ENH] SUBLIST: Enable pagination for SUBLIST results in Smarty templates\n\nSee merge request tikiwiki/tiki!10901","tree":{"sha":"d316df26ebac165ae56ceb611943e4d8afbaf4c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/git/trees/d316df26ebac165ae56ceb611943e4d8afbaf4c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/git/commits/49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2064350?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kroky","id":2064350,"login":"kroky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQzNTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kroky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commit/49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b","node_id":"C_kwDOO1SSh9oAKDQ5ZmUxZTUyZmE4NGRlMjg1MmM1N2U1NWU0YjdhMjk0ZjI3OTUxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commit/f9849f321fd7572e69549ea5d478120dfec774fe","sha":"f9849f321fd7572e69549ea5d478120dfec774fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commits/f9849f321fd7572e69549ea5d478120dfec774fe"}],"sha":"49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commits/49fe1e52fa84de2852c57e55e4b7a294f279515b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49983752?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Moise-Nturubika","id":49983752,"login":"Moise-Nturubika","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTgzNzUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moise-Nturubika","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/commits/f9849f321fd7572e69549ea5d478120dfec774fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:17:38Z","email":"nturumoussa@gmail.com","name":"Moïse Nturubika"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:17:38Z","email":"benoitg@coeus.ca","name":"Benoit Grégoire"},"message":"[MOD] Upgrade jQuery to 4.0.0\n---\n* [FIX] Adapt to jQuery 4''s changed .attr() boolean-value handling\n\n* [MOD] Upgrade jQuery to 4.0.0\n\nBumps jquery 3.7.1 -> 4.0.0, jquery-migrate 3.6.0 -> 4.0.2 (not\n4.0.0/4.0.1, both pulled from npm for a publishing bug), and\njquery-validation 1.20.0 -> 1.22.1 (the first release to declare\njQuery 4 support in its peerDependencies). jquery-ui, jquery-form,\njquery-treetable and jquery-zoom needed no version change -- already\ncompatible with jQuery 4 as currently pinned.\n\ntimeago@1.6.7 (unmaintained since 2019, so its range predates jQuery\n4''s existence) declares \"jquery\": \">=1.5.0 <4.0\", which otherwise\nkeeps jQuery 3.7.1 hoisted at the top level even after the bump.\nAdded an override for it, scoped to timeago rather than applied\nglobally: a global \"jquery\" override makes npm nest jquery-migrate\nand jquery-validation under src/js/common-externals/node_modules,\nwhich breaks the predictable node_modules paths the viteStaticCopy\ntargets rely on and trips the npm ls check in checkEnvironment.\nScoping it keeps every package hoisted at the root, so no build\nconfig change is needed. This does make jquery-migrate load-bearing\nat runtime rather than a dev aid: timeago and several bundled\nlibraries call $.trim/$.isFunction/$.proxy, which jQuery 4 removed\nand Migrate shims.\n\nGoogle''s CDN hosts no jQuery 4.x at all (its newest jQuery is 3.7.1),\nso javascript_cdn=google now falls through to the local copies rather\nthan 404ing on jquery.min.js and leaving those pages with no jQuery\nat all. That block already loaded jquery-migrate locally for exactly\nthe same reason. ''Google'' stays selectable but no longer serves\njQuery; removing the option is a separate maintainer decision.\ncode.jquery.com does carry 4.0.0, so javascript_cdn=jquery is\nunaffected (verified against both CDNs).\n\nlib/headerlib.php''s $jquery_version/$jquerymigrate_version updated to\nmatch.\n\nPart of the jQuery 4.x upgrade (Tiki tracker: move to jQuery 4.x).\n\nSee merge request tikiwiki/tiki!11047","tree":{"sha":"46771dc9ae2c0d10db7cd804ad607fd2938ce125","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/git/trees/46771dc9ae2c0d10db7cd804ad607fd2938ce125"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Olivier-Kango/tiki/git/commits/f9849f321fd7572e69549ea5d478120dfec774fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"ve