: ENABLED\n\n* docs(plugin-new): describe local dev harnesses\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): use frontend dev app helper\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* test(plugin-new): sort mock package versions\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): use JSX frontend template\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): publish frontend federation assets\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): separate frontend entry facade\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): align frontend package metadata\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): add default frontend page icon\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): inherit sidebar icon color\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): use a MUI navigation icon\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): render upstream templates\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): type portable template helpers\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): satisfy lint checks\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): remove obsolete local templates\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): isolate portable template renderer\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* test(plugin-new): restore shared task coverage\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): simplify template helper type\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): limit supported templates\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): address review thread findings\n\n- remove duplicate entryPoint from snapshot file list and merge backend\n  spread entries (test-integrity thread)\n- validate --plugin-package against npm package name rules (input-validation\n  thread)\n- use path.relative() instead of file.slice() in portable template renderer\n  (edge-case thread)\n- reverse context spread so values.name wins over filename override in hbs\n  rendering (edge-case thread)\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): add --template and --module-id options\n\n- add --template <name> to select an upstream portable template by its\n  canonical name (frontend-plugin, backend-plugin, catalog-processor-module);\n  overrides --type when provided and skips the interactive type prompt\n- constrain accepted template names to supportedTemplateNames (the same set\n  as the --type aliases) so untested upstream templates are not silently\n  accepted\n- add --module-id <id> to override the module identifier for module-type\n  templates; defaults to the plugin name for non-interactive use\n- derive isModuleTemplate from the template role so module-id defaulting\n  works correctly whether the caller uses --type or --template\n- expand e2e tests: add shared buildAndExport helper, add plugin export step\n  to the frontend case, add an independent backend plugin test, and verify\n  dist-dynamic/package.json in both cases\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* test(plugin-new): add catalog-processor-module e2e case\n\nScaffold, install, typecheck, build, and export a catalog-processor-module\nproject. Also verify the exported dist-dynamic/package.json backstage\nmetadata: role=backend-plugin-module, pluginId=catalog, and\npluginPackage=@backstage/plugin-catalog-backend, which are the fields the\nRHDH installer uses to wire the module to its host plugin.\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): patch upstream frontend-plugin template for msw v2\n\nThe @backstage/cli-module-new 0.1.6 frontend-plugin template (Backstage\n1.54.6) generates tests that use the MSW v1 API. MSW v1''s setupServer()\nintercepts Node http/https modules and XHR but does NOT intercept native\nNode.js fetch (globalThis.fetch), which Backstage''s fetchApiRef uses via\n@backstage/frontend-test-utils. The generated TodoPage test therefore hangs\non findByText() on any Node version with native fetch.\n\nThe upstream fix (msw@^2 + http/HttpResponse API) shipped in\n@backstage/cli-module-new 0.1.7 (Backstage 1.55.0). Until RHDH targets\nthat release, three RHDH-owned overlay files patch the generated project:\n\n1. templates/plugin-new/frontend-plugin/src/components/TodoPage/\n   TodoPage.test.tsx.hbs — MSW v2 API (http/HttpResponse instead of\n   rest/res/ctx).\n\n2. templates/plugin-new/frontend-plugin/src/setupTests.ts — imports\n   TextEncoder, TextDecoder, BroadcastChannel, TransformStream,\n   WritableStream, and ReadableStream from Node builtins and assigns them to\n   global, mirroring what FixedJSDOMEnvironment does for Jest 30+.\n\n3. templates/plugin-new/frontend-plugin/package.json.hbs — adds\n   jest.testEnvironmentOptions.customExportConditions: [''node'',''node-addons'']\n   so Jest 29 resolves msw/node and @mswjs/interceptors subpath exports via\n   the ''node'' condition rather than the default browser condition.\n\nThe msw@^2 dev dependency override is injected by the RHDH 2.1\nfrontend-plugin role overlay in rhdhProfiles.ts, which runs after template\nrendering via adaptStandaloneProject.\n\nThe renderer gains an optional overlayDir parameter. When present, each\nupstream template file is checked against the overlay tree before rendering;\nfiles found in the overlay replace the upstream version. The RHDH_TEMPLATE_\nOVERLAYS_ROOT constant in command.ts is resolved three directories above this\nfile, which is the package root in both the TypeScript source tree and the\ncompiled dist/ output.\n\nEach overlay file contains a Handlebars comment (stripped at render time)\nexplaining which upstream version it patches and when it should be removed.\n\nIncludes two new renderer tests: overlay file wins when present; upstream\nfile used when overlay directory is absent.\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* docs(plugin-new): expand changelog, AGENTS.md, prompt, and e2e coverage\n\n- expand Unreleased changelog entry: separate Changed / Added / Fixed\n  sections covering upstream template reuse, --template, --module-id,\n  --plugin-package, and the MSW v2 overlay fix\n- add plugin new and overlay mechanism section to AGENTS.md: documents\n  supportedTemplateNames gate, the overlay directory convention, and\n  the audit step required when upgrading the cli-module-new version\n- update interactive type prompt to show both --type aliases and upstream\n  template names so callers know either form is accepted\n- add yarn test step to the e2e buildAndExport helper; all three generated\n  project types now pass their own test suite before being exported\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): address review thread findings\n\n- rename module-level constant rhdhReadmeSection -> RHDH_README_SECTION\n  to match SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE used by adjacent constants\n- add JSDoc comment to pluginPackage in CreatePluginOptions, consistent\n  with the template and moduleId fields above it\n- validate --module-id with assertPluginName before template rendering,\n  consistent with the validation applied to name and pluginPackage;\n  add a test case for the invalid module-id path\n- add CHANGELOG Changed entry documenting that default generated package\n  names no longer carry a type suffix (previously -backend, etc.) and\n  noting --plugin-package as the opt-out\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): address PatAKnight review feedback\n\n- generate .gitignore in adaptStandaloneProject covering dist, dist-types,\n  dist-dynamic, coverage, node_modules, *.local.yaml, and Yarn Berry\n  .yarn/ paths (upstream templates do not include one)\n\n- expand resolveTemplateName to handle two additional cases:\n  - conflict detection: if both --type and --template are supplied and\n    disagree after aliasing, throw an error naming both values\n  - upstream names via type: accept a full upstream template name\n    (e.g. ''frontend-plugin'') passed as --type, which is what the\n    interactive prompt stores when the user types the upstream name\n\n- add README overlays for all three supported template types, replacing\n  upstream README content that references a Backstage monorepo (installing\n  into packages/backend/src/index.ts, running yarn start from the root\n  directory) with RHDH standalone-project guidance focused on yarn start\n  for local iteration and rhdh-cli plugin export for packaging\n\n- add unit tests for the new resolveTemplateName paths: upstream name\n  accepted as --type, conflicting type+template rejected, agreeing\n  type+template accepted\n- add .gitignore content assertions to the parametrised creates-a-plugin\n  test\n- update all three README snapshots\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED","tree":{"sha":"083fd7d66ffb4f558e38db72c4e3f6ac26b88fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/trees/083fd7d66ffb4f558e38db72c4e3f6ac26b88fc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/commits/d71647e83e7a1211fdc5faf166ec1329821d803e","verification":{"payload":"tree 083fd7d66ffb4f558e38db72c4e3f6ac26b88fc4\nparent 63ca3e1d78dc484ee8e5ae3093c8ab24202a1480\nauthor Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com> 1789659778 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789659778 -0400\n\nrefactor(plugin-new): render upstream templates (#208)\n\n* feat(plugin-new): add local dev harnesses\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* docs(plugin-new): describe local dev harnesses\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): use frontend dev app helper\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* test(plugin-new): sort mock package versions\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): use JSX frontend template\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): publish frontend federation assets\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): separate frontend entry facade\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): align frontend package metadata\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): add default frontend page icon\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): inherit sidebar icon color\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): use a MUI navigation icon\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): render upstream templates\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): type portable template helpers\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): satisfy lint checks\n\nAssisted-By: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): remove obsolete local templates\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* refactor(plugin-new): isolate portable template renderer\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* test(plugin-new): restore shared task coverage\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): simplify template helper type\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): limit supported templates\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Stan Lewis <gashcrumb@gmail.com>\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): address review thread findings\n\n- remove duplicate entryPoint from snapshot file list and merge backend\n  spread entries (test-integrity thread)\n- validate --plugin-package against npm package name rules (input-validation\n  thread)\n- use path.relative() instead of file.slice() in portable template renderer\n  (edge-case thread)\n- reverse context spread so values.name wins over filename override in hbs\n  rendering (edge-case thread)\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): add --template and --module-id options\n\n- add --template <name> to select an upstream portable template by its\n  canonical name (frontend-plugin, backend-plugin, catalog-processor-module);\n  overrides --type when provided and skips the interactive type prompt\n- constrain accepted template names to supportedTemplateNames (the same set\n  as the --type aliases) so untested upstream templates are not silently\n  accepted\n- add --module-id <id> to override the module identifier for module-type\n  templates; defaults to the plugin name for non-interactive use\n- derive isModuleTemplate from the template role so module-id defaulting\n  works correctly whether the caller uses --type or --template\n- expand e2e tests: add shared buildAndExport helper, add plugin export step\n  to the frontend case, add an independent backend plugin test, and verify\n  dist-dynamic/package.json in both cases\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* test(plugin-new): add catalog-processor-module e2e case\n\nScaffold, install, typecheck, build, and export a catalog-processor-module\nproject. Also verify the exported dist-dynamic/package.json backstage\nmetadata: role=backend-plugin-module, pluginId=catalog, and\npluginPackage=@backstage/plugin-catalog-backend, which are the fields the\nRHDH installer uses to wire the module to its host plugin.\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): patch upstream frontend-plugin template for msw v2\n\nThe @backstage/cli-module-new 0.1.6 frontend-plugin template (Backstage\n1.54.6) generates tests that use the MSW v1 API. MSW v1''s setupServer()\nintercepts Node http/https modules and XHR but does NOT intercept native\nNode.js fetch (globalThis.fetch), which Backstage''s fetchApiRef uses via\n@backstage/frontend-test-utils. The generated TodoPage test therefore hangs\non findByText() on any Node version with native fetch.\n\nThe upstream fix (msw@^2 + http/HttpResponse API) shipped in\n@backstage/cli-module-new 0.1.7 (Backstage 1.55.0). Until RHDH targets\nthat release, three RHDH-owned overlay files patch the generated project:\n\n1. templates/plugin-new/frontend-plugin/src/components/TodoPage/\n   TodoPage.test.tsx.hbs — MSW v2 API (http/HttpResponse instead of\n   rest/res/ctx).\n\n2. templates/plugin-new/frontend-plugin/src/setupTests.ts — imports\n   TextEncoder, TextDecoder, BroadcastChannel, TransformStream,\n   WritableStream, and ReadableStream from Node builtins and assigns them to\n   global, mirroring what FixedJSDOMEnvironment does for Jest 30+.\n\n3. templates/plugin-new/frontend-plugin/package.json.hbs — adds\n   jest.testEnvironmentOptions.customExportConditions: [''node'',''node-addons'']\n   so Jest 29 resolves msw/node and @mswjs/interceptors subpath exports via\n   the ''node'' condition rather than the default browser condition.\n\nThe msw@^2 dev dependency override is injected by the RHDH 2.1\nfrontend-plugin role overlay in rhdhProfiles.ts, which runs after template\nrendering via adaptStandaloneProject.\n\nThe renderer gains an optional overlayDir parameter. When present, each\nupstream template file is checked against the overlay tree before rendering;\nfiles found in the overlay replace the upstream version. The RHDH_TEMPLATE_\nOVERLAYS_ROOT constant in command.ts is resolved three directories above this\nfile, which is the package root in both the TypeScript source tree and the\ncompiled dist/ output.\n\nEach overlay file contains a Handlebars comment (stripped at render time)\nexplaining which upstream version it patches and when it should be removed.\n\nIncludes two new renderer tests: overlay file wins when present; upstream\nfile used when overlay directory is absent.\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* docs(plugin-new): expand changelog, AGENTS.md, prompt, and e2e coverage\n\n- expand Unreleased changelog entry: separate Changed / Added / Fixed\n  sections covering upstream template reuse, --template, --module-id,\n  --plugin-package, and the MSW v2 overlay fix\n- add plugin new and overlay mechanism section to AGENTS.md: documents\n  supportedTemplateNames gate, the overlay directory convention, and\n  the audit step required when upgrading the cli-module-new version\n- update interactive type prompt to show both --type aliases and upstream\n  template names so callers know either form is accepted\n- add yarn test step to the e2e buildAndExport helper; all three generated\n  project types now pass their own test suite before being exported\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* fix(plugin-new): address review thread findings\n\n- rename module-level constant rhdhReadmeSection -> RHDH_README_SECTION\n  to match SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE used by adjacent constants\n- add JSDoc comment to pluginPackage in CreatePluginOptions, consistent\n  with the template and moduleId fields above it\n- validate --module-id with assertPluginName before template rendering,\n  consistent with the validation applied to name and pluginPackage;\n  add a test case for the invalid module-id path\n- add CHANGELOG Changed entry documenting that default generated package\n  names no longer carry a type suffix (previously -backend, etc.) and\n  noting --plugin-package as the opt-out\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED\n\n* feat(plugin-new): address PatAKnight review feedback\n\n- generate .gitignore in adaptStandaloneProject covering dist, dist-types,\n  dist-dynamic, coverage, node_modules, *.local.yaml, and Yarn Berry\n  .yarn/ paths (upstream templates do not include one)\n\n- expand resolveTemplateName to handle two additional cases:\n  - conflict detection: if both --type and --template are supplied and\n    disagree after aliasing, throw an error naming both values\n  - upstream names via type: accept a full upstream template name\n    (e.g. ''frontend-plugin'') passed as --type, which is what the\n    interactive prompt stores when the user types the upstream name\n\n- add README overlays for all three supported template types, replacing\n  upstream README content that references a Backstage monorepo (installing\n  into packages/backend/src/index.ts, running yarn start from the root\n  directory) with RHDH standalone-project guidance focused on yarn start\n  for local iteration and rhdh-cli plugin export for packaging\n\n- add unit tests for the new resolveTemplateName paths: upstream name\n  accepted as --type, conflicting type+template rejected, agreeing\n  type+template accepted\n- add .gitignore content assertions to the parametrised creates-a-plugin\n  test\n- update all three README snapshots\n\nAssisted-by: claude-sonnet-4-6@default\n\nrh-pre-commit.version: 2.4.0\nrh-pre-commit.check-secrets: ENABLED","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrAqCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeFQQAHe3sq1xX8GygOoG8hjtwQw+\nz66SyflLSyWVAEUgOv3CRF8z3Zg8yh+q0aZ50OK9yZ7bQow7Nzaa7HE4jrguZire\nqHMyWgmxYBUv+e9PKOsven4irbjzFJLR1bhjP39zuiveBPoUloQIF7w4/eLN9j/A\nweKQMl/hc/2P8ErLKZDv886kg+RzrTIl4UcA8cAx//zd7didkyeYcSAKlStU4916\ncCgq0UOQFqm5d/7cQFjzNKmqguvepER+YPLqL0FLGzGsyFMZj88v2Ny2c+sqwmwL\nTKaiiKmHBmHHM0S4Z+5TNy3oevqNSGcMeHkMzz1eRj+eRh1fi7MSIlEyZY2BDtTi\nSEhAEZh2dFbjc9CsrgCjvflNndolbESWx1eRGBTUXMYBfX75OUS5hL5JG1eKiKC1\nge2Lbcoooy+YHjUKCMERZGFsQTTwRCcKOYsGOBmpJ5v7frhIR8jHdd4FDVfw8PNQ\nXA81u0Xxx/07hfN83P9T66eAOM1tHbVU4SbHfuAHWo+yBMvEqwt4n+KBbSiFXG19\n377qJDeGp70PT7VW5W6WSigmT+3miSuDOjMD7KhH1dokIJs+Aog9lFpEcIv59bnM\naZ+uPcL6NeoMFFVN5BsR3Rebo/ISwZErWiCDLTVEFywwiF244FvlWE9nxOWrepIw\nEnu6yc68Bzsr0+HK16mS\n=E6Q3\n-----END PG