","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commits/63ca3e1d78dc484ee8e5ae3093c8ab24202a1480"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115827695?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hopehadfield","id":115827695,"login":"hopehadfield","node_id":"U_kgDOBudj7w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hopehadfield","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commits/eb12137146661e4d1c06d70a195bcb2f12933230/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:46:35Z","email":"hhadfiel@redhat.com","name":"Hope Hadfield"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:46:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: remove scalprum frontend support (#182)\n\n* feat: remove scalprum frontend support\n\nMake frontend plugin export use Backstage standard module federation exclusively and remove the legacy Scalprum bundler, commands, options, and dependencies. Clean legacy artifacts from packaged output, preserve NFS feature metadata when available, and update end-to-end expectations for NFS remotes.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* feat!: release scalprum removal as 3.0.0\n\nDocument the breaking frontend export migration to standard Backstage module federation and NFS metadata. Remove legacy Scalprum options and output references from the supported workflow, and publish the cutover as a major CLI release.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* fix: guard legacy frontend file matching\n\nOnly remove files entries that target dist-scalprum or one of its glob variants, avoiding false positives for unrelated package paths.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* style: group frontend plugin imports\n\nKeep the recursive-readdir third-party import with the other package imports and separate it from the Node.js path import.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* test: remove legacy artifact assertions\n\nKeep the e2e coverage focused on the standard module federation output and feature metadata rather than asserting the absence of removed implementation details.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* refactor: simplify legacy asset matching\n\nUse the minimal dist-scalprum substring check for the small set of supported frontend packages, as suggested in review.\n\n* fix: reject legacy scalprum plugin content\n\nFail frontend exports when plugin metadata, files entries, or output directories still reference Scalprum instead of silently filtering or cleaning them.\n\n* chore: set release version to 2.1.0\n\nKeep the documented Scalprum removal migration on the 2.1 release line as requested.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* fix: warn on legacy scalprum content\n\nKeep legacy Scalprum metadata and files as a warning when exporting through the standard NFS path. The CLI no longer has a Scalprum fallback, so normal NFS export failures still fail naturally. Centralize the legacy inspection and document the migration behavior.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* docs: use standard changelog sections\n\nFold the 2.1.0 migration guidance into the Changed section to keep the changelog compatible with Keep a Changelog.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna","tree":{"sha":"62d7ad2162f155da9fad9d071bfb0c44c1af7bdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/trees/62d7ad2162f155da9fad9d071bfb0c44c1af7bdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/commits/eb12137146661e4d1c06d70a195bcb2f12933230","verification":{"payload":"tree 62d7ad2162f155da9fad9d071bfb0c44c1af7bdc\nparent 1e8aafeb1c4976ca0b862a2b4754b059caf61aee\nauthor Hope Hadfield <hhadfiel@redhat.com> 1789573595 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789573595 -0400\n\nfeat: remove scalprum frontend support (#182)\n\n* feat: remove scalprum frontend support\n\nMake frontend plugin export use Backstage standard module federation exclusively and remove the legacy Scalprum bundler, commands, options, and dependencies. Clean legacy artifacts from packaged output, preserve NFS feature metadata when available, and update end-to-end expectations for NFS remotes.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* feat!: release scalprum removal as 3.0.0\n\nDocument the breaking frontend export migration to standard Backstage module federation and NFS metadata. Remove legacy Scalprum options and output references from the supported workflow, and publish the cutover as a major CLI release.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* fix: guard legacy frontend file matching\n\nOnly remove files entries that target dist-scalprum or one of its glob variants, avoiding false positives for unrelated package paths.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* style: group frontend plugin imports\n\nKeep the recursive-readdir third-party import with the other package imports and separate it from the Node.js path import.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* test: remove legacy artifact assertions\n\nKeep the e2e coverage focused on the standard module federation output and feature metadata rather than asserting the absence of removed implementation details.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* refactor: simplify legacy asset matching\n\nUse the minimal dist-scalprum substring check for the small set of supported frontend packages, as suggested in review.\n\n* fix: reject legacy scalprum plugin content\n\nFail frontend exports when plugin metadata, files entries, or output directories still reference Scalprum instead of silently filtering or cleaning them.\n\n* chore: set release version to 2.1.0\n\nKeep the documented Scalprum removal migration on the 2.1 release line as requested.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* fix: warn on legacy scalprum content\n\nKeep legacy Scalprum metadata and files as a warning when exporting through the standard NFS path. The CLI no longer has a Scalprum fallback, so normal NFS export failures still fail naturally. Centralize the legacy inspection and document the migration behavior.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna\n\n* docs: use standard changelog sections\n\nFold the 2.1.0 migration guidance into the Changed section to keep the changelog compatible with Keep a Changelog.\n\nAssisted-by: gpt-5.6-luna","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrnbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVygQAC0FB1GQgVDZlPDSTNL46a0l\nNItdkcHTqpB2vcfmlEObaD7/cE24xWwuWoXxmWHOQSSqlohNQ3Y0vr3FaZOuKPso\noVcksNKkpvlxJpQDqAiIvj72w5vxJXkV4WcigVS5hxZCKesSn4h/h3vAXYyT38ZT\nReVfTXX70CL01MUHsFQ4YGpLDSqVeBDP7nBcun+IqkH7M4fG2xx1CKhMglT9mcdy\nNw+v4ADh5DCqJh/tuSJsuWKVubB3sjwb0xIPy16ODfH3yX/LjZKvRJroGXtOOPPl\nBWlO0ozmdtRLnaeZ+XLfXKW8T3chTjWGEJmmXPhn6IxR0zhdjC9gJdeXOWRGgkj5\nUucNCc+zokXiJqBDgoPggCwWMkT0bY9NFQ2LSremIiJZo+l7rrPlDoFPJhFrHM4a\nxCeEAWeY2LX+DgV+t5z41PGsRq+VW5lAUz9wcfo2BXcKFNbJwq5M+3Lb9gbgDJpv\nSsgydiPPdADtZ6SxpVNF3riFBoHl+5dk9BCo9BC7HztJz0j3abLamglokmunn3w8\nGIsEKqEgg7UQEWdllQZ1C1hWd2DO6QECDkyfpyJKDiTg8DGCn/qfdQ1xIBBEzZ/A\nN23U3kimZh2YBwj2vZ51svCtxCsCz+ee8hWV4GrJT7ClO+1FxI1msh5WDWWa8ujL\nW/hwmabPELc9owKleeub\n=re1K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T15:46:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","fol