url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commit/84fd1c5c798f6d3bb5ecb249bbbfff1a94105e77","node_id":"C_kwDOO1StmNoAKDg0ZmQxYzVjNzk4ZjZkM2JiNWVjYjI0OWJiYmZmZjFhOTQxMDVlNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commit/7dac1979668716aafb853607ecfc253777515467","sha":"7dac1979668716aafb853607ecfc253777515467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commits/7dac1979668716aafb853607ecfc253777515467"}],"sha":"84fd1c5c798f6d3bb5ecb249bbbfff1a94105e77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commits/84fd1c5c798f6d3bb5ecb249bbbfff1a94105e77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22285490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yangcao77","id":22285490,"login":"yangcao77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjg1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yangcao77","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commits/7dac1979668716aafb853607ecfc253777515467/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:28:42Z","email":"yangcao@redhat.com","name":"Stephanie Cao"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:28:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(RHIDP-14129): add intent-based CLI commands and backstage-cli pass-through (#156)\n\n* add intent based clis to support action execution, other cmd, auth/actions related will use backstage-cli\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* update template\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(RHIDP-14129): fix CI failures for intent-based CLI commands\n\n- Statically import command modules in commands/index.ts instead of\n  using require(), since the backstage-cli bundler only follows static\n  ESM imports/dynamic import() and silently dropped the require()''d\n  files from the packed dist, breaking every command once installed\n  from npm (Cannot find module ''./backstage-passthrough'').\n- Fix TS2352 in intent-errors.ts by adding a safe getStderr() helper\n  instead of casting Error directly to Record<string, unknown>.\n- Restrict the PATH used to resolve backstage-cli via `which` to\n  directories that aren''t group/other-writable, addressing the\n  SonarCloud S4036 PATH-search security hotspot in lib/client.ts.\n- Extract shared runEntityListAction/runRawAction/runSearchAction\n  helpers and a registerPassthroughCommand helper to remove the heavy\n  code duplication SonarCloud flagged across catalog/api/template/\n  search/docs/backstage-passthrough command files.\n- Fix pre-existing lint (no-empty, func-names) and prettier issues so\n  the Checks job can get past the linter/prettier steps.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* refactor(RHIDP-14129): bundle intent-based CLI commands into one directory\n\nMove catalog/api/search/docs/template/backstage-passthrough and their\nsupporting client/format/intent-errors/helpers modules into\nsrc/commands/intent-based-actions/, mirroring the existing\nexport-dynamic-plugin/ and package-dynamic-plugins/ layout, with a\nsingle registerIntentCommands() entry point.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(RHIDP-14129): resolve backstage-cli via PATH scan instead of which\n\nSonarCloud S4036 still flagged spawnSync(''which'', ...) even with a restricted PATH env, since it pattern-matches on shelling out to a path-search utility rather than analyzing the PATH value. Replace it with a direct filesystem walk over PATH entries (skipping group/other-writable directories) and an accessSync executability check, avoiding the flagged pattern entirely.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* input and output UX enhancement\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address fullsend review comments, added the new clis in readme\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* update doc\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* template value flag should be optional\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* add cli mapping table\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* fix ci failure\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* fix human readable output cannot parse too large json object\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* update CLI reference name\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address more docs command\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Tomas Kral <tkral@redhat.com>","tree":{"sha":"81f75cd8917b2f09076d49731d85ac1efc6e0aa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/trees/81f75cd8917b2f09076d49731d85ac1efc6e0aa8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/commits/7dac1979668716aafb853607ecfc253777515467","verification":{"payload":"tree 81f75cd8917b2f09076d49731d85ac1efc6e0aa8\nparent 74cc7b681f7f3e33e71eec2571c2955c033e1d71\nauthor Stephanie Cao <yangcao@redhat.com> 1789482522 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789482522 +0200\n\nfeat(RHIDP-14129): add intent-based CLI commands and backstage-cli pass-through (#156)\n\n* add intent based clis to support action execution, other cmd, auth/actions related will use backstage-cli\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* update template\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(RHIDP-14129): fix CI failures for intent-based CLI commands\n\n- Statically import command modules in commands/index.ts instead of\n  using require(), since the backstage-cli bundler only follows static\n  ESM imports/dynamic import() and silently dropped the require()''d\n  files from the packed dist, breaking every command once installed\n  from npm (Cannot find module ''./backstage-passthrough'').\n- Fix TS2352 in intent-errors.ts by adding a safe getStderr() helper\n  instead of casting Error directly to Record<string, unknown>.\n- Restrict the PATH used to resolve backstage-cli via `which` to\n  directories that aren''t group/other-writable, addressing the\n  SonarCloud S4036 PATH-search security hotspot in lib/client.ts.\n- Extract shared runEntityListAction/runRawAction/runSearchAction\n  helpers and a registerPassthroughCommand helper to remove the heavy\n  code duplication SonarCloud flagged across catalog/api/template/\n  search/docs/backstage-passthrough command files.\n- Fix pre-existing lint (no-empty, func-names) and prettier issues so\n  the Checks job can get past the linter/prettier steps.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* refactor(RHIDP-14129): bundle intent-based CLI commands into one directory\n\nMove catalog/api/search/docs/template/backstage-passthrough and their\nsupporting client/format/intent-errors/helpers modules into\nsrc/commands/intent-based-actions/, mirroring the existing\nexport-dynamic-plugin/ and package-dynamic-plugins/ layout, with a\nsingle registerIntentCommands() entry point.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(RHIDP-14129): resolve backstage-cli via PATH scan instead of which\n\nSonarCloud S4036 still flagged spawnSync(''which'', ...) even with a restricted PATH env, since it pattern-matches on shelling out to a path-search utility rather than analyzing the PATH value. Replace it with a direct filesystem walk over PATH entries (skipping group/other-writable directories) and an accessSync executability check, avoiding the flagged pattern entirely.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* input and output UX enhancement\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address fullsend review comments, added the new clis in readme\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* update doc\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* template value flag should be optional\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* add cli mapping table\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* fix ci failure\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address review comments\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* fix human readable output cannot parse too large json object\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* update CLI reference name\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n* address more docs command\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephanie <yangcao@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Tomas Kral <tkral@redhat.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqVYaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaocQAC+iEqr5LqzaetMa8pPYWEuP\nhbdIVxMzSoc3ZMy4