ub.com/users/kadel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/commits/39c8ff638e0e8b01d04aaa26edf7df56f08b3e31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:47:28Z","email":"tkral@redhat.com","name":"Tomas Kral"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:47:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): align npm dist-tags with GA releases (#143)\n\n* fix(ci): align npm dist-tags with GA releases\n\nPublishing from main now uses the `next` dist-tag instead of `latest`.\nThe `latest` tag is reserved for the auto-detected highest semver\nrelease branch (e.g., release-1.10), matching the convention used\nfor catalog images and quay tags. Older release branches continue\nto use their branch name as the dist-tag.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\n* docs: document npm dist-tag strategy and workflow usage\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\n* fix(ci): add branch dist-tag for latest GA and make latest explicit\n\nAddress PR review feedback: explicitly pass --tag latest for the\nhighest GA branch and add a separate npm dist-tag for the branch name\nso the package is discoverable via both tags.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\n* fix: format README table to pass prettier check\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code","tree":{"sha":"a982cca338fd168d9e0c08ecf67cc7626478ac84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/trees/a982cca338fd168d9e0c08ecf67cc7626478ac84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh-cli/git/commits/39c8ff638e0e8b01d04aaa26edf7df56f08b3e31","verification":{"payload":"tree a982cca338fd168d9e0c08ecf67cc7626478ac84\nparent 27129b4357b911446ddcb6fbfe84ce3391236721\nauthor Tomas Kral <tkral@redhat.com> 1786020448 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786020448 -0300\n\nfix(ci): align npm dist-tags with GA releases (#143)\n\n* fix(ci): align npm dist-tags with GA releases\n\nPublishing from main now uses the `next` dist-tag instead of `latest`.\nThe `latest` tag is reserved for the auto-detected highest semver\nrelease branch (e.g., release-1.10), matching the convention used\nfor catalog images and quay tags. Older release branches continue\nto use their branch name as the dist-tag.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\n* docs: document npm dist-tag strategy and workflow usage\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\n* fix(ci): add branch dist-tag for latest GA and make latest explicit\n\nAddress PR review feedback: explicitly pass --tag latest for the\nhighest GA branch and add a separate npm dist-tag for the branch name\nso the package is discoverable via both tags.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\n* fix: format README table to pass prettier check\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdIJgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ00QAJkYVF1l6E202Ibnx8UKum1i\nn9hZksGZgy3l2AvZJZM3aq++IA8mIUGRsb8IF0Bx5CJkOTlkZQBJMMIE56W5fAXY\n6mzdZo4qiWH3K/aqvkU2P4t/tM++Rp8Nkiz0PfXgF4tt9ft46UfHvQ/KnPpnVXuN\n9PW+Srd52m71TB2iKf9gaJIv2WyWlObjBt0FL7J/0+NfW7kqAgti19Xa860l+H9R\naPfxFIZjrbzu15XZSVlqucHuSlkcQ1xY4j8KZXG8vM3tkr/fJj8ka6rBfm41bHex\nyOi2XLUc4lR+r3QbnA6WS1+ptXVvNdBzHCbp7/fhoCRHg7vXNT6MCkNcIt/pZrzb\n+iwPUx/innmzee+d/UpwchPbWRkKKJn32Fog0x1qjgFYrF866UL9ICmaD4h0etJU\nmL4B3U5EaadJKankMAhYlL05Sm122L0kuA7krcyD2fHHmMm2wf7EIo4/8ixtHeBm\nTmGhLUVlkwHOuoNAuvhUSLpuDoFvsTLKyocyoLWDZ8Nj316eefKZ2c1MHCd49ft4\nEvi2JVbfY7y12sAaq0IvuFJdwDmBi3H83/G1S69WaFw0eLU1ihup6zT5IsO7bQjz\n5fxfN4FXiIX5VpMUJRwx0DeUzWDedCZZGDc97E9JnKT0z9q3AX7zYn+wRydT+G64\ndYHFgZ3s7Egq0ubJz6tb\n=OwXJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T12:48:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/follow